<tr><td>CRPT011780</td><td>F002411</td><td>CMC Steel Fabricators</td><td>Title V</td><td>Metal Fabrication</td><td>CMP000856</td><td>CMC Steel Fabricators Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Order of Abatement by Consent - SA006812 - CMC Monthly Update Report</td><td>02/13/2026</td><td>02/17/2026</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>OAC monthly update report for SA006812 (monthly update 20). 

CRPT011780: CMC is currently unable to operate Mesa Mill No. 2 at or near its maximum production rate on a sustained basis and therefore is unable to achieve continuous compliance with the 30-day rolling average limits for SO2, CO, and NOx. The SO2 has been elevated, both CO and NOx have been at or below the 30-day rolling average limits since June 2025. 

Current report received on February 13, 2026, indicates that the 30-day rolling averages for January 2026 are 0.29 lb/ton for NOx, 0.37 lb/ton for SO2, and 2.33 lb/ton for CO.

SO2 is above the emission limit and NOx and CO are below emission limits in PC Table 18.c.2.

Emission limits in PC 18.c.2 for Mesa Mill No.2 are: 0.30 lb/ton of steel for NOx, 0.30 lb/ton of steel for SO2, and 4.00 lb/ton of steel for CO.

Note: The commissioning issues presented in the table now have extended due dates of March 2026, June 2026, and the end of December 2026.</td></tr>
