<tr><td>CRPT011627</td><td>F006603</td><td>Ball Metal Beverage Container Corporation</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Metal Fabrication</td><td>CMP000443</td><td>Ball Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Second half 2025 semi-annual NSPS certification July 1, 2025 - December 31, 2025</td><td>01/28/2026</td><td>01/28/2026</td><td>Yes</td><td>CRPT011586</td><td>This compliance report was submitted due to missing data from the previous compliance report CRPT011586. No compliance issues were documented from the previous compliance report. 

Review of Ball Metal Beverage Container Corporation's required semiannual notification for the time period of July 1, 2025 - December 31, 2025. The report was submitted to the department within the required deadline of January 30, 2026. The report was submitted in accordance with Permit Condition 15.a. and 15.b.

Per Permit Condition 15.a., the facility submitted the following: 

Where compliance with Permit Condition 6 is achieved through the use of thermal incineration, each 3-hour period when cans are processed, during which the average temperature of the device was more than 28 degrees C below the average temperature of the device during the most recent performance test at which destruction efficiency was determined under Permit Condition 12.

The following dates provided had the average temperature of the device more than 28 degrees C below the average temperature of the device during the most recent performance test at which destruction efficiency was determined:

RTO1 November 23-26, 2025: 20 hours for Annual Planned Maintenance Shutdown
RTO2 July 28-31, 2025: 78 hours for RTO 2 media replacement
RTO2 September 24, 2025: 9 hours for RTO 2 engineering test
RTO2 November 24-26, 2025: 54 hours for Annual Planned Maintenance Shutdown 

Per Permit Condition 15.b., the facility submitted the following: 

In accordance with the reporting requitements list under 40 CFR 60.495(b), the facility is reporting no instances in which the volume weighted average of the total mass of VOC's emitted was greater than the applicable limits specified under 40 CFR 60.492.

Additionally, the facility reported that no new coatings were used during the 6 month certification period.

No compliance issues were noted during the review of the updated compliance report.</td></tr>
