<tr><td>CRPT011652</td><td>F001522</td><td>Mesquite Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP002166</td><td>Mesquite Power LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>In accordance with Title V Permit No. P0010573, the Salt River Project (SRP) is submitting the enclosed Part 60 Excess Emissions and Monitoring Systems Performance Report for Mesquite Generating Station to satisfy the requirements of Title 40 Code of Federal Regulations (CFR) Sections 60.7(c) and (d) as specified by the permit.   This Part 60 Report is for the reporting period from July 1, 2025 through December 31, 2025. If you have any questions or require additional information, please contact D’Armond Chee at (602) 236-0039.</td><td>01/27/2026</td><td>01/30/2026</td><td>Yes</td><td>CRPT011579</td><td>An updated compliance report was submitted in reference to an update from the previous compliance report (CRPT011579). 

The facility is in compliance with the previous compliance report and was documented in inspection INSP217049.

This revised compliance report references the additional downtime events for Units 1, 2, 5, and 6 on December 8, 2025. 

The facility reported there were no NOx and CO emissions excursions or exceedances for CCS Unit 1, 2, 5, and 6 during the reporting period of July 1, 2025 to December 31, 2025. Therefore, the total duration of excess emissions for the reporting period was reported to be less than 1 percent of the total operating time for CCS Units 1, 2, 5 and 6.

The total duration of CEMS downtime for the reporting period was reported to be less than 5 percent of the total operating time for CCS Units 1, 2, 5 and 6.

The highest reported duration of CEMS downtime across all units was for Unit #1, at 1.33% of total operating time.

The facility has complied with the reporting requirements of 40 CFR § 60.7(c) and (d) by only submitting the summary report form for the reporting period.

No compliance issues were noted during the review of the revised compliance report.</td></tr>
