<tr><td>CRPT011593</td><td>F001331</td><td>Quikjet - Monroe I & II Terminals</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Petroleum Products Bulk Storage/Handling</td><td>CMP015463</td><td>Quikjet LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Semi-Annual Compliance Report (NESHAP Subpart BBBBBB & NSPS Subpart Kc) for July 1, 2025 through December 31, 2025</td><td>01/26/2026</td><td>01/30/2026</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semiannual Compliance Report for reporting period July 1, 2025, through December 31, 2025. Compliance report received in the required timeframe as indicated in Permit Condition 18.a.ii.

All elements required by Permit Condition 18.b. was documented and reported.

A table summarizing storage tank compliance status is provided in the compliance report. Gasoline storage tanks subject to 40 CFR 60 Subpart Kc are in compliance with 40 CFR 63 Subpart BBBBBB per 40 CFR 63.11087(f) and 40 CFR 60.110c(h).

Records of tank seal inspection notifications submitted to the MCAQD during the compliance reporting period are provided in the compliance report. The inspection reports submitted to the facility were documented as in compliance.

No loading or reloading of gasoline cargo tanks occurred without the prior receipt of vapor tightness documentation during the compliance reporting period.

There were no equipment leaks that failed to receive a repair attempt within five days of detection or that were not completely repaired within fifteen days after detection for the compliance reporting period.

There were no exceedances or failures to maintain the established monitored operating parameter for the vapor recovery unit continuous emissions monitoring system during the compliance period. The facility is not required to install or operate pressure and/or temperature continuous monitoring systems on the vapor collection system and vapor combustion unit, respectively, until May 2027 per Permit Conditions 6.d. and 8.f.  The facility is currently complying with the alternate monitoring requirements specified in Permit Conditions 6.f and 8.e.ii.

There were no excess emission events that occurred during the reporting period. 

Attachment C includes required CEMS quarterly calibration tests.

No compliance issues noted during the review of the compliance report.</td></tr>
