<tr><td>CRPT011568</td><td>F000308</td><td>City Of Goodyear Well 12</td><td>Minor</td><td>Generator, Stationary (ATO)</td><td>CMP000813</td><td>City of Goodyear</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Unit #2016164425 off site for repairs</td><td>01/20/2026</td><td>01/21/2026</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>ENG003 – Stamford HCI534E1, Serial No. 2016164425
The facility’s engine, which was believed to be EPA-certified at the time of installation, was removed from the facility on December 15, 2025, and returned to the manufacturer in Texas after it was determined that the engine may not, in fact, be EPA-certified. The facility is currently using a mobile non-road engine on an interim basis. The resolution method and timeline remain uncertain.

The facility should be aware of the following:
1. If the non-road engine remains stationary for 12 months or longer, it will no longer be considered a mobile engine and will instead be classified as a stationary engine.
2. If the facility installs or reinstalls an emergency engine other than ENG003 – Stamford HCI534E1, Serial No. 2016164425, MCAQD must be notified and the facility’s equipment list must be updated accordingly.

If the facility has any further questions, please reach out to our Business Assistance Team at 602-506-5102.</td></tr>
