<tr><td>CRPT011384</td><td>F001433</td><td>City Of Surprise Spa 2 Reg Water Rec</td><td>Minor</td><td>Wastewater Treatment Plants and Lift Stations</td><td>CMP000832</td><td>City of Surprise</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Notification</td><td>90 day H2S Fenceline Testing</td><td>12/18/2025</td><td>12/19/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>H2S fence line testing refer to Inspection report INSP215611 for further details.

Submitted due to permit condition 4a. was not submitted at the time of the permit issuance (August 4, 2023). H2S Testing was conducted on December 15, 2025, and received on December 18, 2025. 
a. The Permittee shall perform a compliance demonstration by conducting a test to monitor H2S levels within 90 days of any of the following events: 
i. Being issued a Permit under this General Permit,
ii. At the time of renewal of this General Permit,
iii. The start-up of new ECS equipment,
iv. The reception of a written request from the Control Officer.

b. The compliance demonstration shall be performed using a handheld air analyzer with a suitable range (3.0 ppb – 10.0 ppm H2S). 
-Report indicates that a Jerome 631X Hydrogen Sulfide Analyzer was used. 

c. The compliance demonstration shall be performed at a location representing the nearest point beyond the fence, borderline, boundary or property line that exists separating the premises on which the source of H2S is located, from other premises, parcels or properties.
- Reports indicates that several spots along the fence line was used as sampling locations. 

d. Newly Permitted Sources or Sources with Newly Permitted ECS: The Permittee shall perform an
additional compliance demonstration within six (6) months of completing the initial demonstration. If the
average H2S concentration is less than 0.03 ppmv in any of the first two demonstrations, the monitoring
shall be subsequently conducted every five years, with each permit renewal.

e. The Permittee shall submit a report within 30 days of completion of each demonstration to the Control
Officer, Attn: Compliance Division Manager that details the results of each compliance demonstration.</td></tr>
