<tr><td>CRPT011377</td><td>F000658</td><td>Holsum Bakery</td><td>Minor</td><td>Bakery</td><td>CMP004372</td><td>Holsum Bakery of Tolleson LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Bread Oxidizer was not running during production on 12/17/25 from 6:50am -9:35am. Roughly 2 hours and 45 minutes. 

Product in oven during this time:

Product: 24 oz Wheat Sandwich 
Total Sacks: 234 Sacks 

The Tolleson Bakery Engineering team was first notified of the downtime by the Alarm notification installed on the Bread Oxidizer electrical panel.  Engineering began investigating right away and contacted IES third party electrical contractors to assist with trouble shooting.   The team identified that the thermocouple failed on the catalyst outlet side.  Engineering/IES found a spare thermocouple and rewired the unit. Oxidizer system is functioning as properly as of now.</td><td>12/17/2025</td><td>12/26/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This Compliance Report was submitted due to equipment failure. The bread oven oxidizer failed, and the following permit conditions were met regarding this event:
 
Permit Condition 1.a: 12-month rolling totals of VOCs remained below the 45,100 lbs/yr, with a value of 13,283.9808 lbs/yr (see 12 Month Rolling Totals attachment).
 
Permit Condition 15: The malfunction was documented in a manner compliant to Rules 130 and 140.</td></tr>
