<tr><td>CRPT011185</td><td>F002813</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP000654</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>24 Hour notice of malfunction that occurred 11/11/2025 at 0053. ID Fan had a HIHI vibration alarm that shut down fan, causing Thermal Oxidizer flame to go out and bypass stacks to open.</td><td>11/11/2025</td><td>12/01/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Source submitted 24 hour malfunction notification, advising that on 11/11/25 from 0053 to 0120 hours a malfunction occurred involving the thermal oxidizer, fan, and bypass stack #1 and # 2. The ID fan shut down and caused the Thermal Oxidizer burner to go out and bypass the stacks to open. The thermal oxidizer heated back up and the bypass stacks were closed back at 0120. 

The malfunction notification has been accepted.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT011184</td><td>F002411</td><td>CMC Steel Fabricators</td><td>Title V</td><td>Metal Fabrication</td><td>CMP000856</td><td>CMC Steel Fabricators Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>1. Monthly OAC Report Update
2. OAC Notification of Anticipated Delay</td><td>11/11/2025</td><td>11/12/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Notification of Anticipated Delay Letter and OAC monthly update report for SA006812 (monthly update 17). 

CRPT011184: CMC is currently unable to operate Mesa Mill No. 2 at or near its maximum production rate on a sustained basis and therefore is unable to achieve continuous compliance with the 30-day rolling average limits for SO2, CO, and NOx. 

Current report received on November 11, 2025, indicates that the 30-day rolling averages for October 2025 are 0.25 lb/ton for NOx, 0.23 lb/ton for SO2, and 2.14 lb/ton for CO.

NOx, SO2 and CO are below emission limits in PC Table 18.c.2.

Emission limits in PC 18.c.2 for Mesa Mill No.2 are: 0.30 lb/ton of steel for NOx, 0.30 lb/ton of steel for SO2, and 4.00 lb/ton of steel for CO.

Note: The commissioning issues presented in the table now have extended due dates of February 2026, March 2026, and June 2026.</td></tr>
