<tr><td>CRPT011177</td><td>F002813</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP000654</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Notification</td><td>24 Hour notice of malfunction that occurred 11/08/2025 at 2026. Thermal Oxidizer fell below minimum temperature, which caused bypass stacks to open.</td><td>11/09/2025</td><td>11/10/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Source submitted 24 hour malfunction notification, advising that on 11/08/25 from 2026 to 2043 hours a malfunction occurred involving the thermal oxidizer. Kiln #1 had a plug between the discharge of kiln and the inlet of cooler. The feed was shut off from kiln #1 at 1722 hours. During the clearing of the plug, ambient air entered the thermal oxidizer. This in turn lowered the thermal oxidizer temperature below the allowable limit and caused the bypass stacks to open. The thermal oxidizer was heated back up and the feed shut off via interlock.

The malfunction notification has been accepted.

Permit expiration: 10/31/26
Annual administrative fees: 09/15/25
