<tr><td>CRPT011172</td><td>F001529</td><td>Honeywell International - Phoenix Engines</td><td>Title V</td><td>Aerospace Component Manufacturing</td><td>CMP001662</td><td>Honeywell International Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>7-Day Notice</td><td>Temporary use of portable cooling towers</td><td>11/07/2025</td><td>11/12/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Honeywell Engines facility submitted this request to temporarily replace cooling towers CT-2 & CT-3 with two (2) trailer-mounted cooling towers.

Multiple test cells utilizes a cooling tower loop to support the cooling of the test cell to remove heat from the engine load system during operation. CT-2 & CT-3 each have a maximum water flow rate of 2,775 gallons per minute (gpm) and the trailer-mounted cooling towers each have a maximum flow rate of 1,800 gpm. The facility is planning to use one cooling tower at a time and the additional pump will be locked out to restrict usage.

The facility provided this notification in accordance with Section 403.1 of Rule 210. All of the following standards in Section 403.1 applied to the source.

No compliance issues were noted during the review of the notification. 

AREA OF CONCERN:
On November 7, 2025, communication was made to Senior HSE Supervisor, Diana Furman, regarding questions about the 7-day notification. During the phone call Ms. Furman stated that work for the cooling towers was planned to start on November 8, 2025. 

In the past the cooling towers were considered an insignificant activity and required notifications for any equipment changes were not required to be submitted to MCAQD. 

The cooling towers are no longer considered insignificant at the facility and are applicable to MCAQD rules and regulations. A 7-day notification was not submitted at least seven days prior as required by Rule 210. I notified Ms. Furman that the facility needs to submit the required notification and I will document it as an area of concern since this is the first 7-day notification that has been required for the cooling towers. I notified Ms. Furman that in the future when any equipment changes are required, the facility needs to be submitted at a minimum of seven working days in advance of the equipment change.</td></tr>
