<tr><td>CRPT011097</td><td>F001209</td><td>SR 85 Landfill</td><td>Title V</td><td>Landfills</td><td>CMP000821</td><td>City of Phoenix</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>SR85 Title V Semi-Annual Report for 04.04.25 to 10.03.25 reporting period and the Annual Certification for October 4, 2024 through October 3, 2025.</td><td>10/27/2025</td><td>11/26/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semi-Annual Report Compliance Report covering the period of April 4, 2025 through October 3, 2025 & Title V Certification Report covering the period of October 4, 2024 through October 3, 2025 submitted in accordance with Permit V03-002, Permit Conditions 21.B. and 21.C.
Facility submitted the compliance report prior to the November 3, 2025 deadline. All required information was provided within the compliance report.

SEMIANNUAL COMPLIANCE REPORT
21.B.I.: Monthly opacity reports have been regularly submitted throughout this reporting period. Weekly visible emission observations of the flare have been taken as required by Permit Condition 20.F.I. 
21.B.II.: No odor complaints were reported for this period.
21.B.III.: Gasoline throughput limit has not been exceeded. Most recent twelve month rolling throughput was 2,185 gallons of gasoline.
21.B.IV.: H2S testing was not required or conducted during this time period.
21.B.V.: 12-Month Rolling total emissions were provided
PM10/PM2.5: 1.26 tons
NMOC: 0 tons
VOC: 0.16 tons (Permit Limit: 76.00 tons)
Any Single HAP: 0.06 tons
Total HAPs: 0.17 tons
CO: 11.26 tons
NOx: 4.51 tons (Permit Limit: 25.00 tons)
SOx: 0.54 tons
HCl: 0.30 tons (Permit Limit: 9.98 tons)
21.B.VI.: There were no periods in which the flare operated below the average combustion temperatures established during the most recent performance testing. There were no instances of exceedances of well operational parameters and no deviations from the operational parameters for the flare.
21.B.VII.: No bypass lines are incorporated into the design.
21.B.VIII.: Flame failures and flare maintenance occurred during the reporting period. 
 21.B.IX.: Gas collection system did not exceed five days of no operation.
21.B.X.: The surface was traversed and did not have any exceedances or deviations of 500 ppm of methane.
21.B.XI.: No expansions have been made to the gas collection system.
21.B.XII.: Plant is operated in accordance with SSM plan.
Architectural Coatings: No architectural coating were used during this period.
Landfill Liquids: 39,300 gallons of condensate were recirculated back to the landfill. 

ANNUAL CERTIFICATION REPORT
The annual compliance certification contained the following information:
- The identification of the Permittee and the permit number.
- The identification of each term or condition of the permit that is the basis of the certification;
- The compliance status;
- Whether compliance was continuous or intermittent;
- The method(s) used for determining the compliance status of the source, currently and over the reporting period;
- A signed statement by a responsible official certifying the truth, accuracy, and completeness of the information provided in the report.

Intermittent compliance status selected for the Permit Condition 19.C. is marked due to 2/12/10 direction on recordkeeping from MCAQD until the issuance of the Title V renewal permit when the requirements of 40 CFR 60 Subpart WWW are removed as they no longer are applicable to the facility.

Intermittent compliance status selected for the Permit Condition 21.C. for the Annual Compliance Certification prepared and submitted in accordance with this permit requirement. The Annual Compliance Certification for the reporting period of October 4, 2024 through April 3, 2025 was submitted on April 29, 2025.

No compliance issues were noted during the review of the compliance report.

In the future, per Permit P0007450 issued October 22, 2025, please submit the semiannual monitoring report covering the reporting periods of October 1 – March 31 and April 1 – September 30, respectively. This report shall be submitted no later than April 30 and October 31. Please submit the annual certification report at least annually as required by Permit Condition 21.b.</td></tr>
