<tr><td>CRPT010883</td><td>F000658</td><td>Holsum Bakery</td><td>Minor</td><td>Bakery</td><td>CMP004372</td><td>Holsum Bakery of Tolleson LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>9/12/25 
Bread Oxidizer 
9/12/25 11:29p - 9/13/25 6:30a  (Roughly  6 hours and minute) 

Holsum Bakery F000658 Oxidizer downtime for the Bread Production Line on 9-12-25. The Bread Oven ran from 9/12/25 11:29p - 9/13/25 6:30a without the oxidizer running.  (Roughly  6 hours and minute).  Engineering Preflight check was completed by an Engineer at midnight, and all systems were functioning normally.   A breaker tripped in the Bread Oxidizer Oven Panel (unknown time).  At 7:35 an Engineer observed the issue and reset the breaker.  All systems function normally after the reset.  After further investigation, the root cause was identified on 9/17.  The Engineering Team and 3rd Party Electrician found two wires burned together in one of the conduits bodies causing a short.  Engineering team repaired the wiring.  This would be the root cause of the breaker randomly tripping and finally when the wires fused together it was a complete short circuit.  On the roof where the Bread Oxidizer is located, the blowers would cause vibrations in the conduit raceway and randomly touch together.   

•	Honey Wheat -42 Sacks approximately, 5418 units
•	Perfectly crafted white  (140 sacks) approximately 16240 units
•	Wonder Italian (10sack) approximately 1201 units
•	Perfectly crafted multi Grain (96 Sacks ) approximately 12960 units
•	Perfectly crafted brioche (91 sacks) approximately 11466 units


Honey wheat – Started at divider 22:25pm at divider, went through oven Approximately 23:23 pm – 3 Doughs (42 Sacks) approximately, 5418 units

Perfectly crafted white  – Started at divider 23:20 pm at divider, went through oven Approximately 00:18 am – 10 doughs (140 sacks) approximately 16240 units

Wonder Italian – Started at divider 01:38 am 9/13, went through oven Approximately 01:35 am – 1 dough (10sack) approximately 1201 units

Perfectly crafted multi Grain – Started at divider 02:00 am 9/13, went through oven approximately 02:28 am – 8 doughs (96 sacks) approximately 12960 units

Perfectly crafted brioche – started at divider 03:50 am 9/13, went through oven approximately 04:45 – 7 doughs (91 sacks) approximately 11466 units

9/17/25  
Bred Oxidizer Failure 
1:15am - 6:50 am.  Roughly 5 Hours and 35 Mins 
Holsum Bakery F000658 Oxidizer downtime for the Bread Production Line on 9-17-25.  The Bread Oven ran from 1:15am - 6:50 am.  without oxidizer running (Roughly 5 Hours and 35 Mins).  
An hourly check form was implemented for the engineering department.  At 1:15am an Engineer identified a failure at the panel again.    Engineering tried to reset the breaker in the panel, but the panel kept failing.  After Further investigation, the root cause was identified on 9/17.  On the roof where the bread oxidizer is located, the Engineering Team and 3rd Party Electrician found two wires burned together in one of the conduits bodies causing a short.  Engineering team repaired the wiring.  This would be the root cause of the breaker randomly tripping and finally when the wires fused together it was a complete short circuit.  On the roof where the Bread Oxidizer is located, the blowers would cause vibrations in the conduit raceway and randomly touch together.

Great Value White - (78 Sacks), Approximately 9750 units
PL Rtop White- (91 Sacks)1 Approximately 11375 units
Wonder Classic- (78 sacks), Approximately 9750 units
Wonder Italian- (10sack) approximately 1201 units

Great Value White – Started at 00:10 at divider, went through oven approximately 01:10am – 6 doughs (78 Sacks), Approximately 9750 units

PL Rtop White – Started at 01:37 at divider, went through oven approximately 02:37 am – 7 doughs (91 Sacks)1 Approximately 11375 units

Wonder Classic – Started at 02:57 at divider, went through oven Approximately 03:57am – 6 doughs (78 sacks), Approximately 9750 units

Wonder Italian – Started at 04:20 at divider, went through oven Approximately 04:20 am – 1 dough (10sack) approximately 1201 units

Perfectly crafted white  – Started at 04:40 pm at divider, w</td><td>09/17/2025</td><td>10/07/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Per permit condition 9:

In the event that essential control system maintenance is required (either as a result of a preventive maintenance schedule or an equipment malfunction), bypass is permitted if it can be demonstrated that bakery VOC emissions from new or existing oven can be reduced by at least 81% over the calendar month in which the maintenance occurs (or use a VOC emission factor value of 5.5 pounds per ton for new ovens while the maintenance occurs) and the monthly emission limit is not exceeded. For the purpose of this demonstration, emissions will be calculated using production data, emission factors derived from Rule 343, and the average control system treatment efficiency obtained during the most recent Performance Test.  

The Permittee shall notify the Control Officer of the bypass operation within 24 hours of the occurrence and provide an estimate of the duration of such operation.  

Bypass activities must be appropriately documented at the facility and these records shall be available for review during facility inspections conducted by Department personnel.  

Bread production oxidizer malfunction occurred on 09/12/25 - 09/13/25 and 09/17/25, notification submitted to the Department on 09/17/25. The malfunction notification and documentation has been accepted.

Permit expiration: 03/31/29
Annual administrative fees: 02/08/25
Performance testing: Conducted 06/24/25, report submitted 08/07/25
Routine inspection: 05/30/24, in compliance</td></tr>
