<tr><td>CRPT010900</td><td>F001332</td><td>Caljet</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Petroleum Products Bulk Storage/Handling</td><td>CMP015461</td><td>Caljet of America LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Notification</td><td>Providing an update to Compliance Reports CRPT010810 and CRPT010863 regarding the seal inspection Tank 3. The inspection is scheduled for September 24, 2025 at 6:00 AM</td><td>09/17/2025</td><td>10/06/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The notification, received on September 17, 2025, indicated that tank 3 was scheduled for an inspection on September 24, 2205. This does not meet the 30-day advance notice requirement outlined in the facility’s permit. Please see INSP213683.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT010896</td><td>F000789</td><td>Microchip Technology - Tempe</td><td>Minor</td><td>Semiconductors and Electronics</td><td>CMP002193</td><td>Microchip Technology Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>On September 17, 2025, from approximately 4:00 AM to 4:45 AM, the Munters VOC Abatement Unit RCTO 20-2 was offline due to “combustion actuator fault".  We are not currently running any manufacturing processes which emit VOC's due to announce plant closure.</td><td>09/17/2025</td><td>09/23/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The facility reports that on September 17, 2025 from 4 a.m. to 4:45 a.m. the RCTO 20-2 went offline for 0.75 hours  due to “combustion actuator fault” following which the unit resumed operation. The facility calculates the potential excess emissions at 3.8 lbs; but notes the facility is not currently running any manufacturing process which emits VOC's on account the facility is is being closed and resold as previously announced.

Per section 6.a.iii of the facility's permit [Permit ID: P0011578], a period of up to 4-hours bypass period may be allowed in order to start up the unit acting as the backup VOC abatement unit, and all excess VOC emissions shall be calculated without consideration to emissions reductions.

Ay 08:12 a.m. I telephoned Terry McNally about the alleged status of manufacturing processes. Mr. McNally explained the public announcement was on stock forums and Channel 3 and 5. No correspondence was submitted to MCAQD about the sale. Mr. McNally also clarified statement, "We currently are not running any manufacturing processes which emit VOC’s." to mean, the facility is currently not running any manufacturing processes. Period.

Mr. McNally added the resale of the facility is almost imminent but the details are not yet possible to announce.

The facility's reporting indicates no violations to their Air Quality Permit.</td></tr>
