<tr><td>CRPT010881</td><td>F002411</td><td>CMC Steel Fabricators</td><td>Title V</td><td>Metal Fabrication</td><td>CMP000856</td><td>CMC Steel Fabricators Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Order of Abatement by Consent SA006812 - CMC Monthly Update 15</td><td>09/12/2025</td><td>09/15/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>OAC monthly update report for SA006812 (monthly update 15). 

CRPT010881: CMC is currently unable to operate Mesa Mill No. 2 at or near its maximum production rate on a sustained basis and therefore is unable to achieve continuous compliance with the 30-day rolling average limits for SO2, CO, and NOx. 

Current report received on September 12, 2025, indicates that the 30-day rolling averages for August 2025 are 0.29 lb/ton for NOx, 0.40 lb/ton for SO2, and 2.11 lb/ton for CO.

NOx is below emission limit, SO2 is above the emission limit, and CO is below the emission limit in PC Table 18.c.2.

Emission limits in PC 18.c.2 for Mesa Mill No.2 are: 0.30 lb/ton of steel for NOx, 0.30 lb/ton of steel for SO2, and 4.00 lb/ton of steel for CO.

Note: The commissioning issues presented in the table have extended due dates of October 2025, November 2025, December 2025, and February 2026.</td></tr>
