<tr><td>CRPT010833</td><td>F000612</td><td>Beardsley Rd Water Reclamation Facility</td><td>Minor</td><td>Institutions - Public/Government</td><td>CMP000819</td><td>City of Peoria</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Compliance demonstration for Permit Condition 3 conducted within 90 days of the permit issuance.</td><td>09/04/2025</td><td>10/22/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Reviewed 31OCT2025
Permit Condition 3a.i. -A compliance demonstration test was conducted to monitor H2S levels within 90 days of the date of the renewal of this general permit (Issued 21FEB2025).  **Compliant

Permit Condition 3b. -The compliance demonstration was performed using a handheld air analyzer with a suitable range (3.0 ppb - 10.0 ppm H2S). **Calibration certification submitted & approved.  **Compliant 

Permit Condition 3c. -The compliance demonstration was performed at a location representing the nearest point beyond the
fence, borderline, boundary or property line that exists separating the premises on which the source of
H2S is located, from other premises, parcels or properties.  **Compliant

Permit Condition 3d. -The Permittee shall perform an additional compliance demonstration within six months of completing
the initial demonstration. If the average H2S concentration is less than 0.03 ppmv in any of the first two
compliance demonstrations, the monitoring shall be subsequently conducted on an annual basis. If the
H2S concentration is less than 0.03 ppmv for two consecutive annual compliance demonstrations,
compliance demonstrations will no longer be required. If results from any annual compliance
demonstration indicate that the H2S concentration is greater than 0.03 ppmv, the Permittee shall return
to the semi-annual compliance demonstration schedule.  **Compliant (Testing conducted monthly)

Permit Condition 3e. -The report was not submitted within 30 days of completion of demonstration to the Control Officer.  **Non-Compliant

See Compliance Report # CRPT 101833 for additional findings.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT010831</td><td>F001257</td><td>Costco Wholesale #436</td><td>Minor</td><td>Gasoline Resale</td><td>CMP000948</td><td>Costco Wholesale Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Testing results for VR testing on 8/22/2025.</td><td>09/03/2025</td><td>09/15/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Inspector Nicholas Gilham reviewed provided Compliance Report, submitted by facility on September 3, 2025, on September 15, 2025.  It was noted facility provided documents included results of Pressure Vent Valve Test  (standard TP-201.1E) and Pressure Decay Test (standard TP-201.3).   Testing occurred on August 22, 2025.   

Facility is advised the requirement of notification is a pre-test notification per Permit Condition 12c.

Permit Condition 12c states: "Notice of Testing: The Permittee shall notify the Control Officer in writing at least two weeks in advance of the actual date and time of the test required by Permit Condition 11 so that the Control Officer may have a representative attend."

Correspondence history with this facility was reviewed.  It was noted the facility notified MCAQD of the scheduled testing on August 10, 2025 which was 13 calendar days prior to the scheduled testing date, as required by Permit Condition 12c.  This time period included ten business days and therefore was accepted as two weeks prior to the testing date.

Facility is advised that notification the test is occurring is required two calendar weeks (14 days) prior to testing in the future.  

Reporting of test results is not required, as results are publicly posted by Arizona Department of Environmental Quality (ADEQ), and notification to Maricopa County Air Quality Department (MCAQD) of test results is not required by any current permit condition.  These results are reviewed during the annual inspection file review, and as such, Inspectors are aware of the results prior to inspecting the facility.  Furthermore, administration of these specific tests, and enforcement of compliance, is conducted entirely by ADEQ.  

It is further noted, category selected for this submission was "performance test result" and future notifications should be reported under the "notifications" category.  "Performance Test Result"  dropdown should indicate "no". 

If there are questions or concerns, please contact me using the phone number or email in the email signature line attached to this report.</td></tr>
