<tr><td>CRPT010683</td><td>F001257</td><td>Costco Wholesale #436</td><td>Minor</td><td>Gasoline Resale</td><td>CMP000948</td><td>Costco Wholesale Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Notification</td><td>Testing notification</td><td>08/07/2025</td><td>08/10/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Permit Condition 11 of the facility’s current permit, issued on June 27, 2025, requires the following tests to be conducted every three years:

- CARB Vapor Recovery Test Procedure TP-201.1E
- CARB Vapor Recovery Test Procedure TP-201.3

A review of AQD records did not confirm whether or when these tests have previously been conducted. However, the facility’s prior permit, issued on June 19, 2019, also included the same testing requirements under Condition 5, indicating that this is an ongoing, not  new requirement.

To clarify, I contacted Ray Gallagher, who confirmed that the required testing is performed every three years and that test results are submitted to the Arizona Department of Agriculture (AZDA). This was verified through the AZDA database. Mr. Gallagher stated that testing notifications would be submitted going forward.

Although documentation was provided indicating the due date for the next required tests, it did not specify the actual scheduled date of testing. Upon inquiry, Mr. Gallagher confirmed that the testing is scheduled for August 22, 2025. I advised Mr. Gallagher to include the specific testing date in future notifications to ensure clarity and compliance.</td></tr>
