<tr><td>CRPT010419</td><td>F003110</td><td>WestRock</td><td>Minor</td><td>Pulp and Paper Plant</td><td>CMP003585</td><td>WestRock CP LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>7-Day Notice</td><td>The facility is replacing the starch kitchen which includes a number of components that are listed with AQD ID numbers in the permit: MAT001, MIX001, OTH001, TNK003, TNK004, TNK001 and BAG001.  The project will benefit the facility by 1) providing greater reliability of the starch system, 2) replacement of obsolete equipment, and 3) improved starch consistency.  There will be no production capacity or emission increases related to this project.  Attached is the list of equipment including manufacturer and model numbers where available.

In addition to the equipment update for the air permit and as communicated Addison Garwood, permitting engineer, by email, the facility is also requesting removal on permit conditions that are not applicable to the facility: 1) #10, 11 and 12 refer to Spray Coating Operations (the plant does not have this operation), 2) #18 is a sulfur limit for fuel oil and the plant is not permitted to burn fuel oil and 3) #20 relates to baseline monitoring and testing for a new boiler and the boiler at the plant is an existing unit.</td><td>08/06/2025</td><td>08/07/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Equipment change notification received and accepted. Equipment change complete in IMPACT.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT010666</td><td>F001267</td><td>Costco Gasoline Loc. 827</td><td>Minor</td><td>Gasoline Resale</td><td>CMP000948</td><td>Costco Wholesale Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Notification</td><td>Testing notification for vapor recovery testing</td><td>08/06/2025</td><td>08/10/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Permit Condition 11 of the facility’s current permit, issued on April 28, 2022, requires the following tests to be conducted every three years:

- CARB Vapor Recovery Test Procedure TP-201.1E
- CARB Vapor Recovery Test Procedure TP-201.3

A review of AQD records did not confirm whether or when these tests have previously been conducted. However, the facility’s prior permit, issued on April 19, 2017, also included the same testing requirements under Condition 5, indicating that this is an ongoing, not  new requirement.

To clarify, I contacted Ray Gallagher, who confirmed that the required testing is performed every three years and that test results are submitted to the Arizona Department of Agriculture (AZDA). This was verified through the AZDA database. Mr. Gallagher stated that testing notifications would be submitted going forward.

Although documentation was provided indicating the due date for the next required tests, it did not specify the actual scheduled date of testing. Upon inquiry, Mr. Gallagher confirmed that the testing is scheduled for August 21, 2025. I advised Mr. Gallagher to include the specific testing date in future notifications to ensure clarity and compliance.</td></tr>
