<tr><td>CRPT010637</td><td>F001504</td><td>New Harquahala Generating</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP002301</td><td>New Harquahala Generating Co LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Notification</td><td>New Harquahala Generating Company, LLC owns and operates the New Harquahala Generating Company (NHGC), a merchant power plant in Maricopa County, Arizona, currently generating approximately 1,100 MW using combined-cycle combustion turbines and pipeline-quality natural gas. In 2024, Capital Power acquired a 50% ownership interest in the facility, with the other 50% owned by BlackRock. Capital Power operates, maintains, and manages the facility. The proposed Expansion Project will add one Siemens SGT6-5000F simple-cycle combustion turbine (260 MW) and associated support equipment, including two 45,000-gallon aqueous ammonia tanks for the SCR system. The purpose of the provided air quality modeling protocol is to evaluate emissions of criteria pollutants to demonstrate compliance with PSD requirements under 40 CFR §52.21, including NAAQS and PSD increments, and to satisfy Maricopa County’s Minor NSR modification thresholds per Rule 241.</td><td>08/05/2025</td><td>08/14/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Modeling protocol reviewed, letter with comments sent back to the source.</td></tr>
