<tr><td>CRPT010631</td><td>F001528</td><td>Honeywell International</td><td>Minor</td><td>Aerospace Component Manufacturing</td><td>CMP001662</td><td>Honeywell International Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>40 CFR Part 63 Subpart N Ongoing Compliance Status Report</td><td>07/30/2025</td><td>08/10/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Per part 46.a.ii of the facility's permit, an ongoing compliance status report was submitted as required by 40 CFR 63.344(e).</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT010559</td><td>F041443</td><td>TSMC Phoenix Project</td><td>Title V</td><td>Semiconductors and Electronics</td><td>CMP021099</td><td>TSMC Arizona Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Semiannual Monitoring Report and Compliance Certification - January to June 2025</td><td>07/30/2025</td><td>08/29/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Review of the certification compliance report. 

Report was submitted prior to the due date.

The Compliance Certification included the following information:
- The identification of each permit term or condition of the permit that is the basis of the certification, the compliance status of each term or condition, whether the compliance was intermittent or continuous, and the method(s) used for determining the compliance status of the source.
- Description of and an explanation for any deviations from any permit condition at any time.
- A certification as to the truth and accuracy of the information provided.

Two deviations were documented by the facility as follows: 
May 2, 2025: Combustion chamber temperature was &lt; 733 C, equipment was still operational. 
Excess emissions were documented at the time of the deviation. 
The VOC02 was &lt; 733 C for 4 minutes. The root cause of the issue was determined to be a natural gas valve fault. 
The corrective actions that were taken were to manually adjust the valve and modify the PID. 

June 29, 2025: The combustion chamber temperature was &gt; 787 C. The temperature was increased to 790 C.  
No excess emissions were documented at the time of the deviation. 
The root cause of the issue was determined to be an air flow balancing issue. 
The corrective actions that were taken were to manually adjust the damper. 

An email was sent to source to request Certification Report and Semi-Annual Compliance Report to be submitted as separate reports. 

Due date was for the submittal was given to the end of business on August 22, 2025.

No compliance issues were documented during the review of the certification report.</td></tr>
