<tr><td>CRPT010628</td><td>F000014</td><td>Salt River Project - Agua Fria Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Semiannual Compliance Certification and Title V Monitoring Report. January 1, 2025 through June 30, 2025. Due July 30, 2025.</td><td>07/30/2025</td><td>10/20/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Review of the facility's Semiannual Monitoring Report and Title V Compliance Certification submitted for the time period: January 1, 2025, to June 30, 2025. The report was received by the department on July 30, 2025, which was before deadline required by Permit Condition 51.a-b (by the end of the month following the reporting period). 


SEMIANNUAL MONITORING REPORT [Permit Condition 51.a]:
The Semiannual Monitoring Report included all of the required elements listed under Permit Condition 51.a. 

Notably, the 12-month rolling total Hazardous Air Pollutants (HAPs) emissions as of June 2025 (highest month) were as follows: 
• Maximum Single HAP Emissions was 2.1 tons, which was within the 9.0-ton limit [Permit Condition 18.d]
• Total HAPs Emissions was 2.6 tons, which was within the 22.5-ton limit [Permit Condition 18.d]

No noncompliance issues were noted. 


SEMIANNUAL COMPLIANCE CERTIFICATION [Permit Condition 51.b]: 
The Semiannual Title V Compliance Certification correctly identified the compliance statuses for all of the facility's permit conditions. 

One permit deviation was reported as follows: 

• Permit Condition 6.a: Asbestos: 
- Asbestos renovation projects were completed without submitting the applicable NESHAP application from January 1, 2025, through February 11, 2025. The estimated combined amount of regulated asbestos containing material (RACM) generated was greater than 160 square feet and 260 linear feet. 
- Corrective Action: The Annual Operations & Maintenance (O&M) renovation application was filed on February 11, 2025. Site was notified to stop and reschedule all asbestos work until February 25, 2025. A work order was set up to remind the Engineering department to confirm filing of the application in the future. 

No noncompliance issues were noted.</td></tr>
