<tr><td>CRPT010593</td><td>F001522</td><td>Mesquite Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP002166</td><td>Mesquite Power LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Enclosed for your review, please find the Compliance Certification and Semiannual Monitoring Report from Mesquite Generating Station covering the reporting time period from January 1, 2025 to June 30, 2025, as required in the applicable Title V Permit condition 21.c. If you have any questions regarding this report, please contact D’Armond Chee at (602) 236-0039.</td><td>07/28/2025</td><td>07/30/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The report was submitted within the appropriate time frame.

The report should include, at a minimum, the following:
1) The identification of each term or condition of the permit that is the basis of the certification;
2) The compliance status;
3) Whether compliance was continuous or intermittent;
4) The method(s) used for determining the compliance status of the source, currently and over the reporting period;
5) Other facts as the Control Officer may require to determine compliance status of the source;
6) Each report shall cover all instances of deviations from these permit conditions during the reporting period, the cause of the deviations if any were present, and any applicable corrective actions taken;
7) The Permittee shall include a copy of the portion of the odor log which covers the applicable 6 month reporting period in each of the semiannual compliance reports. If no complaints were received during the reporting period, a statement to that effect may be substituted for the copy of the odor log; and
8) Permittee shall comply with applicable reporting requirements for support operations including Architectural Coatings (Permit Condition 24), Abrasive Blasting (Permit Condition 25), Spray Coating (Permit Condition 26), Solvent Cleaning Operations (Permit Condition 27), and Volatile Organic Compounds (Permit Condition 28).
9) The Permittee shall include the calendar year-to-date hours for all combined cycle systems in which the Tuning and Testing limitations of Table 18.5 were relied upon.

The format of the report satisfies items (1), (2), (3), and (4) from the list above. Each permit condition was listed with statements demonstrating the facility was In Compliance and denoting that the compliance status was continuous or intermittent. 

An intermittent status was noted for Permit Conditions 4.a-d., 18.c.i., 19.e.ii., and 20.f.iii. 

Excess emissions of ammonia from Unit 2 were emitted between the hours of 18:00 and 20:00 on April 6, 2025. The unit exceeded the 10.0 ppmc ammonia normal operation limit on a 24-hour average between the hours of 17:00 and 19:00 on April 7, 2025.  The 24-hr and 72-hr reports for the excess emissions event were submitted to MCAQD as required.

In February 2025, monthly conductivity/TDS sample was collected from Cooling Tower #2 and exceeded the TDS permit limit of 30,000mg/L with a result of 31,400 mg/L. When a sample that is collected close to 15.0 cycles per day, higher levels of conductivity and TDS levels will measured. Field readings were taken, which yielded 26,500 mg/L and digital PI results yielded 27,100 mg/L. The analysis sample yielded 31,400 mg/L for TDS. 
A resample was collected for laboratory analysis which yielded a result of 29,400 mg/L. 
Conductivity and TDS field measurements will continue to be recorded twice a day during each shift, continuous instrument measurements, calculated TDS and calculated cycles of concentration will be monitored more closely to reduce the risk of future exceedances. 

The method used for determining the compliance status was also detailed for each permit condition.

Item (6) - The report demonstrates the facility was in compliance with each permit condition, except for deviations from permit conditions 4.a-d., 18.c.i., 19.e.ii., and 20.f.iii. Deviations occurred in February and April 2025.

Item (7) - The report states there were no odor log entries during the reporting period.

Item (8) - The report indicates the facility is complying with the reporting requirements for operations listed in Permit Conditions 24-28. The report states the status of each of the operations on site for the reporting period.

Item (9) - The report states no tuning and testing was performed during the reporting period. 

No compliance issues were noted.</td></tr>
