<tr><td>CRPT010584</td><td>F001504</td><td>New Harquahala Generating</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP002301</td><td>New Harquahala Generating Co LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>72 hours Notification Report</td><td>07/24/2025</td><td>07/28/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Reviewal of 72 -HR Excess Emissions Notification Report for April 08, 2025

During an internal reviewal of the emissions data for the current year, the facility identified a potential NOx excess emissions event that occurred for April 08, 2025 for Turbine 2. Due to a change in the ammonia injection valve position, this resulted in an exceedance of the 25 lb/hr NOx limitation listed in Table 2 of Permit Condition 18.a.iii.

As the facility failed to report the excess emissions event within the 24-Hr and 72-Hr required reporting periods as required by Permit Condition 16.f., the facility has been issued a notice of non-compliance. 

Additionally, as the facility exceeded the emission limitation listed in Permit Condition 18.a.iii. Table 2 for NOx, the facility has been issued a notice of non-compliance.

See Inspection Report INSP211278</td></tr>
