The compliance report covers Permit Conditions 11.a and 11.b, with notes as follows:

PC 11.a.i: 12-month rolling total emissions as of Jun25:
- HTF HAP Emissions: 50.23tons (limit: 113tons)
- TES VOC Emissions: 0.13tons, with no individual unit over 2.0tons (limit: 12.0tons)
- VOC Emissions from HTF Impacted Soil: 0.0tons, (limit: 2.0tons)
- Ullage system:
-- Total non-fugitive VOCs: 0.89tons (limit: 15tons)
-- Total non-fugitive HAPs: 0.88tons (limit: 15tons)
-- Single non-fugitve HAP (HTF): 0.88tons (limit: 15tons)
PC 11.a.ii: No deviations noted during the reporting period. It was noted that the PS8 testing was conducted in early July, however the test will have to be rerun due to high temperatures causing the CEMS to trip.
PC 11.a.iii: Per the report, the CEMS has been operating as expected. Five CEMS alerts were recorded during the period, with all being resolved without major issues.
PC 11.a.iv: 1230 ball joint leaks reported, grade 1/2/3, with 686 ball joints repacked and 124 ball joints to be repacked.
PC 11.a.v: No new HTF was added to the plant during the reporting period.
PC 11 a.vi: No HTF has been added to the system, with a total HTF loss of 1.6tons.
PC 11 a.viii: No HTF impacted soil was stored on the biopad during the reporting period. Per the report, all HTF impacted soil is stored in sealed drums until removed from the site.
PC 11.b: Per report, facility was in continuous compliance for all permit conditions during the reporting period.

No issues of Non-Compliance were observed after review of the report.</td></tr>
