<tr><td>CRPT010520</td><td>F002411</td><td>CMC Steel Fabricators</td><td>Title V</td><td>Metal Fabrication</td><td>CMP000856</td><td>CMC Steel Fabricators Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Order of Abatement by Consent SA006812 - CMC Monthly Update 13</td><td>07/15/2025</td><td>07/16/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>OAC monthly update report for SA006812 (monthly update 13). 

CRPT010520: CMC is currently unable to operate Mesa Mill No. 2 at or near its maximum production rate on a sustained basis, and therefore is unable to achieve continuous compliance with the 30-day rolling average limits for SO2, CO, and NOx. 

Current report received on July 15, 2025, indicates that the 30-day rolling averages for June 2025 are 0.28 lb/ton for NOx, 0.27 lb/ton for SO2, and 2.61 lb/ton for CO.

NOx is below the emission limit, SO2 is below the emission limit, and CO is below the emission limit in PC Table 18.c.2.

Emission limits in PC 18.c.2 for Mesa Mill No.2 are: 0.30 lb/ton of steel for NOx, 0.30 lb/ton of steel for SO2, and 4.00 lb/ton of steel for CO.

Note: The commissioning issues presented in the table have due dates of September 2025, October 2025 and December 2025. 

This table reflects discussions that have been held in the past between CMC and MCAQD. For this report, the facility removed the ECS Docusign Envelope  since it has been resolved. The facility also removed the DRB item since we do not plan on using at this time.</td></tr>
