<tr><td>CRPT010366</td><td>F000701</td><td>Intel Corp - Ocotillo Campus</td><td>Title V</td><td>Semiconductors and Electronics</td><td>CMP001723</td><td>Intel Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Test Report</td><td>2025 F42 EXSC performance tests completed from April 4th -11th.  F42 EXSC units 4 and 5 exhibited higher HF, HCl, and IPA MDLs. This was due to the degradation of the FTIR infrared (IR) signal at the higher frequency ranges (where these compounds absorb infrared radiation). Since there were a few hours of FTIR data collected without signal loss, the MDLs for these compounds were calculated using 2 MDLs (the MDL when the signal was normal and the 2nd MDL when the IR signal had degraded). To arrive at a single MDL, the weighted average of the two DLs (as a function of time) was used - this is shown in the attachment (2025 Intel OC F42 EXSC Outlet Calcs - full 8-hour run showing pre/post signal loss). Per the conversation with MCAQD on 6/10 - Intel has provided the data from the full 8-hours as well as the adjusted data accounting for the data prior to signal loss.</td><td>06/12/2025</td><td>08/08/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr>
