<tr><td>CRPT010184</td><td>F001759</td><td>Gila River Power Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Enclosed, please find the Semi-Annual Compliance Certification and Monitoring Report & Part 60 Excess Emissions and Monitoring Systems Performance Report for Salt River Project Agricultural Improvement and Power District (SRP) Gila River Power Station (Gila River), reflecting compliance status from October 1, 2024, to March 31, 2025, as required by Permit Condition 21.a. of the Gila River Title V Permit P0009823. A single compliance certification is included in Attachment 1 to demonstrate compliance. Additionally, enclosed is the semi-annual monitoring report, summarizing monitoring results as required by the specific conditions of the Gila River Title V Permit in effect for this monitoring period. The monitoring summaries coincide with the compliance certification period and reflect data and observations from October 1, 2024, to March 31, 2025.</td><td>04/30/2025</td><td>05/08/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The report was submitted within the appropriate time frame.

The report includes, at a minimum, the following:

The report summarized the compliance status with respect to each permit contained in the permit. 

The report demonstrates this requirement by describing and explaining any deviations from any permit condition at any time. 

The facility denotes deviations from various permit conditions as follows: 

Permit Conditions 19.e.i.1, 19.e.i.3., 19.e.i.9., 19.e.i.10. 
While troubleshooting calibration drift on the Unit 2A CO CEMS, SRP discovered an error in the county approved O&M and QA Plan. The approved plan states a 2.5% of span performance specification for the daily calibrations of the CO CEMS. SRP did not intend to subject the CO CEMS to a more stringent CD performance specification and therefore Gila River’s data acquisition and handling system was configured using the performance specifications. This difference between the O&M and QA Plan and the regulatory requirements results in a deviation.
A revised CEMS O&M and QA Plan was submitted to MCAQD and approved on February 25, 2025. To correct the improper validation of CO data prior to CDs exceeding four times the performance specification SRP is continuing to identify the affected hours and will invalidate the data as necessary. Once all hours have been invalidated, SRP will submit revised monitoring reports to reflect the change in monitor availability.

Permit Condition 19.f.iii. 
A review of the plant’s operating data revealed that the catalyst differential pressure (dP) for Unit 2B was outside of the operating range of 0-5" of H2O. Historical data showed that the dP had been operating outside the approved range continuously since December 19, 2024.
At the time this deviation report was logged, it was discovered that there was a cracked metal fitting connecting the pressure transmitter to the isolation valve for the Unit 2B oxidation catalyst dP gauge. The fitting was replaced and the pressure readings returned to the normal operating range of 0 - 5” H2O. Preventive measures have been developed to include alarms when readings fall outside the operating range of 0 - 5" of H2O.

Permit Condition 20.e.i. 
Conductivity analysis was omitted in error for the evaporation pond for the evaporation samples collected during the months of July - September 2024. 
Gila River has reviewed the permit requirements with the environmental staff and revised its monthly sampling practices to ensure that both TDS and conductivity are tested going forward during months that the MSE is operated.

Permit Condition 19.e.ii.1., 20.a.ii. 
A temporary like-kind NOx analyzer was installed at Unit 4B and the diagnostic linearity test was never performed, thus the NOx data resulted in failure of Unit 4B CEMS to meet the minimum data capture requirement for NOx monitoring for 31 consecutive days. 
Corrective actions include implementing a new CEMS analyzer maintenance tracking form to ensure recertification and diagnostic testing events are identified and are performed as needed. Additional
training on maintenance activities will be provided. 

The report includes the 12-month rolling total hours of startup and shutdown operation and monthly normal and duct burner operating hours for each combined cycle.

No visible emissions were observed on site during the reporting period. 

No odor complaints were received during the reporting period. 

The emergency fire pump is fueled with ultra-low sulfur diesel fuel. Bill of lading shows the facility receives ultra-low sulfur diesel fuel.  

The summary of the monthly and 12-month rolling total records of gasoline is included in the report. 

The gasoline AST at the facility is insignificant, thus no inspections are conducted. 

The MSEs did not operate during the reporting period.

The performance summary reports for the CEMS analyzers is included in the report. 

No compliance issues were noted during the review of the compliance report.</td></tr>
