<tr><td>CRPT010181</td><td>F000015</td><td>Salt River Project - Kyrene Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>O&M Plan</td><td>Enclosed is a revised Operation and Maintenance (O&M) Plan for the continuous emissions monitoring system (CEMS) at Salt River Project’s (SRP) Kyrene Generating Station (Kyrene). Revisions to the O&M Plan include:
 - Format changes and minor verbiage changes
 - Revised CO, NOx, and O2 instrument types and CO high analyzer operating and display ranges to reflect replacement analyzers
 - Clarification of corrective action procedures in Section II
 - Revised CO and NOx low range Part 60 CGA QA activity range in Section III to 50-60% of span
 - Inclusion of QA testing frequencies Section III ‘QA Requirements for Part 60 CEMS’ and ‘QA Requirements for Part 75 CEMS’ table
 - Addition of O2 RATA requirements and revision of NOx RATA QA Activity language in the ‘QA Requirements for Part 75 CEMS’ table in Section III
 - Addition of Section IV and Appendix 10 to include a CEMS spare part inventory.
 - Revised daily calibration QA checks in Appendix 1</td><td>04/30/2025</td><td>05/08/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Revised O&M and QA plan</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT010180</td><td>F001504</td><td>New Harquahala Generating</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP002301</td><td>New Harquahala Generating Co LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Semi Annual Title V compliance Certification and Report for 10/01/2024 to 03/31/2025.</td><td>04/30/2025</td><td>06/09/2025</td><td>No-Revision Requested</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Reviewal of Semi-Annual Title V Compliance Certification for October 01, 2024 through March 31, 2025.

Pg.76 of this report was an attachment demonstrating the facility had five hours of excess emissions for Turbine 1 of NOx during the startup phase. Additional information was requested from the source to help clarify the excess emissions as no reporting had been received for this event.

Source confirmed the five hours of exceedances took place on November 22, 2024 and March 04, 2025 and exceeded Table 3 NOx limit of 220 lb/hr within Permit Condition 18. 

Notices of non-compliances were issued to the facility for failure to report the exceedances and for exceeding their emission limitations listed within their air quality permit. Due to these non-compliances being issued, the facility has been informed they are required to revise this certification report to now reflect the two non-compliances. 

See Inspection Report INSP210546 for more information.</td></tr>
