<tr><td>CRPT010175</td><td>F000441</td><td>Butterfield Station Facility</td><td>Title V</td><td>Landfills</td><td>CMP003877</td><td>Waste Management Arizona Landfills Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Butterfield Station Landfill April 2025 Semi-Annual NESHAP Report, October 1, 2024 to March 31, 2025 reporting period</td><td>04/30/2025</td><td>06/19/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Review of Butterfield Station Facility's Semiannual Monitoring Report and Title V Compliance Certification
Reporting Period: October 1, 2024 – March 31, 2025

The Semiannual Monitoring Report was submitted to the department prior to the required air permit deadline. All reporting requirements listed under Permit Condition 21.a were included in the monitoring report and were found to be in compliance with air quality standards.

The facility's Title V Compliance Certification accurately listed the compliance status for each permit condition. No deviations were reported during the reporting period.

No noncompliance issues were noted

Note: The facility’s Semiannual Monitoring Report referenced specific compliance requirements, including startup, shutdown, and malfunction (SSM) reporting, in accordance with both Subpart WWW and the facility’s active Title V permit applicable during the reporting period. The current permit was renewed in April 2025, shortly after the reporting period ended.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT010174</td><td>F001209</td><td>SR 85 Landfill</td><td>Title V</td><td>Landfills</td><td>CMP000821</td><td>City of Phoenix</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>SR85 Semi-Annual Report for the period of October 4, 2024 through April 3, 2025</td><td>04/29/2025</td><td>06/30/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Reviewal of the combined Semi-Annual Report Compliance Report & Title V Certification Report covering the period of October 04, 2024 through April 03, 2025 in accordance with Permit Condition #21(b) and 21(c). 

Facility submitted the report prior to the May 03, 2025 deadline. All required information was supplied within the compliance report submitted.

Intermittent compliance status selected for the Permit Condition #21(c) for failure to submit the prior Annual Compliance Certification by the November 3, 2024 deadline. Corrective action was taken and the report was submitted on December 19, 2024. 

No matters of non-compliance were noted during the reviewal of this report.

INFORMATION REVIEWED
21(c)(I): Monthly opacity reports have been regularly submitted throughout this reporting period.

21(c)(II): No odor complaints were reported for this period.

21(c)(III): Gasoline throughput limit has not been exceeded. Most recent twelve month rolling throughput was 3,179 gallons of gasoline.

21(c)(IV): H2S testing was not required/requested nor conducted during this time period.

21(c)(V): VOC emissions report supplied. This data value was discussed with the Permitting Division as the VOC value provided did not match the VOC values supplied in the annual VOC report, nor in the most recent emissions inventory. Clarification was provided and the VOC value/calculations that have been supplied in this report have been accepted.

21(c)(VI): No exceedances and no deviations occurred.

21(c)(VII): No bypass lines are incorporated into the design.

21(c)(VIII): Flame failure occurred on February 26, 2025 for 2 hrs and 59 mins. Clarification was requested via email from the source on this event. Source clarified that Flare 3 was the only flare operating during the approximate three hour malfunction, while the remaining two flares were on standby mode. Documentation was provided to demonstrate that gas was not flowing to any of the flares during the time of the malfunction.

21(c)(IX): Gas collection system did not exceed five days of no operation.

21(c)(X): The surface was traversed and did not have any exceedances or deviations of 500 ppm of methane.

21(c)(XI): No expansions have been made to the gas collection system.

21(c)(XII): Plant is operated in accordance with plans.

Architectural Coatings: No architectural coating were used during this period.

Landfill Liquids: 30,450 gallons of condensate were recirculated back to the landfill.


RECORDS REQUEST EMAILS SENT
Clarification email below was sent to the source regarding the flame failure on July 10, 2025.

I’m reaching out today regarding the Semi-Annual Compliance Report submitted for SR85 Landfill on April 29, 2025 (CRPT010174). During my reviewal of this report, I noticed that on Page 4 Number 8 “Section 21.B. VIII, Control Device Operation 40 CFR 60 §757(f)(3), §63.1955 (NESHAP Report), and §63.1981(h)(3) and (4) (Subpart AAAA)” a flame failure was report for nearly three hours. 

Please answer the following items concerning the flame failure:

1.	Could you please clarify if this is stating that all the flares were down for nearly three hours or if this was a specific flare? 
2.	If this was only for a specific flare, please provide clarification of which flare this occurred at. 
3.	If the failure only occurred at one flare, please provide clarification if gases were routed to a different flare at this time and if so which flare. 

Clarification email below sent to the source on July 11, 2025.
1.	Could you provide the reason that the other two flares were not operating/in standby when Flare 3 was experiencing flame failure?  
2.	Based on 40 CFR 60.753(e), please provide flow meter data for February 26, 2025, demonstrating that the gas mover system had been shut down and all valves in the collection and control system contributing to venting of the gas to the atmosphere were closed within 1 hour.</td></tr>
