<tr><td>CRPT010085</td><td>F002411</td><td>CMC Steel Fabricators</td><td>Title V</td><td>Metal Fabrication</td><td>CMP000856</td><td>CMC Steel Fabricators Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Order of Abatement by Consent - SA006812 - CMC Monthly Update Report 10</td><td>04/15/2025</td><td>04/16/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>OAC monthly update report for SA006812 (monthly update 10).

CRPT010085: CMC is currently unable to operate Mesa Mill No. 2 at or near its maximum production rate on a sustained basis, and therefore is unable to achieve continuous compliance with the 30-day rolling average limits for SO2, CO, and NOx.
 
Current report received on April 15, 2025, indicates that the 30-day rolling averages for March 2025 are 0.30 lb/ton for NOx, 0.25 lb/ton for SO2, and 3.22 lb/ton for CO.

NOx is at the emission limit, SO2 is below the emission limit, and CO is below the emission limit in PC Table 18.c.2.

Emission limits in PC 18.c.2 for Mesa Mill No.2 are: 0.30 lb/ton of steel for NOx, 0.30 lb/ton of steel for SO2, and 4.00 lb/ton of steel for CO.

Note: The commissioning issues presented in the monthly update 10 table have due dates of August 2025.</td></tr>
