<tr><td>CRPT009986</td><td>F000789</td><td>Microchip Technology - Tempe</td><td>Minor</td><td>Semiconductors and Electronics</td><td>CMP002193</td><td>Microchip Technology Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>This is to serve as notice for an event on the Munters VOC Abatement Unit RCTO 20-1 to the Maricopa County Air Quality Department (MCAQD) from Microchip Technology Incorporated in Tempe (Microchip Tempe). This event occurred on March 29th, 2025.</td><td>03/29/2025</td><td>04/15/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This compliance report is a self-report of an equipment fault that occurred on RCTO 20-1 and RCTO 20-2. The report was submitted on March 29, 2025, and reviewed on April 15, 2025. No violations were noted. 

RCTO 20-1 went offline due to high oxidizer Temperature at 7:46 AM on March 29th, 2025. At 10:05 AM, the backup VOC abatement unit, RCTO 20-2 was brought online.

This event led to a bypass of the RCTO units for 2.23 hours. Excess VOC emissions during the event were approximately 11.39 pounds, with an emissions rate of 5.1 pounds per hour.

The facility submitted the compliance report as indicated in Permit Condition 21.

The facility complies with its current permit per Permit Condition 6.a.iii. since RCTO 20-1 was brought online within the 4-hour emission bypass period.</td></tr>
