<tr><td>CRPT009778</td><td>F000789</td><td>Microchip Technology - Tempe</td><td>Minor</td><td>Semiconductors and Electronics</td><td>CMP002193</td><td>Microchip Technology Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>This notice is to serve as the 72-hour detailed report from Microchip Technology Inc., Tempe to MCAQD regarding the VOC abatement equipment faults that occurred on RCTO 20-2 and RCTO 20-1 on February 19th, 2025 at 11:19 am.</td><td>02/21/2025</td><td>02/24/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This compliance report is a self-report of an equipment faults that occurred on RCTO 20-2 and RCTO 20-1 on February 19, 2025, at 11:19 a.m.

The self-report was submitted as a compliance report within 2 working days of the equipment malfunction as required in Rule 130, so the facility notified the Maricopa County Air Quality Department within the proper time frame.

RCTO 20-1 was brought up and was abating at 6:52 a.m. 

The event resulted in 19.6 hours of downtime. Excess emissions of 100 pounds (lbs) of VOCs were released at a rate of 5.12 lbs per hour.

The facility submitted the compliance report as indicated in Permit Condition 21.

The facility violated their current permit (P0011578) per Permit Condition 6.a.iii. since RCTO 20-1 was brought online after the 4 hour emission bypass period.

Reference inspection report INSP206872 for more details.</td></tr>
