<tr><td>CRPT009752</td><td>F004173</td><td>Air Transport Components</td><td>Minor</td><td>Aerospace Component Manufacturing</td><td>CMP000141</td><td>Air Transport Components LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>FEB-2024/FEB-2025 ANNUAL REPORT.</td><td>02/14/2025</td><td>05/05/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This facility submitted a permit revision application on August 30, 2024.  As the previous permit is expired, and the new permit has not been issued, permit number 180017, revised August 13, 2018, will be used for compliance determination.   

Annual report titled “FEB-2024/FEB-2025 ANNUAL REPORT”  was reviewed on May 5, 2025, by MCAQD Inspector I, Nicholas Gilham. 

It was noted the annual compliance report was submitted on February 14, 2025.  

Permit condition 16(a)(ii) states:
“Each annual compliance report must be prepared no later than January 31 of the year immediately following the reporting period and kept in a readily-accessible location for inspector review. If a deviation has occurred during the year, each annual compliance report must be submitted along with the deviation report, and postmarked or delivered no later than January 31 of the year immediately following the reporting period.”

It is stated in permit condition 12a the annual compliance report should contain information for the "calendar year" (January 1, 2024 through December 31, 2024) with an inferred 30 day preparation period immediately following.  

Permit condition 16(a)(iii) states:
“The Annual Certification of Compliance Report shall contain a statement that the Permittee has implemented the applicable management practices, as practicable.”

I determined this compliance report was submitted 14 days after the required reporting period and preparation period which ended on January 31, 2025.  Report did not reference the correct months of operation.   Report did not contain the required statement indicating “applicable management practices” were implemented, signed by a responsible official.  

As no “deviations” were reported by this facility and no non-compliant conditions were observed during the reporting period, as evidenced by no inspection occurring within the reporting period, an annual compliance report was not required to be submitted by this facility, therefore no violation will be issued for submitting the report late, report containing incorrect reporting period, or lacking a statement of implementation from a responsible official.  It was noted after review of attached documents that reporting period was inconsequential to the compliance determination in this instance, however, future reports containing usage, purchase, or disposal data should comply with the calendar year requirement.  

I reviewed the following documents. 

1.	Annual report contained filter efficiency documentation for 2EKK1 filters (see attachment 772489), which have an efficiency rating of 98% which exceeds the Prep/Sanding Booth requirement of permit condition 29a of 92% and the general spray coating requirement of 92% removal efficiency and meets the 98% filter efficiency requirement for HAP containing coatings in forced air spray booths.  I determined filter efficiency as reported is compliant. 
2.	Annual report contained the EPA NESHAP 6H certification for Adrian Garibay (see attachment 772490) who completed the training on November 1, 2023.  As the training remains in effect for 60 months I determined this training was compliant.  
3.	Annual report contained the EPA NESHAP 6H certification for Frank M Armenta (see attachment 772491) who completed the training on November 1, 2023.  As the training remains in effect for 60 months I determined this training was compliant.  
4.	Annual report contained the EPA NESHAP 6H certification for James Adams (see attachment 772492) who completed the training on November 1, 2023.  As the training remains in effect for 60 months I determined this training was compliant.  

No emissions inventory is due or directed as of the date of Compliance Report review.  

I completed my review of this Compliance Report and prepared a Compliance Report Inspection.</td></tr>
