<tr><td>CRPT009711</td><td>F000789</td><td>Microchip Technology - Tempe</td><td>Minor</td><td>Semiconductors and Electronics</td><td>CMP002193</td><td>Microchip Technology Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>This is to serve as notice for an event on the Munters VOC Abatement Unit RCTO 20-2 to the Maricopa County Air Quality Department (MCAQD) from Microchip Technology Incorporated in Tempe (Microchip Tempe).</td><td>02/10/2025</td><td>02/10/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This compliance report is a self-report of an equipment malfunction that caused VOC emissions to bypass RCTO 20-2 for 3.42 hours, beginning at 9:40 a.m. and ending at 1:05 p.m. on February 9, 2025. 

The 3.42-hour bypass event was a result of a combustion fan overload. Approximately 17.4 pounds (lbs) of VOCs were released at a rate of 5.1 lbs per hour.

The self-report was submitted as a compliance report within 2 working days of the equipment malfunction as required in Rule 130, so the facility notified the Maricopa County Air Quality Department within the proper time frame. 

The facility submitted the compliance report as indicated in Permit Condition 21.

The facility did not violate their current permit (P0011578) per Permit Condition 6.a.iii. since RCTO 20-1 was brought online within 4 hours.

No compliance issues were noted.</td></tr>
