<tr><td>CRPT009600</td><td>F000701</td><td>Intel Corp - Ocotillo Campus</td><td>Title V</td><td>Semiconductors and Electronics</td><td>CMP001723</td><td>Intel Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>This is the Annual 2024 Compliance Report along with the H2 2024 Semi-Annual Compliance Report</td><td>01/29/2025</td><td>02/10/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This report has been reviewed within the FCE Report for the INSP203395. See report for full record review and compliance determination.

This includes the Title V Compliance Certification required of the facility in permit condition 40.c. It also includes the H2 Semi-Annual Compliance Report of the period July 1, 2024 – December 31, 2024, required of the facility in permit conditions 3.h and 40.b.
This report was submitted on January 29, 2025, which is within 30 days of the end of each reporting period.

The Title V Compliance Certification reported 2 intermittent compliance determinations. These were both fully detailed in the H2 Semi-Annual Report including the Cause, Corrective Action, and Preventative Measures.
-	Condition 30.a and b of P0010018 for Fugitive Dust From Dust-Generating Operations – Dust Control Plan Requirements was reported as Intermittent stating “One dust control permit deviation occurred in 2024. Refer to the H2 Semi-Annual Report. I am in the process of locating this report with the facility contacts.
-	Condition 47.a of P0010018 for Site Wide Requirements - Contingent Requirements (Asbestos) was reported as Intermittent stating, “A Notice of Non-Compliance for failure to wait the 10 working days as required by the Asbestos NESHAP was issued to the Contractor. Refer to the 2024 H2 Semi-Annual Monitoring Report.” After further review I was able to determine that this was not issued as a Notice of Non-Compliance. It was included in Inspection Report INSP204284 as an Area of Concern where Senior Inspector/NESHAP Coordinator, Jeremy Robertson, stated, “During the discussion regarding the NESHAP notification, it was determined that both the modulars and lunch tent would fall under the NESHAP requirements, however there was some miscommunication which resulted in the lunch tent being dismantled prior to the 10 day wait period clearing. I discussed the issue with Ms. Toller and she stated that work would stop immediately until an inspection was completed to confirm that all NESHAP requirements are being met. Due to the miscommunication, a Notice of Non-Compliance for failure to wait the 10 working days as required by the NESHAP.”</td></tr>
