<tr><td>CRPT009591</td><td>F000014</td><td>Salt River Project - Agua Fria Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Salt River Project Agricultural Improvement and Power District (SRP) operates the Agua Fria Generating Station located at 7302 West Northern Avenue, Glendale, AZ 85303 in accordance with Title V Permit No. P0011528 (Permit).  SRP is submitting the enclosed Semiannual Monitoring Report and Compliance Certification to satisfy Permit Condition 51.a and 51.b for the reporting period from July 1, 2024 through December 31, 2024.  

Please contact Sheena Alvarado at (602) 236-7616 or Jenn Paskash at (602) 236-4746 if you have any questions.</td><td>01/28/2025</td><td>03/25/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Review of the facility's Semiannual Monitoring Report and Title V Compliance Certification submitted for the time period: July 1, 2024 - December 31, 2024. The report was received by the department before the required air permit deadline. The Semiannual Monitoring Report included all the mandatory information listed under the facility's permit reporting requirements.

Permit deviations reported:

Dust control records for the month of October 2024 were missing for an onsite 69kV and 230Kv SRP Substation yard.
Corrective Action: Facility personnel will be taking over responsibility for completing all onsite dust control inspections. Previous inspections were maintained by SRP's substation maintenance group, which is an offsite group that is tasked with maintaining all SRP facility switch yards.

The facility failed to provide a 7-day notice for a 6 square foot drift eliminator section replacement on Cooling Tower #2. No other cooling tower permit requirements were reported to be in noncompliance.
Corrective Action: The facility has updated the drift elimination inspection form to include information on notification requirements for non-routine maintenance activities.

Maricopa County Air Quality Department received an odor complaint for the facility in late August. The investigating inspector did not observe or detect any odors coming from the facility. SRP was notified of the odor complaint so the concern can be properly documented in the facility's odor log per P.C 18.a.

The Semiannual Title V Compliance Certification correctly identified the compliance statuses for all facility permit conditions.

No noncompliance issues were noted.</td></tr>
