<tr><td>CRPT009572</td><td>F002504</td><td>Solana Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP000333</td><td>Arizona Solar One LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Title V semi-annual compliance report and annual certification completed</td><td>01/27/2025</td><td>04/24/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semiannual Compliance Certification and Monitoring Report for the period of 7/01/2024 to 12/31/2024.  Report was submitted in a timely manner on 1/27/2025. 

The compliance report covers Permit Conditions 11.a and 11.b, with notes as follows:

PC 11.a.i: 12-month rolling total emissions as of Dec24:
- HTF HAP Emissions: 50.42tons (limit: 113tons)
- TES VOC Emissions: 0.06tons, with no individual unit over 2.0tons (limit: 12.0tons)
- VOC Emissions from HTF Impacted Soil: 0.0tons, (limit: 2.0tons)
- Ullage system:
-- Total non-fugitive VOCs: 1.14tons (limit: 15tons)
-- Total non-fugitive HAPs: 1.13tons (limit: 15tons)
-- Single non-fugitve HAP (HTF): 1.13tons (limit: 15tons)
PC 11.a.ii: No deviations noted during the reporting period.
PC 11.a.iii: Per the report, the CEMS has been operating as expected since the cleaning, repair and reprogramming adjustments made as part of the ongoing issue originally discussed with the MCAQD Performance Testing group. At the time of the report the RATA and drift testing was completed by Solana, however was still in review by the Performance Testing group. As of 4/23/2025, the Performance Testing group approved the RATA and drift testing.
PC 11.a.iv: 4053 ball joint leaks reported, grade 1/2/3, with 2156 ball joints repacked and 348 ball joints to be repacked.
PC 11.a.v: 221.86tons of new HTF was added to the plant in between Aug24 and Sep24.
PC 11 a.vi: No HTF has been added to the system, with a total HTF loss of 0.005tons.
PC 11 a.vii: No HTF impacted soil was stored on the biopad during the reporting period. Per the report, all HTF impacted soil is stored in sealed drums until removed from the site.
PC 11.b: Per report, facility was in continuous compliance for all permit conditions during the reporting period.

No issues of Non-Compliance were observed after review of the report.</td></tr>
