<tr><td>CRPT009524</td><td>F003328</td><td>Stryker - 51st St</td><td>Minor</td><td>EtO Facility</td><td>CMP003125</td><td>Stryker Sustainability Solutions Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>On January 16, 2025, Stryker Sustainability Solutions, Inc. (“Stryker”) reported via telephonic communication with the Business Services Division, Mr. Tallini, that an excess emission that occurred on January 14, 2025.
This letter is to provide a detailed report of the exceedance, in accordance to Section 501.2 of Rule 140, that occurred. 
On January 14, 2025, on or around 4:00PM, at 10232 South 51 St., Phoenix AZ 85044, 33.35284, -111.97366.
Stryker’ allowable emissions from a single run where 6.6lbs of EtO utilized is 0.066lbs.  The malfunction allowed for 1/3 of the emissions to escape the normally closed bypass resulting in excess emissions of 2.2lbs.
It was observed on or around 4:00pm. On or around 6:20pm the EtO sterilization system was set to idle, resulting no additional emissions.  Stryker stopped all EtO sterilization operations.  
The equipment from which the emissions emanated is the Sterilizer – Custom Built, 304 (the “Sterilizer”) and Equipment Assembly - ECS, Safe-Cell Model 2002 (“Safe-Cell”) (together, the “Equipment”).
The cause of the emission was due to an electrical malfunction at the safety pressure bypass valve at the Safe-Cell (the “Valve”), that prevented the Valve from closing, during an EtO purge.</td><td>01/17/2025</td><td>01/22/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Written notification of an excess emissions report was received on January 17, 2025, which is within 72 hours of the excess emission event. 

After reviewing the compliance report and permit, it was determined that the facility is in violation with Permit Condition 3.a.

