<tr><td>CRPT009488</td><td>F002411</td><td>CMC Steel Fabricators</td><td>Title V</td><td>Metal Fabrication</td><td>CMP000856</td><td>CMC Steel Fabricators Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Order of Abatement by Consent SA006812 - CMC Monthly Update 7</td><td>01/10/2025</td><td>01/14/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>OAC monthly update report for SA006812 (monthly update 7). 
CRPT009488: CMC is currently unable to operate Mesa Mill No. 2 at or near its maximum production rate on a sustained basis and therefore is unable to achieve continuous compliance with the 30-day rolling average limits for SO2, CO, and NOx. 
As indicated in CMC’s prior monthly update reports, the facility has made considerable improvement in NOx and CO emissions but SO2 emissions remain elevated. 
Current report received on January 10, 2025, indicates that the 30 day rolling averages are 0.30 lb/ton for NOx, 0.29 lb/ton for SO2 and 2.8 lb/ton for CO, which are at or below the limits in PC 18.c.
Limits in PC 18.c for Mesa Mill No.2 are 0.30 lb/ton of steel for NOx, 0.30 lb/ton of steel for SO2 and 4.00 lb/ton of steel for CO.</td></tr>
