<tr><td>CRPT009416</td><td>F002622</td><td>Nammo Talley</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP002276</td><td>Nammo Defense Systems Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Soil Vapor Extraction Unit Test Report</td><td>Performance Test Report for SVE System 11.20.24</td><td>12/30/2024</td><td>01/10/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>61.g: The carbon adsorption system achieved at least 90% removal efficiency for 1,1 - DCE and TCE. All other compounds were found to be below detectable thresholds.

63.a.i: Grab samples are taken at the influent and effluent of the soil vapor extraction unit (SVEU).
63.a.ii: Samples are analyzed using EPA method 8015 as required by the facility's permit. The test demonstrated 90% or greater removal efficiency for all detected VOCs.
63.a.iii: The volumetric flow rate of gas streams into the soil vapor extraction unit was measured and found to be 78 square cubic feet per minute (scfm).

63.c.i: The date of sampling, type of air pollution control in use and the name of the company preforming the laboratory analysis was recorded.
63.c.ii: The concentration of the VOC at the inlet of the SVEU was recorded.
63.c.iii: The emission rate of the VOC exiting the SVEU was recorded.
63.c.iv: The VOC efficiency for the SVEU was recorded.

63.f: The performance test was conducted on November 20, 2024, and submitted to MCAQD for review on December 30, 2024; therefore, the results of the test were submitted within 45-days of the test being performed as specified in the facility's permit.</td></tr>
