Item  3: The temperature is monitored. The logs are attached (Chart Recorder).  Please note, thermocouples are received from the manufacturer already calibrated for the temperature span required based on the flare’s specifications so there is no additional calibration required once acquired and installed. In the landfill industry, thermocouples are considered consumable equipment and are replaced when they fail. This is usually indicated when the temperature values of the recorded flare data start to fall outside of the typical range usually resulting in a flare shutdown. The data is reviewed with this in mind so that issues can be quickly identified. Additionally, the flare is also inspected monthly to ensure all components are operating within parameters.</td><td>12/20/2024</td><td>01/09/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Additional source records for the routine inspection of the facility conducted on September 16, 2024. See Inspection Report INSP201428 for further details.</td></tr>
