<tr><td>CRPT009394</td><td>F002622</td><td>Nammo Talley</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP002276</td><td>Nammo Defense Systems Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Notification</td><td>Proposed Bon Fire DOT Testing 1.8.25</td><td>12/19/2024</td><td>01/08/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Facility observed to have one day of proposed burning activities, with the activities planned for January 8, 2025. 

The facility calculated to have ~ 55 lbs of PM emissions, which exceeds the allowed 2 lbs of PM emissions under Rule 314 Section 320.8 due to Wednesday, January 8, 2025, being a forecasted PM10 No Burn Day, as indicated by the Arizona Department of Environmental Quality (ADEQ) air quality forecast. 

The facility was informed of the possible restricted burn period on Wednesday, January 8, 2025, during a phone call on Friday, January 3, 2025. 

If the planned activities continued as indicated a non-compliance would be issued. 

An email was also sent to the facility contact, informing them of the regulations and possible non-compliance. Environmental Project Engineer Katie Blatchford informed me that the she would use the resources in the email to determine if the test would need to be canceled or rescheduled. 

On January 6, 2025, Ms. Blatchford informed via email that the test would be rescheduled to Thursday, January 9, 2025. An additional compliance report was going to be submitted representing the notification of the rescheduled test date. 

This compliance report is being rejected due to the data provided demonstrating that the PM emissions for January 8, 2025, were anticipated to be exceeded on a possible PM10 No Burn Day. 

On January 8, 2025, a PM10 High Pollution Advisory was declared as indicated by the ADEQ air quality forecast. 

I received an email from Ms. Blatchford on January 8, 2025, indicating that the described test would be rescheduled to February 2025.

No compliance issues were documented since the test is being rescheduled and was not conducted during a restricted burn period.</td></tr>
