<tr><td>CRPT009317</td><td>F003654</td><td>Ninety-First Avenue Renewable Biogas</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Production Site</td><td>CMP002313</td><td>Ninety-First Avenue Renewable Biogas LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Ambient H2S Monitoring Report for monitoring conducted on October 30, 2024</td><td>12/05/2024</td><td>02/10/2025</td><td>No-Revision Requested</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Reviewal of the Ambient H2S Monitoring Report as required by Permit Condition 7.a.i.

The facility was issued the permit on October 02, 2024 and testing occurred on October 30, 2024 (within the 90 day timeframe). The facility did not submit this report until December 05, 2024 which is past the required 30 day deadline following the completion of the demonstration. A Notice of Non-Compliance was originally issued for this matter, however it has now been rescinded due to discussion with the source and my supervisor, please refer to Inspection Report INSP206338.

Additionally, the location of the H2S testing is farther than the requirements listed within the permit, "the compliance demonstration shall be performed at a location representing the nearest occupied place beyond the premises on which the source of H2S is located.”. The calibration incoming gas log also listed that it was out of calibration. Source clarified on February 13, 2025 the calibration status of the meter and confirmed that it was in calibration on October 30, 2024 for the testing that was conducted. 

Source has been notified that a retest of H2S will be required to demonstrate compliance. Deadline to submit the retest compliance report was originally set to close of business March 14, 2025, however it has been extended at the request of the source to now be the close of business April 14, 2025.</td></tr>
