<tr><td>CRPT009286</td><td>F000079</td><td>Glendale Mun Sanitary Landfill/Fld Oper</td><td>Title V</td><td>Landfills</td><td>CMP000808</td><td>City of Glendale</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>May 2024-October 2024 Glendale Landfill Semi-Annual Report and Semi-Annual Certification (Appendix H)</td><td>11/27/2024</td><td>12/24/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This Semiannual Monitoring Report for Title V Compliance Certification was originally submitted on November 27, 2024. I requested the facility submit a revision to this compliance report as it seemed to be missing an attachment. I spoke with Ernie Ruiz regarding this and he was able to upload the correct documentation.

Permit condition 21.b
No deviations were recorded during the reporting period.

Permit condition 21.b.i Visible emissions observations
Appendix A includes all required visible emissions observations per Permit Condition 20.b.i. No visible emissions were observed during this time period. They conduct weekly inspections.

Permit Condition 21.b.ii Odor Log
Appendix E states there were no complaints during this period.

Permit Condition 21.b.iii Solvent Cleaning
Appendix B details their cleaning solvent usage per Permit Condition 20.b.iii. VOC contents are recorded for these materials. Safety Data Sheets were included. They used NAPA Mac’s 4800 Non-Chlorinated Brake Cleaner and Safety-Kleen Premium Solvent. No testing related to solvent cleaning, was performed during this period.

Permit Condition 21.b.iv H2S Monitoring Report
The facility confirmed that since there were no odor complaints filed, they did not require H2S Testing to be performed.

Permit Condition 21.b.v Maximum Potential Waste Acceptance Rate Exceedance
The facility confirmed that they did not exceed maximum potential waste acceptance rate.

Permit Condition 21.b.vi Value and length of time for exceedance of applicable parameters
Various wells did have a positive pressure (listed in Appendix C)
According to the report, the compliant readings were recorded for all extraction wells on September 13 and 23, 2024 (60 days from initial exceedance). The Root Cause Analysis (RCA) forms are included in Appendix C.  
The facility confirmed that there were no exceedances of any other applicable parameters during this period

Permit Condition 21.b.vii Description and duration of all periods when the gas stream is diverted from the control device through a bypass line or the indication of bypass flow.
The facility confirmed there were no instances when the gas stream was diverted from the control device. 

Permit Condition 21.b.viii Description and duration of all periods when the control device was not operating for a period exceeding 1 hour and length of time the control device was not operating.
The facility confirmed this information is kept in Appendix G.

Permit Condition 21.b.ix All periods when the collection system was not operating in excess of 5 days.
The facility confirmed no instances occurred where the collection system was not operating more than 5 days during the reporting period.

Permit Condition 21.b.x Methane Exceedance Information 
The facility noted two locations with exceedances from the Second Quarter 2024 and no exceedances from the Third Quarter 2024. This information is seen in Appendix D.

Permit Condition xi 21.b.xi; The date of installation and the location of each well or collection system expansion added.
The facility confirmed there were no new wells installed during this time period. This is confirmed in Appendix F.

Permit Condition 21.b.xii; Fuel flow rate and the heating value of the fuel.
The facility confirmed that there is no bypass in the system and no alternative fuel is used to power the system. They state 100% of the landfill gas is sent to the enclosed flare for destruction. This information is provided in Appendix G

Permit Condition 21.b.xiii; The operating limits provided in this Permit, and any deviations from these limits.  
No deviations were reported.

Permit Condition 21.b.xiv; Any problems or errors suspected with the fuel rate meters.
The facility stated there were no issues with the fuel rate meters during the reporting period. 

No compliance issues were observed for this Semiannual Monitoring Report.

See inspection report INSP204809 for compliance status.</td></tr>
