<tr><td>CRPT009151</td><td>F000013</td><td>Salt River Project - Santan Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Semiannual Compliance Certification and Title V Monitoring Report. Reporting Period: April 1, 2024 through September 30, 2024. Due October 30, 2024.</td><td>10/30/2024</td><td>11/01/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semiannual Compliance Certification and Monitoring Report for April 1, 2024, through September 30, 2024.

Report received by October 30, 2024, due date.

Facility reported deviations from the permit:

Permit Condition 18.a.iii., Table 3 was documented intermittent compliance for exceeding 1-hour rolling average CO startup emission limit for one hour on Unit S-6A on May 21, 2024. The time of the exceedance was from 11:00 to 11:59. Maricopa County Air Quality Department (MCAQD) issued a Notice of Non-Compliance for this event as part of the non-routine inspection INSP198184. 
The 72-hour notification report (CRPT008332) includes the corrective actions that were taken. Corrective actions included the review of startup procedures and temperature match , assess possible temperature-match permissive modifications, and updating default/initial temperature match setpoint. CO emissions were returned to normal, compliant levels immediately after detection of the issue. 

Permit Condition 19.g.v.1.e,f and 19.g.v.2 was documented as intermittent compliance for foreign matter being found inside the aboveground storage tank (AST) spill containment receptacle (SCR) during a routine air quality inspection conducted by MCAQD on August 28, 2024. MCAQD issued a Notice of Non-Compliance as part of the routine inspection INSP200276. 
Corrective actions were taken upon discovery of the foreign matter. The foreign matter was properly removed and disposed of properly. To prevent future recurrences, all operators who conduct the fuel delivery inspections will be re-trained on how to properly perform a delivery inspection. 

No other deviations were reported in this semiannual period. MCAQD did not issue any additional non-compliance during this period.

All requirements of Permit Condition 21.a. are included in this report.

No noncompliant usage, operations, or visible emissions reported.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT009152</td><td>F000013</td><td>Salt River Project - Santan Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Semiannual Part 60 Excess Emissions and Monitoring System Performance Report. Reporting Period April 1, 2024 through September 30, 2024. Due October 30, 2024</td><td>10/30/2024</td><td>10/31/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semiannual Part 60 Excess Emissions and Monitoring System Performance Report for April 1, 2024 - September 30, 2024.

Report received by October 30, 2024, deadline.

All reporting requirements included in compliance report submittal.

This report satisfies the reporting requirements of the applicable subpart of 40 CFR Part 60 as specified by Permit Condition 21.d.i.

The CEMS Performance Summary and Excess Emissions Reports for each affected unit are included in the compliance report. There were no instances of excess emissions of 1 percent or more of the total operating time or CEMS downtime of 5 percent or more of the total operating time. 

No compliance issues noted.

Reference inspection report INSP203208 for more details.</td></tr>
