<tr><td>CRPT009110</td><td>F002126</td><td>Arlington Valley</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP000343</td><td>Arlington Valley LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Attached is the 2nd Semi-Annual Tile V certification and CEMS Excess Emissions and Monitoring Downtime Report. Each report has its own respective certification page.</td><td>10/23/2024</td><td>03/18/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The review of CRPT009110 is for Arlington Valley’s 2nd Semi-Annual Tile V certification and CEMS Excess Emissions and Monitoring Downtime Report. Each report has its own respective certification page. The report is for the time operating period of April 1, 2024 through September 30, 2024. This was submitted on October 23, 2024 prior to the due date of October 30, 2024. The permit used for this review is P0011934 which was in effect until their new permit became effective on January 30, 2025.

The reporting requirements are listed by the facility as follows:

Permit Condition 21.b.i (Reporting Requirements) — Duct Burner Nitrogen Oxides For each 24-hour period (beginning at 12:01 AM and ending at 12:00 midnight and during which natural gas was combusted in the duct burner for the entire 24 hours) the following information is provided: During this compliance period there was one day on July 23rd which natural gas was combusted in the duct burners for an entire 24-hour period. Included in Attachment 2 are daily emission tables from the data acquisition handling system (DAHS) listing hourly NOX emission rates (lb/MW-hr) demonstrating partial operations each calendar day during the compliance period. All records were kept properly.

Permit Condition 21.b.iii (Reporting Requirements) — Operating Conditions During CEMS Downtime (NOX and CO): Compliant

Permit Condition 21.b.iv (Reporting Requirements) — NOX and CO Compliance Statement: Compliant
The status of compliance for each permit condition is stated in the Semi-Annual Compliance Certification and Monitoring Report enclosed in Attachment 1. 

Permit Condition 21.b.v (Reporting Requirements) — Semi-Annual Excess Emissions and Downtime Report (NOX): Compliant. There were no excess emissions this compliance period and CEMS downtime for the reporting period was less than 5 percent.

Permit Condition 21.d.i and 21.d.ii (Reporting Requirements) — Semi-Annual Compliance Certification and Monitoring Report: Compliant

Permit Condition 21.d.iii (Reporting Requirements) — Hours of operation for the period is summarized on the report. Compliant

Permit Condition 21.d.iv (Reporting Requirements) - Opacity Readings: Compliant

Permit Condition 21.d.v (Reporting Requirements) — Odor Complaints: None received.

Permit Condition 21d.vi (Reporting Requirements) — Fuel Supplier Certifications: No additional diesel fuel oil was delivered.

Permit Condition 21.d.vii (Reporting Requirements) — Turbo Mister Operations: The Turbo Mister did not operate.                           

Permit Condition 21.d.viii and ix (Reporting Requirements) – Other Reports: Compliant

Attachment 1 – Title V Semi-Annual Compliance Certification Form
Deviations listed:
- Permit Condition 4.a – “Weekly visible emission records for the Facility were not documented for a few weeks from the year to date back to 2023. This was discovered during the Title V annual inspection review process and has since been corrected. No visible emissions were noted during this compliance period.”

Attachment 2 – Nitrogen Oxide Emissions Rate (lb/MW-hr) Reports (Unit 1&2)
- All emissions recorded for both T1 and T2 appear to be within compliance standards for Table 2 of P0011934.

Attachment 3 – Nitrogen Oxide Emissions Rate (lb/MW-hr) Start-up/Shutdown Reports (Unit 1&2) 
- All emissions recorded for both T1 and T2 appear to be within compliance standards for Table 3 of P0011934.

Attachment 4 – Semi-Annual Excess Emissions and Monitor Downtime Reports (Units 1&2)
- CEMS Downtime and Excess Emissions Reporting appear to be within regulatory standards.

No additional compliance issues were noted.</td></tr>
