<tr><td>CRPT009104</td><td>F001684</td><td>Fisher Sand & Gravel</td><td>Minor</td><td>Asphalt Plant, Portable</td><td>CMP001368</td><td>Fisher Sand & Gravel Co</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Attached is a letter of findings that have been repaired.  Also attached is a general analyzer test performed on the plant after the corrections were made.  Please let us know if you have any questions or concerns.
Chris Smith - csmith@fisherind.com / Greg Groneberg - ggroneberg@fisherind.com / Todd Mack  tmack@fisherind.com / Cory Schoonover - cschoonover@fisherind.com</td><td>10/23/2024</td><td>10/25/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Performance testing conducted on August 1, 2024 at the El Mirage HMA plant. The specific issue encompasses CO and VOC emission levels caused by a change in the combustion zone of the drum dryer. Even though the combustion zone flighting was in great working shape, the drum gained some circumference allowing the spacing on the combustion flights to separate further during production than manufacturer’s tolerance. This took multiple parties to help identify the issue, as soon as the diagnosis was made, the parts were procured to correct the issue and were installed September 24, 2024. 

Stack retest scheduled for November 7, 2024.</td></tr>
