<tr><td>CRPT008968</td><td>F045562</td><td>Soil and Groundwater Remediation System</td><td>Minor</td><td>Groundwater/Soil Remediation</td><td>CMP023552</td><td>Vantage Commercial Properties Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Soil Vapor Extraction Unit Test Report</td><td>Compliance Sampling Results Report for August 22, 2024</td><td>09/22/2024</td><td>09/24/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>SVE sampling conducted on 08/22/24. Report received on 09/22/24. Advance notification provided.

Performance testing conducted as required by permit condition 8. Test was completed after replacement of the primary activated carbon with fresh carbon in the activated carbon system, treating emissions from the groundwater air stripper in the DPES system. This test is the fifth test out of required 6 monthly performance tests.

Vapor samples collected included:
Catalytic oxidizer inlet
Catalytic oxidizer outlet (stack)
Air stripper outlet
Primary carbon canister outlet
Carbon system stack

Based on Total Petroleum Hydrocarbon concentration of 4,480 ug/liter and a flow of 248 cfm into the catalytic oxidizer, the total hydrocarbon mass being treated was 106.6 lb/day. The outlet stack concentration was &lt;100 ug/liter, resulting in a hydrocarbon destruction efficiency of the catalytic oxidizer being greater than 98%. This is greater than the minimum of limit of 95%. The emissions rate is less than 2.22 lb/day of hydrocarbons. No VOCs were detected above laboratory detection limits in the catalytic oxidizer stack.

Submitted report included all required information.

Next performance testing is scheduled for September 30, 2024.

Permit expiration: 09/15/27
Annual administrative fees: 09/04/24
Routine inspection: 12/27/23

Performance test report and results accepted.

