<tr><td>CRPT007592</td><td>F003399</td><td>Hydro Extrusion USA</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Metal Production - Foundry, Forge, etc</td><td>CMP001686</td><td>Hydro Extrusion USA LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Semi-Annual Single HAP Emissions Report for the period July 1, 2023 through December 31, 2023, due date January 30, 2024.</td><td>09/13/2024</td><td>09/16/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semi annual single HAP emissions report for July 1, 2023, through December 31,2023. Due on or before January 1, 2024, and received on September 13, 2024.

All hazardous air pollutants were under emission limits.

Per permit condition 3:
The Permittee shall file semiannual reports twice a year with the Department through the AQD Online Portal, Attn:  Compliance Manager.  Each report shall contain the rolling 12-month single HAP emissions. Each semiannual reporting period shall cover the 6 month period of Jan 01 – Jun 30 and of Jul 01 – Dec 31.  Each report shall be filed by the end of the month following the reporting period (Jul 31 and Jan 31).  

Per Rule 241, Section 305:
RACT REQUIRED: An applicant for a permit or permit revision subject to Rules 210, 220, or 230 of these rules shall implement RACT for each pollutant emitted for which the increase in potential to emit is less than the BACT thresholds set forth in Section 304 of this rule. 

Email sent to source on 09/13/24 inquiring about semi annual excess emission/summary report for February 2024. Response from source received on 09/13/24. Per source, the semi annual single HAP emissions report report was uploaded into the AQD Online Portal on 01/16/24 but was not certified. To prevent future occurrences of non-certified reports, the source has updated internal procedures to require retention of both submittals and confirmation of submission to be verified prior to deadlines. 

Refer to INSP201526.

