Annual administrative fees received: 09/06/24
Routine inspection conducted: 01/05/23, notice of non-compliance issued for failure to submit O&M Plan for dust collection system
Semi annual single HAP emissions report received: 07/30/24
Performance testing report received: 04/12/24, review in progress
Dust Control Plan received: 12/20/23
Operations & Maintenance Plan received: 12/20/23</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT007593</td><td>F003399</td><td>Hydro Extrusion USA</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Metal Production - Foundry, Forge, etc</td><td>CMP001686</td><td>Hydro Extrusion USA LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Semi-Annual Excess Emission / Summary Report for period July 1, 2023, through December 31, 2023 - Due February 29, 2024</td><td>09/13/2024</td><td>09/18/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semi annual excess emission/summary report received on 09/13/24 per permit condition 16b.

Reporting period July 1, 2023, through December 31, 2023. Report due on or before 02/29/24.

Per permit condition 16b this report is to be submitted bi-annually. The most recent report was submitted on 08/26/24 and was accepted. Previous reports were submitted on 08/11/23, 02/15/23, 07/22/22, 01/26/22, 07/23/21, and so forth. No semi annual excess emission/summary report in between the most recent submittal on 08/26/24 and the previous submittal on 08/11/23.

Email sent to source on 09/13/24 inquiring about semi annual excess emission/summary report for February 2024. Response from source received on 09/13/24. Per source, the report was uploaded into the AQD Online Portal on 01/16/24 but was not certified. To prevent future occurrences of non-certified reports, the source has updated internal procedures to require retention of both submittals and confirmation of submission to be verified prior to deadlines.

Per email response from source, none of following occurred during reporting period of June 2023 through December 2023. 

1.	An excursion of a compliant process or operating parameter value or range.  
Hydro did not have an excursion of a compliant process or operating parameter value or range. Attachment B indicates no excess emission occurred during the reporting period.
2.	A malfunction.   
Hydro included non-monitoring equipment (Melter and Holder) malfunctions in Attachment C and E for the reporting period. None of the malfunctions noted caused or had the potential to cause an exceedance of an applicable standard. 
3.	Melting furnace, holding furnace, or in-line fluxer was not operated according to the requirements of these conditions.
Hydro operated the melting furnace, holding furnace, and in-line fluxer in accordance with requirements of [permit] conditions. Compliance report certifications are included in Attachment A for the reporting period. 

Report accepted.

Permit expiration: 09/30/28
Annual administrative fees received: 09/06/24
