<tr><td>CRPT008912</td><td>F004173</td><td>Air Transport Components</td><td>Minor</td><td>Aerospace Component Manufacturing</td><td>CMP000141</td><td>Air Transport Components LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>2023/2024 - Spread sheet containing expirables , Rolling 12month VOC , EPA 6h training certs , Spray gun check list , Paint both Filter spec,</td><td>09/10/2024</td><td>09/27/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>In accordance with Part 12 of the facility's permit, the following was provided to the Maricopa County Air Quality Department:

Part 6.b of the facility's permit required that all spray booths, preparation stations and mobile enclosures are fitted with a type of filter technology that is demonstrated to achieve at least 98%  capture of paint overspray. The document provided by the facility indicates that the filters being used have a 98% efficiency rating, which complies with the permit condition.

Part 11 of the facility's permit, requires that individuals conducting spray coating must complete 6H training which adheres to part 11.b of the permit, within 180-days of hire. The facility provided documentation that the following individuals completed the required training on November 1, 2023:

Adrian Garibay 
Frank M Armenta
James Adams 

Part 3 of the facility's permit limits daily VOC emissions to 15.0 lbs. and 12-month rolling VOC emissions to 2.0 tons. These emissions are required to be calculated monthly by the end of the following month and this record is required to be kept on site for inspection or submittal upon request. The facility's permit does not require these emission totals to be submitted for review at any regular interval.

The facility provided a copy of their Spray Gun Checklist. Although this document demonstrates good working practices, its submittal is not required by the facility's permit.</td></tr>
