<tr><td>CRPT008834</td><td>F041851</td><td>MC#4</td><td>Minor</td><td>Crushing and Screening, Portable</td><td>CMP018050</td><td>Superstition Crushing LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Portable Equipment Move Notice</td><td>Portable Source Move Notice  Facility Name - MC#4 - Facility ID  F041851 - 4-9-22</td><td>08/27/2024</td><td>08/28/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Mark Ledlow, Director of Safety and Compliance with Superstition Crushing LLC submitted this Portable Equipment Move Notice that the portable generator (#305) will be moved from a sand and gravel plant off of Camelback Rd near Buckeye to their storage yard at 3914 E Presidio St in Mesa.  This generator will not be used again by this company in Maricopa County.

*****INSPECTOR COMMENTS*****
Superstition Crushing operates multiple crushing and screening facilities. This one has generated emissions reduction credits by changing out engines. This facility has gone to line power and no longer uses engines. The important matter is removing the engines out of the area of non-attainment and having the required information listed below. 

Upon installation of the Tier 4 Final Engines, the Permittee shall permanently remove the following existing engines, from the nonattainment area or render the replaced equipment permanently disabled and dispose of in a manner that complies with all applicable local, state, and federal laws:

#305 – Cummins 750 kW (S/N: K060992120) Mfg. 2006 (1,006 BHP)
#319 – Caterpillar 3406 320 kW (S/N: 04JK00630) Mfg. 2004 (429 BHP)

b. The Permittee shall provide evidence of proper disposal or removal upon request from the Control Officer or from the permitted source using the ERCs as offsets. Evidence shall include at a minimum, the serial number and location of where or how the equipment was disposed or removed and the date of disposal or removal.

c. The Permittee shall not install or operate any engine that does not meet EPA Tier 4 final emission
standards.

------------------------------------------------------------------

13. Recordkeeping: The Permittee shall maintain the following records for a period of at least five years from the date of the records and make them available to the Control Officer upon request:

a. For each engine used to generate credits, provide all of the following:
i. Equipment manufacturer,
ii. Model number,
iii. The model year,
iv. Equipment category, and
v. A description of the equipment including serial number

b. Information on sources used to obtain family or test group, fuel capacities, and emission rates of each engine when used to calculate emission reduction credits.

c. The date each engine was:
i. Added to the inventory.
ii. Repowered.
iii. Removed from the inventory

d. Records of proper disposal or removal of the existing diesel engine

e. Operational Records:
i. Monthly: For each Tier 4F engine used to generate ERCs, the Permittee shall record a description of all:
-Maintenance;
-Repairs; and
-Hours of operation.</td></tr>
