<tr><td>CRPT008735</td><td>F001186</td><td>91st Ave Wastewater Treatment Plant</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Wastewater Treatment Plants and Lift Stations</td><td>CMP000821</td><td>City of Phoenix</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Semi Annual SOx and Digester Gas report for the period Jan-Jun 2024.   Due 8/14/2024</td><td>08/07/2024</td><td>11/01/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Per PC 3, the facility is required to submit a semiannual report containing the following information for the period of January 2024 - June 2024:

a. Monthly and 12-month rolling total emissions of SOX during the preceding 12 months, calculated in accordance with Permit Condition 2;
b. Results of the digester gas sulfur tests for each city business day;
c. Daily, monthly and 12 month rolling total volume of digester gas (MMscf) burned at the facility in each boiler and flare.
d. Verification, in accordance with Permit Condition 17.a.ii, that no diesel fuel exceeding 15 ppm sulfur content is burned in stationary equipment at the facility.
e. Monthly and 12 month rolling total number of times sodium bisulfite is loaded into the tank for each calendar month during the preceding 12 months.

After careful review, I determined compliance with the following items:

a. Monthly and 12-month rolling total SOx emissions recorded and reviewed. The rolling total emissions for every month were compliant. The highest month was May 2024 (June 2023 - May 2024) at 143,045 lbs; limit is 182,000 lbs/yr.

b. Sulfur tests were recorded for business day the tests were conducted. There were no fuel burning units that exceed the 800 ppmv permit limit.

c. Daily, monthly, and 12-month rolling total volume of digester gas in MMscf was recorded and reviewed for the time period requested. No 12-month rolling totals exceeded the 1400 MMscf permit limit.

d. The facility is in compliance with this condition.

e. Sodium bisulfite deliveries were recorded monthly and 12-month rolling totals were provided for each month in the time period requested.

The facility is in compliance with the semiannual reporting requirements per PC 3. They submitted the report within 45 days of the conclusion of the reporting period. They have met all of the conditions.

**No violations noted.

Refer to INSP203254.</td></tr>
