<tr><td>CRPT008643</td><td>F003392</td><td>Platypus Development</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Data Centers (&gt;100 MW)</td><td>CMP002547</td><td>Platypus Development LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>First Half of 2024 (January 1, 2024 to June 30, 2024) Bi-Annual Emissions Report due by July 30, 2024. All permit-required information is contained in the attached report.</td><td>07/30/2024</td><td>08/05/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Per condition 10 of the facility's permit, a bi-annual emissions report was submitted on July 30, 2024, for the periods between January 1, 2024 to June 30, 2024. This report was submitted no later than 30-days after the end of the reporting period and contained the following information:

 i.	Hours of operation of each engine.
ii.	The maximum output kW load placed on the generators during each run.
iii.	For each run: The total time the engine is operated and the amount of time at which the engine exhaust is less than 572 ºF.
iv.	The emission factors and 12-month rolling total emissions of NOx and CO.

The facility reported that Group 1, 2, 3, 4 and fire pump engines emitted a total of 0.05 tons of NOx during this period and Group 5, 6 and 7 emitted a total of 0.01 tons of NOx during this period.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT008679</td><td>F000014</td><td>Salt River Project - Agua Fria Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Salt River Project Agricultural Improvement and Power District (SRP) operates the Agua Fria Generating Station located at 7302 West Northern Avenue, Glendale, AZ 85303 in accordance with Title V Permit No. P0011528 (Permit).  SRP is submitting the enclosed Semiannual Monitoring Report and Compliance Certification to satisfy Permit Condition 51.a and 51.b for the reporting period from January 1, 2024 through June 30, 2024.  

Please contact Sheena Alvarado at (602) 236-7616 or Jenn Paskash at (602) 236-4746 if you have any questions.</td><td>07/30/2024</td><td>09/17/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>I reviewed the Semiannual Compliance Certification and Monitoring report for the reporting period of January 1, 2024 to June 30, 2024.

The report should include, at a minimum, the following:

(1) Hours of the operation for each steam unit and each combustion turbine
(2) Dates on which opacity reading were taken, the test method used, and the observed
opacity
(3) Fuel supplier certification of sulfur content for all fuel oil delivered during reporting
period
(4) A copy of the log of neighbor complaints of odors or air pollution, and the results of
investigations performed in response to odor or air pollution complaints and any
corrective actions taken
(5) Whether any gaseous fuels other than pipeline natural gas were used
(6) Any deviations from the approved Dust Control Plan
(7) Emissions calculations necessary to determine compliance with the facility-wide HAPs
emission limits in Permit Condition 18.d
(8) Year-to-date gross energy output or net energy output sold to an electric grid and the
potential electric output of Unit 7 and Unit 8
(9) The identification of each term or condition of the permit that is the basis of the certification
(10) The compliance status
(11) Whether compliance was continuous or intermittent
(12) The method(s) used for determining the compliance status, currently and over the reporting
period
(13) Other facts the Control Officer may require to determine compliance status

The format of the report satisfies items (9), (10), (11), (12), and (13) from the list above. Each permit condition was listed with statements demonstrating the facility was In Compliance and denoting that the compliance status was continuous or intermittent. The method used for determining the compliance status was also detailed for each permit condition. The facility reported a deviation from PC 32.a, 33.a, and 49.b that details an instance where a new employee did not observe loading of gasoline on March 5, 2024. 

Item (1) - The report details the hours of operation for each Unit during this sixth-month period.

Item (2) - The report states there were no opacity readings were required to be taken during the reporting period.

Item (3) - The report indicates the there was no Fuel Oil was delivered to AFGS during the reporting period.

Item (4) - The report states there were no odor log entries during the reporting period. 

Item (5) - The report states the facility only uses pipeline quality natural gas. 

Item (6) - Deviations from the Dust Control Plan were not detailed.

Item (7) - The emissions calculations were provided for facility-wide HAPs.

Item (8) - The year-to-date gross energy output or net energy output sold to an electric grid and the potential output of Unit 7 and Unit 8 were provided.

The report was submitted on the second to last day of the month following the reporting period, which is within the appropriate time frame.

No compliance issues were noted.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT008680</td><td>F000014</td><td>Salt River Project - Agua Fria Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Salt River Project Agricultural Improvement and Power District (SRP) operates the Agua Fria Generating Station located at 7302 West Northern Avenue, Glendale, AZ 85303 in accordance with Title V Permit No. P0011528 (Permit).  SRP is submitting the enclosed Part 60 Excess Emissions and Monitoring Systems Performance Report (Part 60 Report) to satisfy the requirements of Title 40 Code of Federal Regulations (CFR) Part 60 Subparts A and KKKK as specified by the Permit.   This Part 60 Report covers the reporting period from January 1, 2024 through June 30, 2024.  

