<tr><td>CRPT008631</td><td>F002681</td><td>SFPP-Phoenix Terminal</td><td>Title V</td><td>Petroleum Products Bulk Storage/Handling</td><td>CMP002921</td><td>SFPP LP</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Notification</td><td>PX-52 & PX-168 Inspection Report</td><td>07/30/2024</td><td>10/31/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>EFR Seal Gap Inspection report for tank inspections conducted on 18-Jul-24. Notification was submitted in a timely manner on 30-Jul-24. Tanks PX-52, PX-168 were inspected and found to be in compliance.

No issues of non-compliance observed during review of compliance report.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT008661</td><td>F002681</td><td>SFPP-Phoenix Terminal</td><td>Title V</td><td>Petroleum Products Bulk Storage/Handling</td><td>CMP002921</td><td>SFPP LP</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>1H 2024 Title V Semiannual & GDGACT Reports</td><td>07/30/2024</td><td>10/16/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Compliance report is the Semiannual Compliance Certification and Monitoring Report for the period of 01-Jan-24 to 30-Jun-24. Compliance report was submitted in a timely manner on 30-Jul-24.

Per the Compliance Certification Report, two deviations were recorded during the reporting period. Specifically, on 16-May-24, a hydrocarbon smell was noted during a water draw on tank P-6. The pressure test was completed on 20-May-24 and it was determined that the hose needed to be replaced. Additionally, on 31-Jan-24, the data recorder unit for temperature trending malfunctioned. The unit was diagnosed and replaced the same day. The deviations did not require a compliance report submission as they did not result in excess emissions for the facility. All other permit conditions were noted as being in continuous compliance during the reporting period.

The semi-annual monitoring report was found to be in compliance with Permit Condition 37.f. I reviewed the monitoring report, with notes as follows:

- i: Monthly inspections conducted in compliance with no deviations noted.
- ii: John Zink Oxidizer operated in bypass mode due to the saturator not being installed. A deviation was noted due to the temperature trending data recorder malfunctioning on 31-Jan-24. The issue was solved the same day.
- iii: CAU-1 is currently out of operation. Emissions were routed through the John Zink Oxidizer for the reporting period.
- 37.f.iv: SVE units did not operate during the reporting period.
- v: No issues observed with the "card access" system.
- vi: No visible emissions observed during the reporting period.
- vii: No odor complaints observed during the reporting period.
- viii: VOC list reviewed and in compliance.
- ix: No issues observed during walk-around inspections.
- x: No issues observed with architectural coatings.
- xi: No external blasting occurred during the reporting period. 
- xii: No deviations in dust-control requirements.
- xiii: 12-month rolling VOC emissions totaled 69.26tons.
- xiv/xvi: Two deviations noted, on 31-Jan-24 and 16-May-24.
- xvii: Excess emissions reports submitted in a timely manner.

The Subpart BBBBBB Report met all requirements of 40 CFR Subpart 63. The report notes 2hours of excess emissions during the reporting period due to control equipment problems. 

Overall the compliance report was found to be in compliance with no issues observed.</td></tr>
