<tr><td>CRPT008653</td><td>F000041</td><td>APS Ocotillo Power Plant</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP003677</td><td>Arizona Public Service Company</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Test Report</td><td>Submitting 2024 APS Ocotillo Stack Test reports for units GT4 and GT6. A cover letter and the applicable MCAQD Performance Test Submittal forms are also included.</td><td>07/26/2024</td><td>12/20/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT008650</td><td>F000192</td><td>Marlam Industries</td><td>Title V</td><td>Plastics, Polymers, Fiberglass, Foam</td><td>CMP002105</td><td>Marlam Industries Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>This is the semi-annual monitoring report for the period January 1, 2024 through June 30, 2024.</td><td>07/26/2024</td><td>11/14/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Per PC 23, the facility is required to submit a semiannual report for the period of January 1 - June 30 and July 1 - December 31; this semiannual report was for the period of January 1, 2024 through June 30, 2024.

There are 11 items listed under PC 23 that detail what should be included or addressed in this report.

After careful review, I determined compliance for each of the 11 items items in PC 23.a.i - 23.a.xii. The facility provided all the statements or data required from this section.

The facility's highest reported 12-month rolling total VOC emissions was 2.30 tons; limit is 95 tons. The facility's metrics met all other HAP emissions limits as listed in MACT 6W.

The facility also submitted the compliance certification detailing the following information: 
i. The identification of each term or condition of the permit that is the basis of the certification;  
ii.The compliance status;  
iii. Whether compliance was continuous or intermittent;  
iv. The method(s) used for determining the compliance status, currently and over the reporting period; and  Other facts the Control Officer may require to determine compliance status.
 
The facility is in compliance with the semiannual reporting requirements per PC 23.b. They submitted the report within 30 days of the conclusion of the reporting period. They have met all of the conditions.

**No violations noted.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT008641</td><td>F000015</td><td>Salt River Project - Kyrene Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Test Report</td><td>Annual RATA and Compliance Test Reports for Unit K-7, due July 26.</td><td>07/25/2024</td><td>01/03/2025</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT008654</td><td>F000397</td><td>Exponent</td><td>Minor</td><td>Gasoline Non-resale</td><td>CMP001308</td><td>Exponent of Delaware Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Notification</td><td>The Arizona Department of Environmental Quality’s Air Quality Forecast webpage indicates that a high pollution advisory and restricted burn period has been issued for today, 7/25/2024.  A test, detailed below, is scheduled for today falls under the ‘shall approve’ portions of Maricopa County Rule 314 pertaining to safety testing related to DOT/DOD/commercial/other requirements (Sections 320/321, subsections 7 & 8). 

Exponent intends to conduct burn velocity testing to characterize gaseous VOC blends for application under ANSI/ASHRAE Standard 34-2001.  Each test will burn less than 2 grams of VOC and up to 15 tests will be conducted for a total of daily fuel mass of 20 grams (0.04409 pounds).  

Burning of the gaseous VOC samples is not expected to emit any particulate. Additionally, the total fuel mass (0.04409 pounds; 20 grams) for the series of tests is less that the 2lb, which could not conceivably generate more than 2lbs of particulate during testing.</td><td>07/25/2024</td><td>08/08/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Facility Contact/Senior Environmental Health & Safety Specialist - James Busch submitted via email a request to conduct burn velocity testing to characterize gaseous VOC samples on a High Pollution Advisory Day. The email request was received on July 25, 2024, at 12:13 p.m., a High Pollution Advisory (HPA) Day was declared for the proposed date of testing (July 25, 2024) for Ozone. 

Testing conducted on a HPA Day must emit less than 2 pounds of particulate matter.

Mr. Busch informed in this email that the testing would generate less than 2 pounds of particulate matter, values provided anticipated 0.04409 pounds of particulate matter. As this value provided falls within the allowable limit, the testing was approved on July 25, 2024 at 12:48 p.m.

All requirements in Maricopa County Air Pollution Regulations Rule 314 § 320 have been satisfied and will result in a compliant report.</td></tr>
