-- Single non-fugitve HAP (HTF): 2.27tons (limit: 15tons)
PC 11.a.ii: No deviations noted during the reporting period
PC 11.a.iii: Per the report, the CEMS system has had numerous difficulties since the annual test in Mar-24. MCAQD Performance Testing group has been in close contact regarding the issues, and contingent measures have been put in place to ensure compliance while options are being explored for updating/replacing the CEMS system.
PC 11.a.iv: 2512 ball joint leaks reported, grade 1/2/3, with 1058 ball joints repacked and 327 ball joints to be repacked.
PC 11.a.v: No HTF has been added to the system during the reporting period.
PC 11 a.vi: No HTF has been added to the system, with a total HTF loss of 0.005tons.
PC 11.b: Per report, facility was in continuous compliance for all permit conditions during the reporting period. However,Solana continues to work through the CEMS technical issues which may affect compliance status should the CEMS issues result in a Notice of Non-Compliance. See INSP187524 for more details.</td></tr>
