<tr><td>CRPT008530</td><td>F001759</td><td>Gila River Power Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>O&M Plan</td><td>Enclosed, please find the revised Operations and Maintenance (O&M) and Quality Assurance (QA) Plan for the Continuous Emission Monitoring Systems (CEMS) operated at the Gila River Power Station. Proposed changes include the following:

•	The O&M Plan has been edited to indicate that the air dryers have been removed from all 8 units.  The associated annual maintenance checklist has been updated to remove "replacing the Air Dryer Towers".   

     Note:  The Air Dryers were not part of the original CEMS installation. During the turbine upgrades from 2021 -2023, the dryers were added as part of a modification at 
     each CEMS Shack to support the analyzers installed to monitor the Gas Turbine Exhaust for tuning purposes.  Upon installation, the dryer assembly produced inconsistent plant air flow to the Stack O2 analyzers during span checks.  This inconsistent air flow made setting the instrument span during adjustments difficult.  
    Removing the air dryers resolves this issue without impacting CEMS regulatory compliance. 

•	Updates to the alternative performance specification for low-range Cylinder Gas Audits.
•	Minor grammar and formatting changes.

If you have any questions or need additional information, please contact David Camacho at (520) 482-9726 or Zach Harbin at (602) 236-5779.</td><td>07/05/2024</td><td>07/12/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>No changes to permitted equipment list needed.</td></tr>
