<tr><td>CRPT008497</td><td>F006370</td><td>Microsoft Corp - Olive Ave</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Data Centers (&gt;100 MW)</td><td>CMP003908</td><td>Microsoft Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Attn Compliance Offer: Synthetic Minor Reporting for Jan 2023 - Dec 2023 in accordance with permit condition 2. The attached is a calculation of annual emissions values based on 2023 permit NOx emissions values for PHX80 within facility F006370.</td><td>06/28/2024</td><td>06/28/2024</td><td>No-Revision Requested</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This is submitted to satisfy permit condition 2 of P0011357 & P0011407. Please ensure the facility submits a cover letter when submitting these Synthetic Minor Periodic Reports. Facility is required to submit this report by close of business 30 days following the reporting period, which would be January 30, 2024. Non-compliance has been noted. Also requesting a revision from the facility to submit the monthly data as well. Facility submitted Revision as CRPT008513.

See INSP198944 for full details.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT008496</td><td>F002622</td><td>Nammo Talley</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP002276</td><td>Nammo Defense Systems Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Notification</td><td>Proposed Testing Schedule for Open Burn/Open Detonation week of 7/1/24</td><td>06/28/2024</td><td>06/28/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Proposed date of testing is July 01, 2024 and July 02, 2024. Total PM Emissions are calculated to be 0.018 lbs. ADEQ Forecast does not currently list a High Pollution Advisory Alert nor Watch for either day as of today's forecast (June 28, 2024). As Total PM Emissions are less than two pounds per day of testing, the testing has been approved as it is in compliance with Maricopa County Air Pollution Rule 314 § 320.

No matters of non-compliance have been noted.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT008494</td><td>F001522</td><td>Mesquite Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP002166</td><td>Mesquite Power LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>72-hour excess emissions report for the Unit 2 June 26, 2024 NOx lb/hour and NOx ppm excess emissions event.</td><td>06/28/2024</td><td>07/05/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>72-hour Excess Emissions report reviewed and determined to be in compliance with the excess emissions reporting requirements detailed in Permit Condition 16.f.

Facility claimed the event occurred between the hours of 7 a.m. - 10:00 a.m. on June 26, 2024, with the facility dispatching a technician after an SCR NOx Fault alarm went off just after 8 AM. Environmental Scientist/Engineer D'Armond Chee notified the County of this event almost exactly 24-hours from when the facility noted the first alarm went off, on June 27, 2024. The 24-hour notification letter was attached via email.

The facility submitted the 72-hour notification letter attached to this Compliance Report in IMPACT on June 28, 2024, which is 48 hours after the event occurred and within 72 hours of the 24-hour notification letter submission.

The 72-hour notification letter contained all the information required in Permit Condition 16.f.ii. The two exceedances identified were a 1-hour average for NOx and a 3-hour average for NOx corrected to 15% O2 emanating from Unit 2 during normal operating conditions. The 1-hour average emissions for NOx were 22.8 lbs/hr; the permit limitation is 22.2 lbs/hr. The 3-hour average emissions for NOx were 2.8 ppm; the permit limitation is 2.5 ppm. The facility was found to be in non-compliance with the 1-hour average and 3-hour average corrected to 15% ppm NOx emissions standards listed in Permit Condition 18: Tables 18.2 and 18.3. The source of the non-compliance was determined to be an insufficient level of anhydrous ammonia to keep Unit 2 under the emissions limits. 

The facility listed three corrective actions that will be taken, highlighting additional training for control room operators after being notified of the first data alarm warning.

Corrective Action and Compliance Verification: Compliance has been verified as the required reports have been submitted and the facility has corrected the excess emissions.

See INSP199457 for additional details.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT008493</td><td>F000037</td><td>Palo Verde Nuclear Generating Station</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP003677</td><td>Arizona Public Service Company</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>UPDATE NOTICE OF HOUR METER FAILURE ON UNIT 3A EMERGENCY DIESEL GENERATOR (EDG)</td><td>06/27/2024</td><td>07/09/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Review of facility notification regarding an update to the repair schedule for a non-resetting totalizing hour meter for a facility emergency standby internal combustion engine. The facility's updated maintenance schedule was set for August 16, 2024 for unit repair.

Facility submitted the initial notification (CRPT008431) for the unit malfunction on June 14, 2024, with an expected repair scheduled for June 18, 2024.


Refer to INSP200542 for compliance determination.</td></tr>
