<tr><td>CRPT008342</td><td>F002622</td><td>Nammo Talley</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP002276</td><td>Nammo Defense Systems Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Notification</td><td>Notification for product testing (open detonation) for the week of 5/28/24</td><td>05/28/2024</td><td>05/30/2024</td><td>No</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Facility noted to have contacted Business Assistance prior to submitting compliance report. Facility observed to have two days of proposed burning activities, with the activities planned for May 30, 2024 observed to have 3.5 lbs of PM emissions, which exceeds the allowed 2 lbs of PM emissions under Rule 314 Section 320.8 due to Thursday, May 30, 2024 being a forecasted High Pollution Advisory day for Ozone, as indicated by the Arizona Department of Environmental Quality (ADEQ) air quality forecast. 

Facility was informed of the non-compliance if the planned activities continued as indicated. On May 29, 2024, a call was made and an email was sent to the facility contact, informing them of the regulations and possible non-compliance. Environmental Project Engineer Katie Blatchford informed me that the schedule would be difficult to adjust, but an effort would be made to contact their testing department to inquire on a modified testing event or postponed testing.

On May 29, 2024 Ms. Blatchford informed via email that the testing would be split into two day to keep the emissions below the 2lbs of PM emissions. An additional compliance report was requested to be submitted representing the new values that each testing day would produce in PM emissions. 

This compliance report is being rejected due to the data provided demonstrating that the PM emissions for May 30, 2024 were anticipated to be exceeded on a HPA day. Due to the attachment being listed as a "Trade Secret" document, I emailed Ms. Blatchford to determine if this was intentional or accidental and informed her that if it was purposeful then a process will need to be followed to make the information confidential. Ms. Blatchford confirmed that the information should not contain any confidential information and the trade secret status can be removed.

Please refer to Compliance Report CRPT008356 for further information on updated values.</td></tr>
