• Henceforth use the update forms for both Protocol and report submittals, the latter of which is located at 
www.maricopa.gov/DocumentCenter/View/93123
• This document is citing wrong Permit ID: which is P0011107


I verified compliance with the permit as follows:

[PC 7.c.i]
Maricopa County Waste Resources & Recycling Department submitted the
performance test report within 30 days (May 9, 2024) of conducting its quarterly SVE-Carbon Adsorption System performance testing (April 11, 2024).

The test was conducted by WSP Environment & Infrastructure Solutions, Inc. (Formerly Wood Environment & Infrastructure Solutions, Inc.) and represents the second quarterly test of the calendar year 2024.

[PC 7.c.ii][permit condition 5.h].
Actual volumetric flow rate of the gases exiting the carbon adsorption system not provided. Instead, standardized flow rate was provided, which I determined is apropos.

[PC 7.c.iii] 
Process temperature of (the process stream entering) the carbon adsorption system 102°F

[PC 7.c.iv] 
Influent concentration of VOCs observed to be 16.4 ppmv
Effluent concentration of VOCs observed to be 5.3 ppmv

[PC 7.c.v] 
The emission rate of VOCs and HAPs exiting the SVCU (lb/hr):
VOCs: 0.251 lb/hr
HAPs: 0.0642 lb/hr

[permit condition 5.f].
The combined VOC [4.4 ppmv] and HAP [7.8 ppmv] inlet concentrations [combined 12.2 ppmv] to the carbon adsorption system does not exceed 400 parts per million by volume (ppmv).

System VOC removal efficiency was 68%; and the outlet concentration was less than 10 ppmv demonstrating compliance with [permit condition 5.g].

[permit condition 1.a.]
12 month rolling total of VOCs for period of September 14, 2022 through April 11, 2024 observed to be lbs 85.1 pounds; under the limitation of 294 pounds.  
12 month rolling total of HAPs for period of September 14, 2022 through April 11, 2024 observed to be 400 pounds; under the limitation of 2,256 pounds</td></tr>
