<tr><td>CRPT008199</td><td>F001347</td><td>Southwest Regional Landfill</td><td>Title V</td><td>Landfills</td><td>CMP000180</td><td>Allied Waste Industries Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Semi-Annual report for Southwest Regional Landfill covering the reporting period from October 1, 2023 through March 31, 2024.</td><td>04/30/2024</td><td>10/18/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semi-Annual Report covering the reporting period from October 1, 2023 through March 31, 2024, submitted through the AQD Online Portal in a timely manner as required by Permit Condition 21.c.

Visible emission observations were conducted during the reporting period. No visible emissions were observed. Submitted as required by Permit Condition 21.c.i.

No odor complaints were received during the reporting period. Submitted in report as required by Permit Condition 21.c.ii.

No hydrogen sulfide monitoring was required during this reporting period. Submitted in report as required by Permit Condition 21.c.iii. 

An emissions report including all calculations and data used to estimate the semi-annual emissions in order to demonstrate compliance with emissions limitations required under Permit Condition 18. Submitted in report as required by Permit Condition 21.c.iv.

Value and length of time for exceedance of applicable parameters monitored under 40 CFR §60.756 are submitted in report as required by Permit Condition 21.c.v.

The GCCS does not have a bypass that allows Landfill Gas to be diverted from the control device. Statement provided in report as required by Permit Condition 21.c.vi.

A description and duration of all periods when the control device was not operating for a period exceeding 1 hour and length of time the control device was not operating was provided in the report as required by Permit Condition 21.c.vii.

Periods of when the collection system was not operating in excess of 5 days was provided in the report as required by Permit Condition 21.c.viii.

The location of each exceedance of the 500 part per million surface methane concentration, and the concentration recorded at each location for which an exceedance was recorded in the previous month is provided in the report as required by Permit Condition 21.c.ix.

The date of installation and the location of each well or collection system expansion added is provided in the report as required by Permit Condition 21.c.x.

Special Waste PCS Reporting and Liquid Waste Solidification Reporting is provided in the report as required by Permit Condition 21.c.xi.

Southwest Regional Landfill (SWRL) does not have a bypass line of the control system. No problems or errors with the flow meter was observed during the reporting period. The flow meter was calibrated on January 30, 2024. Provided in report as required by Permit Condition 21.c.xii. 

The semi-annual Startup Shutdown Malfunction (SSM) Plan report has been discontinued. Periods of downtimes of the flare are summarized in the report as required by Permit Condition 21.c.xiii.

The review of the facility’s semiannual monitoring report and TV compliance certification was pending Maricopa County Air Quality Department’s (MCAQD) delegation of authority of the federal plan for existing municipal solid waste landfills (40 CFR 62 Subpart OOO). The MCAQD state plan was officially approved by EPA in the summer of 2023.

The compliance determination for the semiannual monitoring report was based solely on the reporting requirements listed in the facility permit for the respective reporting period. 

The Environmental Protection agency (EPA) conducted a full compliance evaluation of the facility in April of 2022. On October 12, 2022, EPA delivered their Findings and Notice of Violation to Southwest Regional Landfill. The final compliance determination for the facility pending the close out of EPA’s pending case.</td></tr>
