<tr><td>CRPT008157</td><td>F000041</td><td>APS Ocotillo Power Plant</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP003677</td><td>Arizona Public Service Company</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>72-hour letter for APS Ocotillo GT6 Excess Emission report on April 19, 2024.</td><td>04/22/2024</td><td>04/29/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>•	Observed: The facility submitted CRPT008146 on April 19, 2024 and CRPT008157 on April 22, 2024 notifying an exceedance discovery and the exceedance report within 72 hours of discovery. 24- and 72- hour timelines have been followed according to permit condition (P0007177) 16.f. The permit condition and table that was observed to be in non-compliance was Permit Condition 18.b, Table 3: Hourly emission limits for Units GT3 – GT7 during periods when gas turbines operate in startup/shutdown (lb/hour, 1-hour average). The NOx hourly limit is 31.4 lbs. The facility had an exceedance where they were operating at 32.7 lbs/hour during the 18:00 hour on January 26, 2024. The excess emissions have been fixed and were discovered to have been from a system failure of the ammonia injection system. I confirmed this information with Lavonda Begay over the phone on April 29, 2024.
•	Corrective Action and Compliance Verification: Compliance has been verified as the reports have been submitted and the facility has corrected the excess emissions.


See INSP196550 for full details</td></tr>
