<tr><td>CRPT007886</td><td>F000015</td><td>Salt River Project - Kyrene Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Revised 2023b Semiannual Monitoring Report and Compliance Certification for the reporting period of July 1, 2023, through December 31, 2023. Due March 1, 2024.  Updated data included in Attachment 6.</td><td>03/01/2024</td><td>03/21/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>CRPT007712</td><td>Resubmittal of semiannual monitoring report and compliance certification for the reporting period 01-Jul-23 to 31-Dec-23. Report was resubmitted in a timely manner on 01-Mar-24, and reviewed on 21-Mar-24. 

The semiannual monitoring report was reviewed and determined to be in compliance, with notes as follows:
- i) SRP reported continuous compliance throughout the reporting period.
- ii) No deviations were reported over the reporting period.
- iii) Updated summary of unit operating hours provided and in compliance. Per compliance report revision, SRP was reporting partial operating hours as full operating hours, resulting in an overestimation of total hours of operation for units K-4, K-5, and K-6. The original data stated 73hrs, 57hrs, and 163hrs respectively, while the updated data confirmed 48hrs, 42hrs, and 33hrs respectively. The process is continuing to be monitored to ensure the data remains consistent going forward.
- iv) Summary of opacity readings provided with no visible emissions observed.
- v) No odor complaints received during the reporting period.
- vi) Ultra-low sulfur fuel confirmed.
- vii) 12-month rolling fuel throughput totaled 97,143gal as of Dec-23.
- viii) A fill pipe inspection was not conducted during this reporting period.
- ix) No support operations meet reporting requirements.
- x) Emissions deviations reporting and performance summary reports provided to Maricopa County via other compliance reports

The compliance certification report was reviewed, with Permit Conditions 18.a.ii Table 2 and 18.a.ii Table 4 noting intermittent compliance. The deviations were addressed in a Notice of Non-Compliance inspection report. See INSP184138 for further details.

No issues of non-compliance observed throughout review.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT007893</td><td>F001529</td><td>Honeywell International - Phoenix Engines</td><td>Title V</td><td>Aerospace Component Manufacturing</td><td>CMP001662</td><td>Honeywell International Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Annual Compliance Certification for 2023 (i.e. January 27, 2023 - January 26, 2024)</td><td>02/29/2024</td><td>04/10/2024</td><td>No-Revision Requested</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Revision was requested to include a certification of Completion, Truth, and Accuracy.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT007894</td><td>F001529</td><td>Honeywell International - Phoenix Engines</td><td>Title V</td><td>Aerospace Component Manufacturing</td><td>CMP001662</td><td>Honeywell International Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Title V Semi-Annual Monitoring Report for the second half of 2023 (i.e. July 27, 2023 - January 26, 2024)</td><td>02/29/2024</td><td>04/17/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The Semi-annual monitoring report was submitted on February 29, 2024. This is within the required time frame prior to the due date. The due date is 45 days from the end of the monitoring period ending January 26, 2024. 
The report includes a Certification of Truth, Accuracy, and Completeness. This is electronically submitted and signed by Israel San Pedro.

DEVIATION REPORT
The deviation report included two deviations from the permit P008563, however neither of them created excess emissions. 
Deviation from January 18, 2024 included cooling tower monthly PM calculations from permit condition 4.a and 19.f. The facility identified on January 18, 2024 that the monthly calculations for the PM emissions from the NSR regulated cooling towers were not being conducted for March 2023 to December 2023. The facility has determined the root cause and corrected this on January 18, 2024. Some of the cooling towers do not yet exist as the test cells do not yet exist. This includes cell 937, 938, and 939.

Deviation from August 10, 2023 was regarding the annual emission inventory fee from permit conditions 4.a, 4.e, and 11. The facility identified on August 10, 2023 that the annual emission inventory fee was paid after the due date of July 27, 2023. The facility corrected this on August 14, 2023. I confirmed all deviation information with Diana Furman on April 29, 2024

VISIBLE EMISSIONS REPORT
No visible emissions were observed during this reporting period.

EMISSIONS TABLES
12-month HAP emissions calculations: All 12-month rolling totals for single HAPs were below 9 tons on page 15. 
Total 12-month rolling total was 2.62 tons from January 2024. Highest was 3.37 tons in July 2023.
Records for jet fuel usage are kept.
Hard chromium plating records are kept below permitting limitations.
Test cell emissions and calculations are kept up to date. No issues noted.

SOLVENT DIP CLEANING 
The monthly solvent usage was recorded for all solvents used on-site. Monthly records have been kept. This is listed on page 13.

SOLVENT USAGE OTHER THAN DIP CLEANING
Monthly records of all other solvents used is kept up to date. This is listed on page 14. 

CHROME SCRUBBER
Chrome scrubber daily records appear to be operating within O&M Plan limits.

FUEL BURNING EQUIPMENT
The only piece of equipment that has usage during this time period are the Superior Mohawk Boilers. 12-month rolling total NOx is 0.41 tons which is below the limit of 1.1 tons. The GasTech Air Heaters were also used and have a 12-month rolling total for NOx of 0.13 tons.</td></tr>
