<tr><td>CRPT007686</td><td>F000701</td><td>Intel Corp - Ocotillo Campus</td><td>Title V</td><td>Semiconductors and Electronics</td><td>CMP001723</td><td>Intel Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Intel Corporation is submitting this Semi-Annual Compliance Report for the Ocotillo facility, located at 4500 South Dobson Road in Chandler, Arizona 85248 per Title V Permit P0010018, Facility ID F000701. This semi-annual compliance report is for the reporting period from July 1st, 2023 to December 31st, 2023.</td><td>01/29/2024</td><td>02/06/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semi-Annual Report for reporting period July 1, 2023 - December 31, 2023.

Report received by January 30 deadline.

All elements of Permit Condition 3.h.i. included.

No PALs 12-month rolling total emissions exceeded.

PAL emission calculation supporting data provided in Attachment A.

No emissions units were modified or added during the reporting period, though once cooling tower and three boilers for the F52/F62 were in the initial commissioning process. These emissions units are on the current Intel Title-V permit, and start-up emissions were included in PAL calculations.

No monitoring system or calculation procedure changes reported.

A deviation with Permit Condition 30.a. was reported. On July 14, 2023, a contractor began dust-generating operations in an area not included on the Dust Control Plan. This deviation was included as intermittent compliance on the 2023 Annual Compliance Certification Report, and non-compliance was not pursued for the issue.

Two temporary monitoring system shutdowns were reported. F22 RCTO #5 experienced a gas flow meter failure in June 2023. The RCTO continued to operate, though Intel determined that the unit did not operate outside of it's Operations & Maintenance Plan parameters. Additionally, a flow meter leak affected an HCL tank at the IWW. In both instances, most recent data was used to calculate emissions for both units, as part of sitewide PAL emission calculations. No compliance issues noted.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT007689</td><td>F000701</td><td>Intel Corp - Ocotillo Campus</td><td>Title V</td><td>Semiconductors and Electronics</td><td>CMP001723</td><td>Intel Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Intel Corporation is submitting this Annual Compliance Certification Report for the Ocotillo facility, located at 4500 South Dobson Road in Chandler, Arizona 85248 per Title V Permit P0010018, Facility ID F000701. This annual compliance certification report is for the reporting period from January 1st, 2023 to December 31st, 2023.</td><td>01/29/2024</td><td>02/06/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Annual Compliance Certification Report for Intel Ocotillo.

Report received within required timeframe.

Intermittent compliance was reported for two specific conditions:

Permit Condition 19:
A performance test on Fab 42 Boiler #1 showed NOx emissions that exceeded limitations set in PC 19.a.i. Table 4. An OTC-FRV was issued by Maricopa County as part of INSP176412.

Permit Condition 30:
Two deviations were reported for the failure to follow the most recently approved Dust Control Plan. In both instances, contractors conducted dust-generating operations that were temporarily not included on the Intel Dust Control Plan. These deviations were reported in both Semiannual Compliance Reports for 2023, CRPT006791 and CRPT007686. Maricopa County did not pursue noncompliance for either of these deviations.

General Condition 45 was also marked as intermittent for the two deviations listed above.

No additional deviations or noncompliance were reported by Maricopa County during 2023.</td></tr>
