<tr><td>CRPT007628</td><td>F045290</td><td>DBY Mine Site Buckeye</td><td>Minor</td><td>Sand & Gravel</td><td>CMP023370</td><td>DBY Mining LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Dust Control Plan</td><td>Corrections to Rule 316 Dust Control Plan to include ASTM method test and probe.</td><td>01/21/2024</td><td>02/06/2024</td><td>No</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>DCP unable to be approved on 02/06/24. Source advised that the following items were to be emailed to Inspector in order to approve. Due date is 02/13/24.

1.	Section 2(v)(2) – soil moisture testing methods
a.	The facility indicated that it is using a Speedy Moisture Meter. If using the speedy Moisture Meter, the following documents must be attached.
b.	Description of product (attach product specification sheets).
c.	Correlated results from both the ASTM C 566-97 and Speedy Moisture Meter for 20 samples.
d.	Description of the calibration process.
e.	Agreement to calibrate the Speedy Moisture Meter on a bi-weekly basis.
f.	Identification of at least 3 sampling points per process line used for calibration (3 each – beginning, middle, and end of process).
g.	Agreement to revert back to ASTM C 566-97 if Speedy Moisture Meter results do not correlate with ASTM C 566-97.

2.	Section 2(v)(4) – soil moisture testing attachments
a.	Process diagram identifying progression of material containing product less than 0.25” diameter through the process.
i.	Identify all screen outlets of material containing product &lt; 0.25” in diameter.
ii.	Identify all crusher outlets of material containing product &lt; 0.25” in diameter.
iii.	Identify all stacker points of material containing product &lt; 0.25” in diameter.
iv.	Identify all sample points for soil moisture tests.
v.	Identify the applicable minimum soil moisture content for each sample point.
b.	Provide an explanation or justification for each sampling point that a sample cannot be taken from.

3.	Section 2y – map
a.	A Dust Control Plan will not be approved unless a drawing is submitted showing all of the following elements.
b.	Property boundaries.
c.	Nearest public cross roads with street names.
d.	Identify staging areas, areas for stockpiles, haul roads, access roads, storage and parking areas, etc.
e.	Identify paved areas and cohesive hard surfaces.
f.	Exit locations, with type of trackout control equipment if applicable.
g.	North arrow.
h.	Acres to be disturbed.

Facility responded via email on 02/06/24 advising that they are not using Speedy Moisture Meter. Therefore, a new DCP is to be submitted on or before COB 02/13/24. Email to source sent.</td></tr>
