<tr><td>CRPT007572</td><td>F002504</td><td>Solana Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP000333</td><td>Arizona Solar One LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Semi-annual report for S2 2023 and annual certification/compliance</td><td>01/12/2024</td><td>03/25/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semiannual Compliance Certification and Monitoring Report for the period of 01-Jul-23 to 31-Dec-23.  Report was submitted in a timely manner on 12-Jan-24. 

The compliance report covers Permit Conditions 11.a and 11.b, with notes as follows:

PC 11.a.i: 12-month rolling total emissions as of Dec23:
- HTF HAP Emissions: 51.96tons (limit: 113tons)
- TES VOC Emissions: 0.53tons, with no individual unit over 2.0tons (limit: 12.0tons)
- VOC Emissions from HTF Impacted Soil: 0.0tons, (limit: 2.0tons)
- Ullage system:
-- Total non-fugitive VOCs: 3.23tons (limit: 15tons)
-- Total non-fugitive HAPs: 3.20tons (limit: 15tons)
-- Single non-fugitve HAP (HTF): 3.20tons (limit: 15tons)
PC 11.a.ii: No deviations noted during the reporting period.
PC 11.a.iii: CEMS outages were due to normal maintenance, with no outages due to unit malfunctions.
PC 11.a.iv: 1206 ball joint leaks reported, grade 1/2/3, with 848 ball joints repacked and 245 ball joints to be repacked.
PC 11.a.v: 331.42tons HTF added to the system throughout May23, and 222.64 added in Sep23.
PC 11 a.vii: HTF mass balance as of Dec23 totaled 11,984tons.
PC 11 a.viii: All HTF impacted soil was covered in sealed drums on-site with emissions calculated on mass balance.
PC 11 a.ix: No applicable HTF contamination events during the reporting period.

PC 11.b: Per report, facility was in continuous compliance for all permit conditions during the reporting period. However, items pertaining to the CEMS data (PC 9.a.ii.5 – PC 9.a.ii.12) did not that CEMS data could be erroneous. The issue, as noted in the most recent inspection report, involves the inaccurate data collection method of the CEMS unit. The Performance Testing group is currently working with Solana to rectify the issue, in which case compliance status could be updated accordingly. See INSP187524 for more details.</td></tr>
