<tr><td>CRPT007437</td><td>F039334</td><td>City of Tempe Fire Fighting Instruction</td><td>Open Burn</td><td>Not Applicable</td><td>CMP000836</td><td>City of Tempe</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Notification</td><td>Monique Rodriguez with City of Tempe submitted a Presumptive Permission to Burn for a fire fighting training activity to occur on Thursday, December 14th from 0830-1430 hrs.</td><td>12/13/2023</td><td>12/13/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Monique Rodriguez with City of Tempe submitted a Presumptive Permission to Burn for a fire fighting training activity to occur on Thursday, December 14th from 0830-1430 hrs.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT007436</td><td>F000789</td><td>Microchip Technology - Tempe</td><td>Minor</td><td>Semiconductors and Electronics</td><td>CMP002193</td><td>Microchip Technology Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Microchip’s report on the 3.5-hour emergency bypass of RCTO 20-2 that occurred on Monday, December 11 from 6 am to 9:30 am, including Rule 130 defense.</td><td>12/13/2023</td><td>02/01/2024</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This compliance report is a self-report of an equipment malfunction that caused VOC emissions to bypass RCTO 20-2 for 3.5 hours, beginning at 6:00 a.m. and ending at 9:30 a.m. on December 11, 2023. The 3.5-hour bypass event was a result of an equipment fault that occurred during their most recently scheduled maintenance period (November 15-17, 2023). Approximately 17.5 lbs of VOCs were released.

The facility invoked Rule 130 as a defense. The self-report was within 2 working days of the equipment malfunction as required in Rule 130, so the facility notified the Maricopa County Air Quality Department within the proper time frame. However, there is no permit requirement the facility notifies the Department of a malfunction or upset, but they did anyway in this compliance report.

There were three additional emergency bypass events that occurred after the December 11, 2023 one that was reported in this compliance report. The facility is in violation of Rule 338 §301 because their RCTO 20-2 was not properly functioning at all times. A violation report will be written to account for all four of these instances.

Refer to INSP191531 for more information.</td></tr>
