<tr><td>CRPT007321</td><td>F000109</td><td>American Industries Diversified</td><td>Minor</td><td>Metal Fabrication</td><td>CMP000209</td><td>American Industries Diversified Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Quarterly AID Exceedance Report 7-23 to 9-23</td><td>11/09/2023</td><td>11/09/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>I reviewed the quarterly exceedance report for the months of July 2023 to September 2023. This report was requested for submittal as corrective action to Notices of Non-Compliance issued during an inspection conducted due to a complaint investigation. The investigation concluded with the discovery of solvent emissions exceedances pursuant to 40 CR Part 63 Subpart T that went unreported at the time it occurred. As a result of this inspection/violation, the Maricopa County Air Quality Department (MCAQD) requested the facility submit the exceedance reports on a quarterly basis instead of a semi-annual basis until further notice. See INSP187921 for more information.

This report states there were no 3-month rolling average emissions exceedances between July 2023 and September 2023. The next quarterly report shall be submitted for October 2023 to December 2023. Permit Condition 23.b details the exceedance reporting requirements for this facility and explains how MCAQD is allowed to request the change in reporting frequency.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT007314</td><td>F000109</td><td>American Industries Diversified</td><td>Minor</td><td>Metal Fabrication</td><td>CMP000209</td><td>American Industries Diversified Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Requested Source Records</td><td>Six Month Exceedance Report 7/2020 to 12/2020</td><td>11/09/2023</td><td>11/09/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>I reviewed the semi-annual exceedance report for the months of July 2020 to December 2020. This report was requested for submittal as corrective action to Notices of Non-Compliance issued during an inspection conducted due to a complaint investigation. The investigation concluded with the discovery of solvent emissions exceedances pursuant to 40 CR Part 63 Subpart T that went unreported at the time it occurred. See INSP187921 for more information.

This report states there was one exceedance of the 3-month rolling average emissions limit of 215 lbs/month during this time period. The report states the exceedance, why it occurred, and if that matter is resolved. There was an equipment leak at the time and all the necessary repairs have been made. Permit Condition 21.a.ii, 21.b, and 23.b detail the exceedance and reporting requirements for this facility.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT007313</td><td>F000109</td><td>American Industries Diversified</td><td>Minor</td><td>Metal Fabrication</td><td>CMP000209</td><td>American Industries Diversified Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Requested Source Records</td><td>Six Month Exceedance Report 1/2020 to 6/2020</td><td>11/09/2023</td><td>11/09/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>I reviewed the semi-annual exceedance report for the months of January 2020 to June 2020. This report was requested for submittal as corrective action to Notices of Non-Compliance issued during an inspection conducted due to a complaint investigation. The investigation concluded with the discovery of solvent emissions exceedances pursuant to 40 CR Part 63 Subpart T that went unreported at the time it occurred. See INSP187921 for more information.

