The department has invalidated the material sample test results due to the results showing inconsistent values for the expanded beads.  The results show a site average of 1.32% pentane for all the samples taken; the South side samples averaged 2.51% pentane with the North side averaging 0.97% pentane.  The results show that  11 of the 22 samples were below 1% pentane with 18 of 22 samples being below 2% pentane.  The department believes these values are not representative of actual operations and that there might have been issues with the sampling.  A retest will be required.

