<tr><td>CRPT007247</td><td>F003607</td><td>Vulcan Asphalt</td><td>Minor</td><td>Nonmetallic Mineral Processing</td><td>CMP003521</td><td>Vulcan Asphalt LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Test Report</td><td>Compliance test report, covering testing dates of 8/23/23, 10/2/23 and 10/12/23.  The initial test conducted on 8/23/23 exceeded allowable limits despite a prior black light test noting all bags in good working order, and a 0.0% opacity observed during the performance test. Production rates observed during the test were not linear with PM concentrations, which would be inconsistent with a malfunctioning control device. The unit was retested on 10/2/23 however the testing company denoted reagent contamination during the laboratory analysis. The third test was conducted on 10/12/23, and was well below emission limits.  Due to the inconsistent results during the first performance test  and contamination observed during the second performance test, Vulcan would request only the results from the third performance test be used to determine compliance.  An extension for this report was requested and grated by Scott Treece on 10/13/23, the extension required the report be submitted on 10/27/23.</td><td>10/27/2023</td><td>12/28/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The initial performance test conducted on August 23, 2023, indicate the CMI HMAP failed to meet the PM permit limits. The retest conducted on October 12, 2023 showed compliance with the PM permit limits.</td></tr>
