<tr><td>CRPT007224</td><td>F001644</td><td>Northwest Regional Landfill</td><td>Title V</td><td>Landfills</td><td>CMP003877</td><td>Waste Management Arizona Landfills Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Northwest Regional Landfill (Permit No. V97-016) Semi-Annual Compliance Report for the reporting period of April 1, 2023 to September 30, 2023</td><td>10/26/2023</td><td>11/06/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semi-annual compliance report submitted for the reporting period from 01-Apr-23 to 30-Sep-23. The report was submitted in a timely manner on 26-Oct-23. The report covers the reporting requirements as part of Permit Condition 21 of the facility’s air quality permit, with notes as follows:


SEMI-ANNUAL MONITORING REPORT

Report was reviewed with no issues observed for Permit Conditions 21.A.i – 21.A.x, and 21.A.xii – 21.A.xv, with notes as follows:

PC21.A.vi Emissions Report per PC18: Emissions report was attached in Appendix D.
- Facility wide 12-month rolling emissions:
-- VOC: 9.70tons(limit: 50tons)
-- CO: 87.22tons (limit: 225tons)
-- NOx: 23.36tons (limit: 85tons)
-- SOx: 2.89tons (limit: 25tons)
-- PM10: 6.78tons (limit: 30tons)
-- PM2.5: 6.78tons (limit: 30tons)
-- Single HAP: Toluene – 1.18tons(limit: 9tons)
-- Total HAPs: 3.71tons (20tons)

PC21.A.xi Surface Emissions Monitoring: Quarterly landfill surface emissions monitoring completed by SCS Field Services from 17-May-23 to 19-May-23 (Q2) and from 14-Sep-23 to 15-Sep-23 (Q3). 
- Q2: There were exceedances observed during the observation period, however per the report the exceedances were not observed in the NSPS-regulated area of the facility and were used for general evaluation purposes. No exceedances were observed in the NSPS-regulated area of the facility during the observation period.
- Q3: A total of three exceedances were noted during this monitoring event, at wells EW107, EW115 and one surface exceedance. The areas were re-monitored on 15-Sep-23 after remediation efforts and each site was determined to be below 500ppm.

PC21.A.xii Well Expansion System: No well expansions were conducted during the period.


COMPLIANCE CERTIFICATION

Per the report, the facility was in continuous compliance with all permit conditions.</td></tr>
