Exponent completed exothermic testing on September 1st involving a full size passenger truck weighing exactly 6070 pounds.  The testing was intended to evaluate how fire propagates and progresses in this vehicle and was performed in accordance with County Rule 314, subsections 320 & 321.  
 
In accordance with to County Rule 314, subsections 320, 321, & 501.2, I am documenting the following data which are an update to the estimates found in the previous emails:
•	501.2a - Date of the burn – September 1, 2023
•	501.2b - Time of Day of Testing – Initiated at 8:56am 
•	501.2c - The legal location of testing - Exponent, Inc at 23445 N. 19th Avenue, Phoenix, AZ 85027 (33 deg 42’00 N, 112 deg 05’19 W) within our thermal test area. 
•	501.2d,e - Designation and quantity of unit under test – A single 2020 Nissan Titan Platinum Reserve Truck; the truck will have full engine fluids but the gasoline tank will be drained to 1/4 tank capacity (approximately 6.5 gallons).  
•	501.2f,g,h - Type & Quantity of Material Burned; Total Charge Weight; Total Emissions - See table below for the post-test measurements and resultant emissions calculation: test consumed 130 lbs of car parts and did not involve the fuel tank.  
•	501.2i - Test Procedure - Lab Test Safety Plan 2308292.000 - 3536
•	501.2j - Duration of Burn – 32 minutes
•	501.2k - Estimated Emissions - See below tables.  
 
