<tr><td>CRPT007003</td><td>F045086</td><td>MTM Transit</td><td>Minor</td><td>Gasoline Non-resale</td><td>CMP025499</td><td>MTM Transit LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Permit Close Request</td><td>PCR</td><td>09/08/2023</td><td>09/11/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Received permit cancellation request via AQPermits</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT007002</td><td>F000397</td><td>Exponent</td><td>Minor</td><td>Gasoline Non-resale</td><td>CMP001308</td><td>Exponent of Delaware Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Notification</td><td>Bryan, Brandon, Frank (and Scott)  – 
The county air quality department website indicates that a high pollution advisory and restricted burn period has been issued for tomorrow, 9/8/2023.  A test, detailed below, is scheduled for tomorrow and falls under the ‘shall approve’ portions of Maricopa County Rule 314 pertaining to safety testing related to DOT/DOD/commercial/other requirements (Sections 320/321, subsections 7 & 8). 
 
We will be studying eddy current and wind patterns using small smoke generating candles (see photo in attached email) on a vehicle to better understand the effect that wind has on fire propagation in passenger vehicles.  Each smoke generating candle weighs 2-ounces and we will be consuming up to 1-pound of them over the course of tomorrow’s testing.  Emissions calculations have not been performed as the emissions cannot exceed the fuel load (e.g., 1-pound of smoke candles) and would therefore be less than the permitted 2-pounds of particulate emissions described in the sections of Rule 314 sited above.</td><td>09/07/2023</td><td>09/11/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Review of notification for facility test operations.  Submitted test report confirmed less than 2.0lbs of particulate matter would be emitted during testing activity.  Facility request approved during restricted burn period on September 8, 2023.

No noncompliance issues noted.</td></tr>
