<tr><td>CRPT006792</td><td>F001522</td><td>Mesquite Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP002166</td><td>Mesquite Power LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Enclosed for your review, please find the Compliance Certification and Semiannual Monitoring Report from Mesquite Generating Station covering the reporting time period from January 1, 2023 to June 30, 2023, as required in the applicable Title V Permit condition 21.c. If you have any questions regarding this report, please contact D’Armond Chee at (602) 236-0039.</td><td>07/31/2023</td><td>10/23/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>I reviewed the Semiannual Compliance Certification and Monitoring report for the reporting period of January 1, 2023 to June 30, 2023.

The report should include, at a minimum, the following:

1) The identification of each term or condition of the permit that is the basis of the certification;
2) The compliance status;
3) Whether compliance was continuous or intermittent;
4) The method(s) used for determining the compliance status of the source, currently and over the reporting period;
5) Other facts as the Control Officer may require to determine compliance status of the source;
6) Each report shall cover all instances of deviations from these permit conditions during the reporting period, the cause of the deviations if any were present, and any applicable corrective actions taken;
7) The Permittee shall include a copy of the portion of the odor log which covers the applicable 6 month reporting period in each of the semiannual compliance reports. If no complaints were received during the reporting period, a statement to that effect may be substituted for the copy of the odor log; and
8) Permittee shall comply with applicable reporting requirements for support operations including spray coating Architectural Coatings (Permit Condition 24), Abrasive Blasting (Permit Condition 25), Spray Coating (Permit Condition 26), Solvent Cleaning Operations (Permit Condition 27), Wipe Cleaning Operations (Permit Condition 28), and Volatile Organic Compounds (Permit Condition 29).
9) Visible emissions and opacity readings

The format of the report satisfies items (1), (2), (3), and (4) from the list above. Each permit condition was listed with statements demonstrating the facility was In Compliance and denoting that the compliance status was continuous. The method used for determining the compliance status was also detailed for each permit condition.

Item (6) - The report demonstrates the facility was in compliance with each permit condition and that there were no deviations from these permit conditions.

Item (7) - The report states there were no odor log entries during the reporting period.

Item (8) - The report indicates the facility is complying with the reporting requirements for operations listed in Permit Conditions 24-29. The report states the status of each of the operations on site for the reporting period.

Item (9) - The report states the facility logged visible emissions testing and that there were no visible emissions observed outside of uncombined water.

The report was submitted on the last day of the month following the reporting period, which is within the appropriate time frame.

No compliance issues were noted.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT006793</td><td>F001522</td><td>Mesquite Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP002166</td><td>Mesquite Power LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Enclosed for your review, please find the attached Semiannual Excess Emissions and Monitoring System Performance report from Mesquite Generating Station reflecting the period from January 1, 2023 to June 30, 2023. This report is submitted in accordance with 40CFR60.7(c) and (d). Data in the report reflects all plant operations for the entire reporting period for the Units 1, 2, 5, and 6. If you have any questions regarding this report, please call D’Armond Chee at 602-236-0039.</td><td>07/31/2023</td><td>10/23/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>I reviewed the Semiannual Excess Emissions and Monitoring Report.

The facility is required to submit only the summary report form if the total duration of excess emissions for the reporting period was reported to be less than 1 percent of the total operating time and the total duration of CEMS downtime for the reporting period was reported to be less than 5 percent of the total operating time for all CCS units.

The facility reported there were no NOx and CO emissions excursions or exceedances during the reporting period of January 1, 2023 to June 30, 2023. Therefore, the total duration of excess emissions for the reporting period was reported to be less than 1 percent of the total operating time for CCS Units 1, 2, 5 and 6. 

The total duration of CEMS downtime for the reporting period was reported to be less than 5 percent of the total operating time for CCS Units 1, 2, 5 and 6. The highest reported duration of CEMS downtime across all units was for CCS Unit #2 (pollutant was NOx), at 1.85% of total operating time. 

The facility has complied with the reporting requirements of 40 CFR §60.7(c) and (d) by only submitting the summary report form for the reporting period.

The summary report form was submitted in the format required in 40 CFR §60.7(d).

The report was submitted on the last day of the month following the reporting period, which is within the appropriate time frame.

No compliance issues were noted.</td></tr>
