<tr><td>CRPT006814</td><td>F000015</td><td>Salt River Project - Kyrene Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>72-Hour Excess Emissions Report for Unit K-7. On July 26 in hours 11:00, 12:00, and 13:00, Unit K-7 exceeded its 3-hour average CO corrected concentration and mass emissions rate limitations. Due July 30 at 11:00 AM.</td><td>07/28/2023</td><td>08/16/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>72hr excess emissions report submitted for incident that occurred on 26-Jul-23. Report was submitted in a timely manner on 28-Jul-23. 

The incident on 26-Jul-23 details a malfunction in the duct burners elements which caused higher CO concentration during a period of increased fuel flow to the burners from 1138 to 1148. The higher level of fuel flow from the duct burners lead to an exceedance in the 3hr average CO emissions limitation and the CO concentration limit. Specifically, the limits were exceeded as follows:

3hr average limit with duct burner on (limit: 17.3lbs/hr)
- hour 1100: 43.3lbs/hr
- hour 1200: 43.8lbs/hr
- hour 1300: 43.8lbs/hr

3hr average CO corrected concentration for K-7 unit (limit: 3.9ppm)
- hour 1100: 12.6ppm @ 15% O2
- hour 1200: 12.6ppm @ 15% O2
- hour 1300: 12.6ppm @ 15% O2

As a corrective action, the duct burners were removed from service to prevent further issues until a full maintenance inspection can be completed.

A Notice of Non-Compliance has been issued for exceeding emissions limitations. See INSP184138 for further details.</td></tr>
