<tr><td>CRPT006778</td><td>F002681</td><td>SFPP-Phoenix Terminal</td><td>Title V</td><td>Petroleum Products Bulk Storage/Handling</td><td>CMP002921</td><td>SFPP LP</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>2023 1H Phoenix Semiannual & GDGACT Submittal</td><td>07/27/2023</td><td>08/15/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Compliance report is the Semiannual Compliance Certification and Monitoring Report for the period of 01-Jan-23 to 30-Jun-23.  


AREA OF CONCERN

The semi-annual monitoring report contained inaccurate information for the following sections:

- 37.f.iv: The report stated temperatures were recorded during periods of SVE unit use, however after conversation with Corbin Hennick, Permitting Compliance Specialist, it was confirmed that the SVE units have been offline since 2021. Mr. Hennick stated that the facility is hoping to replace the units, however for the time being they will remain offline.
- 37.f.xi: The report stated that contractor abrasive blasting work was conducted on-site as part of out-of-service tank maintenance. After conversation with Mr. Hennick, it was confirmed that all blasting was internal blasting, with no external blasting occurring during the reporting period. 

An addendum was requested electronically in order to clarify the above inaccuracies. The addendum was received on 21-Aug-23 and reviewed on 14-Sep-23.

Per the Compliance Certification Report, one deviation was reported on 11-Apr-23 and documented in compliance report CRPT006347. All other permit conditions were noted as being in continuous compliance during the reporting period.

The semi-annual monitoring report was found to be in compliance with Permit Condition 37.f. I reviewed the monitoring report, with notes as follows:

- i: Monthly inspections conducted in compliance with no deviations noted.
- ii: John Zink Oxidizer operated without deviations and operated in bypass mode due to the saturator not being installed.
- iii: CAU-1 is currently out of operation. Emissions were routed through the John Zink Oxidizer for the reporting period.
- v: No issues observed with the "card access" system.
- vi: No visible emissions observed during the reporting period.
- vii: No odor complaints observed during the reporting period.
- viii: VOC list reviewed and in compliance.
- ix: No issues observed during walk-around inspections.
- x: No issues observed with architectural coatings.
- xii: No deviations in dust-control requirements.
- xiii: 12-month rolling VOC emissions totaled 58.38tons.
- xiv/xvi: One deviation was noted on 09-Apr-23, and was submitted to MCAQD on 11-Apr-23.
- xvii: Excess emissions reports submitted in a timely manner.

The Subpart BBBBBB Report met all requirements of 40 CFR Subpart 63. The report notes 2hours of excess emissions during the reporting period due to control equipment problems. 

Overall the compliance report was found to be in compliance with no issues observed.</td></tr>
