<tr><td>CRPT006606</td><td>F006603</td><td>Ball Metal Beverage Container Corporation</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Metal Fabrication</td><td>CMP000443</td><td>Ball Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Test Report</td><td>Ball Glendale Performance Test Report</td><td>06/08/2023</td><td>10/26/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The RTO did not meet the destruction efficiency (DE) requirement of Permit Condition 5.c. The results show that the RTO system had a 96.6% DE. The permit requires a 98% DE. Sampling took place on the shared stack of two RTOs. It was recommended that the 98% DE compliance be determined on the separate RTO stacks. 30 days from 26OCT23 were provided for provided a retest date, and 60 days was provided from 26OCT23 for the retest to be conducted.</td></tr>
