<tr><td>CRPT006446</td><td>F001644</td><td>Northwest Regional Landfill</td><td>Title V</td><td>Landfills</td><td>CMP003877</td><td>Waste Management Arizona Landfills Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Northwest Regional Landfill Semi-Annual Compliance/NSPS/NESHAP Report for the reporting period of October 1, 2022 through March 31, 2023</td><td>04/27/2023</td><td>08/14/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semi-annual compliance report submitted for the reporting period from 01-Oct-22 to 31-Mar-23. The report was submitted in a timely manner on 27-Apr-23. The report covers the reporting requirements as part of Permit Condition 21 of the facility’s air quality permit, with notes as follows:


SEMI-ANNUAL MONITORING REPORT

Report was reviewed with no issues observed for Permit Conditions 21.A.i – 21.A.x, and 21.A.xii – 21.A.xv, with notes as follows:

PC21.A.vi Emissions Report per PC18: Emissions report was attached in Appendix E.
- Facility wide 12-month rolling emissions:
-- VOC: 4.57tons(limit: 50tons)
-- CO: 96.84tons (limit: 225tons)
-- NOx: 23.17tons (limit: 85tons)
-- SOx: 2.95tons (limit: 25tons)
-- PM10: 6.88tons (limit: 30tons)
-- PM2.5: 6.88tons (limit: 30tons)
-- Single HAP: HCl – 0.50tons(limit: 9tons)
-- Total HAPs: 0.77tons (20tons)

PC21.A.xi Surface Emissions Monitoring: Quarterly landfill surface emissions monitoring completed by Tetra Tech BAS from 11-Nov-21 to 17-Nov-21 (Q4) and from 17-Mar-22 to 23-Mar-22 (Q1). 
- Q4: There were exceedances noted at the following locations: EW-118, CS-6, LCR-10, EW-30 (16-Nov-21), and LCR-8 (17-Nov-21). The areas were re-monitored on 24-Nov-21, with only LCR-10 exceeding a second time. LCR-10 was monitored again on 03-Dec-21 and determined to be below 500ppm. All exceedance locations were re-monitored on 15-Dec-21 and confirmed to be below 500ppm.
- Q1: No exceedances were noted during this monitoring event.

PC21.A.xii Well Expansion System: No well expansions were conducted during the period, however it was noted that wells NWREW113, NWREW120, NWREW121, NWREW123 and NWREEW124 were abandoned in Dec-22.


COMPLIANCE CERTIFICATION

Per the report, the facility was in continuous compliance with all permit conditions.</td></tr>
