<tr><td>CRPT006210</td><td>F004009</td><td>NexusTek</td><td>Minor</td><td>Generator, Stationary (ATO)</td><td>CMP024774</td><td>NexusTek LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Ownership Transfer</td><td>Received Permit Transfer Request via AQ Permits email</td><td>03/09/2023</td><td>03/14/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Received Permit Transfer Request via AQ Permits email</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT006209</td><td>F000048</td><td>Northwest Water Reclamation Plant</td><td>Minor</td><td>Wastewater Treatment Plants and Lift Stations</td><td>CMP000816</td><td>City of Mesa</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Submitting a report on event that occurred on March 6, 2023</td><td>03/09/2023</td><td>03/15/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Report received and reviewed. 

The deviation from normal operation is noted due to the failure of the Variable Frequency Drives (VFDs) during an emergency generator load test. 

While the site exceeded Permit condition 3.b.ii, the 19.6 hours of maintenance could not be avoided due to unplanned failure of equipment, which caused the flare from running at the site's indicated operational parameters in their O&M Plan. Backup controls of the on-site boiler and cogeneration unit could not be used due to the compressor that provides the gas to the boiler and cogeneration unit being un-operational due to the failure of the VFDs.

Methane gas normally routed to the flare for destruction was not purposefully routed to bypass the control systems in place. Due to this, a notice of non compliance was not issued. According to the report, the gas continued to flow into the flare, despite the flare not operating at the ideal temperature. 

The amount of methane discharged and the amount of H2S detected at the nearest occupied presence (Chicago Cubs Spring Training Stadium) were both found to be within permitted limits.

The facility took the appropriate actions by immediately addressing the issues which caused the facility to be operating outside of their O&M Plan, and the facility appropriately notified the Maricopa County Air Quality Department of the deviations from their permit.</td></tr>
