<tr><td>CRPT006004</td><td>F000833</td><td>Skyline Steel</td><td>Minor</td><td>Metal Fabrication</td><td>CMP002977</td><td>Skyline Steel Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>MACT 6X compliance report (2022)</td><td>02/24/2023</td><td>03/02/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>I commenced review of the required report. I could not complete review without interview so I called the facility and requested to speak to on-site operator, Mr. Camp.  The unidentified contact who I spoke to told me Mr. Camp does not work there anymore and suggested I speak with "Mark" the Chief Operating Officer, who will not be in until tomorrow. I left message requesting a return call on Friday, March 3, 2023.

On March 3, 2023, I received email from consultant, Bob Peshak of Envirosure LLC inviting me to contact him for my queries.  I telephoned Mr. Peshak and he explained the "Wheelabrator" is alias for emission unit ABS-001, the Gietart GW-1500. I arranged to submit queries by email.

I exchanged email correspondence with Mr. Peshak regarding the monitoring and updated Facility Contacts List. 

Monday, March 6, 2023.
After review of the provided monitoring records and correspondence, I determined it was compliant with the required Tier 1 graduated monitoring schedule, which is currently on a Quarterly frequency.

I made the following ancillary observations:

Neither the 2021 Annual certification of Compliance was submitted; nor required monitoring previous to June 16, 2022; but this issue has already already been addressed and cited, see May 24, 2022 INSP168455 for detail.


NOTE:
	Report includes records for fugitive dust emission monitoring for the Plasma
	cutting tables and abrasive blaster.  However, neither MACT XXXXXX nor the
	permit requires the plasma cutting monitoring. The required monitoring
	is solely for the welding operations. The inclusion of the monitoring for the plasma
	cutting operations is compliant, but not required. 

	The monitoring for the abrasive blaster i.e. "Wheelabrator" is subject to the O&M Plan
	recordkeeping and is not a required element of the annual certification of compliance
	report required by PC 14.

	The training records included are a record required by O&M Plan CRPT005006; but is not
	a required element of the annual certification of compliance report required by PC 14.


On March 6, 2023; I telephoned Compliance Contact, Shelley Gindling and explained the following area of concern
	  and provided compliance determination for this report.

AREA OF CONCERN [Rule 370 § 302.148; 40 CFR 63.11519(b)(2)(iii); PC 14]; which, in summary
		 requires the annual certification for compliance to be submitted no later
		 than January 31.
	• Report was submitted on 24-Feb-2023. 
	• While the late submittal of this report is non-compliant on its face, I observe
	   the report had been prepared on January 31, 2023; only not submitted by the
	   preparer as required.
	• Facility had some turnover, including the previous CROMERR certifier. The
	  current certifier, Ms. Gindling was recently added as Compliance Contact
	  on February 23, 2023; and the report submitted the following day.
	• Henceforth, a citation may be issued for late submittals of the required
	  annual certification and compliance report.
 
Ms. Gindling confirmed she is sole Compliance Contact for the facility.

No violations noted.</td></tr>
