<tr><td>CRPT005408</td><td>F001194</td><td>South Resource Bureau</td><td>Minor</td><td>Institutions - Public/Government</td><td>CMP000821</td><td>City of Phoenix</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>2022 Malfunction Report</td><td>02/22/2023</td><td>03/14/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Malfunction Report submitted as required by permit condition 13.d.
The permittee reported the gasoline dispensing system failed the annual stage I test and was taken out of service on September 27, 2022.
The system was shut down to reduce vapor loss and emissions.
Repairs were made and the system passed the Stage I test on December 6, 2022.

By March 15 of each year, the Permittee shall report the number, duration, and a brief description of each type of malfunction which occurred during the previous calendar year and which caused or may have caused any applicable emission limitation to be exceeded. The report must also include a description of actions taken by the Permittee to minimize emissions in accordance with Permit Condition 3, including actions taken to correct a malfunction.</td></tr>
