<tr><td>CRPT006023</td><td>F003028</td><td>MMI Tank and Industrial Service</td><td>Minor</td><td>Metal Fabrication</td><td>CMP000440</td><td>Baker Commodities Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Annual Report</td><td>02/01/2023</td><td>02/10/2023</td><td>No-Revision Requested</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Reviewed Annual Certification and Compliance Report for reporting period of January 1, 2022 through December 31, 2022.
No visible emissions reported in excess of 20% opacity.

Method 22 visible emissions (VE) are conducted quarterly as allowed by permit condition 17.c.iv.
The highest VE readings reported were on February 17, 2022, August 24, 2022 and November 24, 2022 for the abrasive blasting operation, at 10% opacity.

the Abrasive Blasting Visible Emissions Reporting Table shows a reading was conducted on April 24, 2022, however; there is no Method 22 form included for this date.
There is a Method 22 form for August 24, 2022, but this  date does not correspond with the reporting table.

An email was sent to Dave Cooper, the General Manager for MMI Tank and Industrial Service, and advised him to amend the report to show the correct dates for the VE readings, by February 13, 2023.

In addition, the annual report was due by January 31, 2022, and not received until February 1, 2022. 

I sent Mr. Cooper a preliminary findings email to inform him I am issuing a notice of non-compliance, for failure to submit this Annual Certification and Compliance Report by the due date of January 31, 2023.

February 14, 2023:

I received an email from Dean Patel, the Environmental Consultant for MMI Tank and Industrial Service.
The string of emails showed, Mr. Patel sent an email to our department on January 15, 2023, asking how the report is to be submitted.
Mr. Patel did not receive a response until January 30, 2023 and did submit the report on February 1, 2023.
Due to the late response Mr. Patel received, a violation will not be issued.

Mr. Patel also submitted the revised report to show the correct dates for the VE readings.</td></tr>
