<tr><td>CRPT005959</td><td>F000014</td><td>Salt River Project - Agua Fria Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Part 60 Excess Emissions and Monitoring Downtime Report. July 1, 2022 through December 31, 2022. Due on January 30, 2023.</td><td>01/26/2023</td><td>02/15/2023</td><td>No-Revision Requested</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Unit 8 CEMS performance summary shows total duration of excess emissions to be 1 hour. Unit 8 exceedance events show the duration to be 2 hours. The excess emission report submitted on January 13, 2023, also indicated unit 8 only had one hour of exceedance. The facility informed me the 72 hour report erroneously left out hour 2100 on December 15, 2022, and a new 72-hour emission will be submitted. The revised 72-hour report was submitted under CRPT006063 which validates the Unit 8 CEMS performance summary.

Facility is revising CEMS report summary to show accurate hours and causes for Unit 8.</td></tr>
