The following report to comply with the Cogeneration Conditions Section 13b of Facility# F000048. The Total Sulfur must be &lt;0.08%.</td><td>01/26/2023</td><td>02/07/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This report submitted regarding the sulfur content in the waste gas of the Cogeneration Engine per Section 13b meets the required monthly monitoring records requirement, indicating less than 0.08% sulfur by weight, as outlined in condition 12a. No compliance issues noted.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT005956</td><td>F003876</td><td>Revolution Industrial</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Abrasive Blasting, Portable</td><td>CMP027293</td><td>Loenbro Industrial Construction LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Semi-Annual HAP Report for July-December 2022</td><td>01/26/2023</td><td>02/07/2023</td><td>No-Revision Requested</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semi-annual emissions report for the reporting period from 01-Jan-22 to 30-Jun-22.

After review of the compliance report, it was determined that the report did not properly meet the requirements of Permit Condition 4 of the facility's most recently approved permit. Specifically, permit conditions 4.a and 4.b require that monthly and 12-month rolling totals be provided for the HAP emissions and HAP usage on-site, respectively. The compliance report only provides the rolling totals for the 6 months of the reporting period, rather than the 12 calendar months preceding the end of the reporting period.

I spoke with Belen Angulo, Safety Director, over the phone to discuss the issue. Mr. Angulo stated that the compliance reports were submitted by their consulting company Envirosure. I stated that the semiannual reports for both the Jan22-Jun22 and Jul22-Dec22 reporting periods will need to be resubmitted to meet the permit requirements. I stated that an email would be sent outlining the resubmission request.

Bob Peshak, Consultant with Envirosure, confirmed over email that the compliance reports had been resubmitted with updated information.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT005072</td><td>F003876</td><td>Revolution Industrial</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Abrasive Blasting, Portable</td><td>CMP027293</td><td>Loenbro Industrial Construction LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>This Compliance Report is the Semiannual HAP report for January 2022 through June 2022.</td><td>01/26/2023</td><td>02/07/2023</td><td>No-Revision Requested</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semi-annual emissions report for the reporting period from 01-Jan-22 to 30-Jun-22.

After review of the compliance report, it was determined that the report did not properly meet the requirements of Permit Condition 4 of the facility's most recently approved permit. Specifically, permit conditions 4.a and 4.b require that monthly and 12-month rolling totals be provided for the HAP emissions and HAP usage on-site, respectively. The compliance report only provides the rolling totals for the 6 months of the reporting period, rather than the 12 calendar months preceding the end of the reporting period.

I spoke with Belen Angulo, Safety Director, over the phone to discuss the issue. Mr. Angulo stated that the compliance reports were submitted by their consulting company Envirosure. I stated that the semiannual reports for both the Jan22-Jun22 and Jul22-Dec22 reporting periods will need to be resubmitted to meet the permit requirements. Additionally, a Notice of Non-Compliance will be issued for failure to submit the Jan22-Jun22 report in a timely manner. I stated that an email would be sent outlining the resubmission, and a separate preliminary findings email for the Notice of Non-Compliance. See INSP177213 for more information regarding the Notice of Non-Compliance.

Bob Peshak, Consultant with Envirosure, confirmed over email that the compliance reports had been resubmitted with updated information.</td></tr>
