<tr><td>CRPT005884</td><td>F001700</td><td>Phoenix Manufacturing</td><td>Minor</td><td>Metal Fabrication</td><td>CMP002507</td><td>Phoenix Manufacturing Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Period 1/1/2022' to 12/31/2022'. Due date no later than 1/31/203'. Supporting documents are the quarterly reports, annual report and an explanatory document for activities, including notable issues during the 2022' year.</td><td>01/17/2023</td><td>03/15/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Permit condition 6 requires that an annual report be submitted for January 1 - December 31 of the previous calendar year and be submitted no later than January 31. The report for January 1, 2022 through December 31, 2022 was received January 17, 2023. No valid EPA Method 9 certification was submitted for the employee who did the readings for quarters 1 and 2, however the explanatory document stated that the employee that took the readings had left the company and they do not have proof of valid Method 9 certification. This was revealed during a routine inspection by Justin Suryanata, who issued a violation. The document also explains that readings were not taken during quarter 3 because that was when it was discovered that no employee had valid certification. Readings for quarter 4 were taken a few days after an employee was certified. All other required reporting conditions are present. No issues considering the facility is working with an inspector and can account for all discrepancies.</td></tr>
