<tr><td>CRPT005660</td><td>F001684</td><td>Fisher Sand & Gravel</td><td>Minor</td><td>Asphalt Plant, Portable</td><td>CMP001368</td><td>Fisher Sand & Gravel Co</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Test Report</td><td>Attached is a copy of the Black light test performed on 8/11/2022.</td><td>11/17/2022</td><td>11/22/2022</td><td>No</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The test report cannot be accepted for the following reasons:

1.	No advance notification was provided to the Department.  The facility is required to provide at least a 14 day advance notification.  The advance notification which includes the date/time of testing, shall be uploaded into AQD Online Portal.
2.	The incorrect number of bags was stated in the report.  In January 2022, Almis confirmed that the baghouse has 940 bags.  However, the report states that 1,044 bags are present.
3.	The report identified 19 bags needing replacement but the report has 17 bags being replaced as part of the corrective action.
4.	The report was not submitted to the Department in a timely manner.  The facility is required to submit the report within 30 days of testing.  The report shall be uploaded into the AQD Online Portal.
5.	The testing and report were not conducted in accordance with applicable rules/regulations nor the approved Operations & Maintenance Plan.

Therefore, the biannual black light testing will need to be reperformed.  Advance notification of testing is to be provided to the Department and the test shall be conducted on or before Tuesday, 12/20/2022.

The recent inspection conducted by Inspector Emma Coleman may result in the issuance of notices of non-compliance relating to the black light testing.  The Inspector will notify you in writing if this is the case.  

Source notified via email on 11/22/2022.</td></tr>
