<tr><td>CRPT005589</td><td>F000789</td><td>Microchip Technology - Tempe</td><td>Minor</td><td>Semiconductors and Electronics</td><td>CMP002193</td><td>Microchip Technology Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>RCTO 20-2 scheduled maintenance report. Per air permit, the RCTO can be taken down for 72 hours total annually over two scheduled maintenance events outside of ozone season. Microchip's total scheduled maintenance hours for 2022 to date are 26 hours and no other maintenance activities are scheduled for 2022.</td><td>11/02/2022</td><td>11/15/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This report details the scheduled maintenance event, which occurred on October 18-19, 2022. During this time period, the source bypassed their RCTO 20-2 Emission Control Device, to the atmosphere, for scheduled maintenance. The source reports this operation occurred for a total of 17 hours, and released approximately 85 pounds of Volatile Organic Compounds to the atmosphere. This report and the related maintenance activities are in compliance, as permit condition six and all other reporting requirements were satisfied during these procedures. 

Permit Condition 6.a.ii: 
2. This is the second of two allowable scheduled maintenance activities to be performed in the 2022 calendar year. 
3. This maintenance activity did not occur in the ground-level ozone season. 
4. The total duration of scheduled maintenance activities has not exceeded 72 hours. A total of 26 hours have been utilized for scheduled maintenance activities; nine hours in February 2022, and 17 hours in October 2022. 
5. Michael Aire, Environmental Manger, provided me with more than 7 days notice, via email, prior to commencing maintenance operations.</td></tr>
