<tr><td>CRPT005557</td><td>F001644</td><td>Northwest Regional Landfill</td><td>Title V</td><td>Landfills</td><td>CMP003877</td><td>Waste Management Arizona Landfills Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Second 2022 Compliance TV NSPS AAAA Rpt</td><td>10/27/2022</td><td>08/15/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semi-annual compliance report submitted for the reporting period from 01-Apr-22 to 30-Sep-22. The report was submitted in a timely manner on 27-Oct-22. The report covers the reporting requirements as part of Permit Condition 21 of the facility’s air quality permit, with notes as follows:


AREAS OF CONCERN

PC21.A.xi Surface Emissions Monitoring: Quarterly landfill surface emissions monitoring completed by Tetra Tech BAS from 02-Jun-22 to 08-Jun-22 (Q2) and from 22-Aug-22 to 26-Aug-22 (Q3). 
- Q2: The compliance report submitted by NW Regional noted that "all exceedances above 500ppm were corrected" and that the areas were re-monitored one month later and were measured to be below 500ppm. There was no record submitted in the compliance report showing these readings. The surface monitoring report submitted by Tetra Tech BAS did not show any exceedances, however on their monitoring summary page the facility was listed as "Butterfield Station LF." 

I discussed the issues with David Bearden, Senior Environmental Protection Manager, over the phone and Mr. Bearden confirmed that both issues were typos. Mr. Bearden confirmed the data and stated that there were no emissions for Q2 of 2022, and that the monitoring summary page matched the data for NW Regional. Mr. Bearden stated that he would have the typos corrected, and would send an updated compliance report to me. 

I received and reviewed the updated compliance report and found the information to be corrected. Both copies of the compliance report have been saved for reference.


SEMI-ANNUAL MONITORING REPORT

Report was reviewed with no issues observed for Permit Conditions 21.A.i – 21.A.x, and 21.A.xii – 21.A.xv, with notes as follows:

PC21.A.vi Emissions Report per PC18: Emissions report was attached in Appendix E.
- Facility wide 12-month rolling emissions:
-- VOC: 3.81tons(limit: 50tons)
-- CO: 84.34tons (limit: 225tons)
-- NOx: 18.09tons (limit: 85tons)
-- SOx: 2.38tons (limit: 25tons)
-- PM10: 21.89tons (limit: 30tons)
-- PM2.5: 5.62tons (limit: 30tons)
-- Single HAP: Toluene – 0.77tons(limit: 9tons)
-- Total HAPs: 1.39tons (20tons)


COMPLIANCE CERTIFICATION

Per the report, the facility was in continuous compliance with all permit conditions.</td></tr>
