<tr><td>CRPT005512</td><td>F001759</td><td>Gila River Power Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>7-Day Notice</td><td>In accordance with Rule 210, Section 403.2 of Maricopa County Air Quality Department (MCAQD) regulations, the purpose of this letter is to notify MCAQD of replacement of pollution control equipment at Gila River Power Station. SRP is replacing the drift eliminators in Cooling Tower #3. The new drift eliminators will have the same efficiency as those previously used. SRP estimates that the cooling tower will be returned to service on December 15, 2022.</td><td>10/18/2022</td><td>11/07/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>7-day notice does not include the new model number for the cooling towers drift eliminators. Equipment list in the permit (P0009164) does not need to be updated.</td></tr>
