<tr><td>CRPT005456</td><td>F002276</td><td>Insulfoam</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Plastics, Polymers, Fiberglass, Foam</td><td>CMP027601</td><td>Carlisle EPS Holding LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Revised 1st half 2022 Compliance Report. Due 10/11/22</td><td>10/10/2022</td><td>10/13/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Revised semiannual bead usage and VOC emissions report for the reporting period of 01-Jan-22 to 30-Jun-22. Revision was requested on 29-Sep-22 with a due date of 13-Oct-22. Specifically, the storage emissions loss calculations were corrected with updated storage emissions factors for mid-pentane and low-pentane beads using the last performance test verified emissions factors. Report was submitted in a timely manner on 11-Oct-22 and reviewed on 13-Oct-22.

The VOC emissions report contained the following information, as per Permit Condition 9:

a) 12-month rolling weight of EPS beads:
- Mid-pentane: 5,093,928lbs
- Low-pentane: 4,834,833lbs
b) 12-month rolling VOC emissions:
- Facility wide: 88.74tons (limit: 90tons)
- Per 100lbs of raw beads: 2.94lbs (limit: 3.0lbs)
c) Pressure differential averaged between 0.03 and 0.065
d) Per report, Permit Conditions 4 and 8.c were not met during the reporting period, however a violation had already been submitted through Performance Testing for these issues.
e) No excess emissions due to ECS failure during the reporting period.
f) Emissions loss factors as follows:
- Process Loss Emissions Factor: 34.2%
- Storage Loss Emissions Factor: 39.5%
- Grinding Loss Emissions Factor: 26.8%
g) 12-month rolling total NOx and CO emissions:
- NOx: 2.68tons
- CO: 0.88tons

Overall, VOC emissions totaled 88.74tons from Jul-21 to Jun-22, or 99% of their permit limits. I discussed the issue with Justin Ivy, Environmental Manager, and Scott Reddig, Consultant for Insulfoam and Mr. Reddig stated that the facility is aware of the limitations and is currently determining the best path forward to ensure the facility remains within permitting limits.

No issues of non-compliance observed upon review.</td></tr>
