<tr><td>CRPT005420</td><td>F000789</td><td>Microchip Technology - Tempe</td><td>Minor</td><td>Semiconductors and Electronics</td><td>CMP002193</td><td>Microchip Technology Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Notification</td><td>Notification of planned maintenance event on RCTO 20-2 allowed during non-ozone season.</td><td>10/05/2022</td><td>10/11/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This report details a scheduled maintenance event, planned to occur October 17, 2022. This report meets all the requirements outlined in the source's permit, specifically permit condition 6.a.ii:

1. The source estimates this bypass will cause 70 pounds of VOC emissions to be released to the atmosphere. This is approximately 0.09% of this source's VOC emission limit, per permit condition 1a. 

2. This is the second of two allowable scheduled maintenance activates per calendar year. 

3. This maintenance activity is scheduled to occur on October 17, 2022. This date is out of the ground level ozone season (May 1- September 30). 

4. The total duration of all scheduled maintenance activities appears to not exceed 72 hours, this calendar year. The first, on February 16, 2022 was proposed to last five hours. The second, on October 17, 2022 is proposed to last 10 hours. These yield 15 total hours of scheduled maintenance. 

5. A written notice was provided at least seven days in advance of performing the scheduled maintenance. The notice was received on October 5, 2022, and the maintenance is scheduled to occur on October 17, 2022.</td></tr>
