<tr><td>CRPT005364</td><td>F000015</td><td>Salt River Project - Kyrene Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Requested Source Records</td><td>With this submittal, Salt River Project (SRP) is providing the information requested during the inspection conducted by the Maricopa County Air Quality Department (MCAQD) at the Kyrene Generating Station (Kyrene), F000015, on September 12, 2022.  The requested documentation has been submitted via IMPACT.</td><td>09/26/2022</td><td>09/28/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This compliance report was requested as part of inspection report INSP169134, conducted on 12-Sep-22. The revised records request document was sent electronically on 12-Sep-22, with a due date of 26-Sep-22. The requested records were provided via this compliance report on 26-Sep-22. Records were reviewed from 28-Sep-22 to 03-Oct-22 and found to be in compliance.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT005363</td><td>F002681</td><td>SFPP-Phoenix Terminal</td><td>Title V</td><td>Petroleum Products Bulk Storage/Handling</td><td>CMP002921</td><td>SFPP LP</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Loading Rack 8 Excess Emissions Report 9-23-22</td><td>09/23/2022</td><td>09/26/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Excess emissions report due to loading rack incident on 21-Sep-22. Excess emissions report was submitted in a timely manner on 23-Sep-22. 

Per the report, excess emissions were created due to a transport truck driver with Tim Savage Trucking failing to properly disconnect the loading arms and vapor hoses from loading rack #8 on 22-Sep-22. The driver drove away while still connected, damaging the dry breaks on the loading arms and causing approximately 20gal of gasoline to spill onto engineered containment. SFPP estimates that the 20gal spill resulted in approximately 112lbs of VOC emissions, assuming 100% of the gasoline was evaporated. The report notes that the product was washed to an oil water separator and that the driver and truck are locked out of the facility until further investigation has been completed.

A Notice of Non-Compliance will be issued for the failure to prevent gasoline spillage by properly disconnecting the gasoline and vapor recovery hoses. See INSP172342 for further details.</td></tr>
