<tr><td>CRPT005292</td><td>F003184</td><td>UFP Chandler</td><td>Minor</td><td>Wood Products (Not Furniture)</td><td>CMP003416</td><td>UFP Chandler LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Notification</td><td>I am submitting a Non-TV Minor Modificaiton as part of my renewal applicaiton, not changing any equipemnt just asking for an increase in the sawdust limitation from 2900 tons rolling 12 mo to 3500 tons per rolling 12 mo.  Permit engineer is Courtney Medina.</td><td>09/01/2022</td><td>09/14/2022</td><td>No</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Modification submitted as P0009413</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT005291</td><td>F002813</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP000654</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>72 Hour Letter for Malfunction that occurred 8/28/22 at 1725.  Failed transmitter led to artificially high pressure readings.  This caused the #1 Bypass Stack to open.</td><td>09/01/2022</td><td>09/01/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>72 hour malfunction report and rolling emissions report</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT005290</td><td>F002813</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP000654</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Notice of malfunction that occurred 8/28/2022 at 1925.  Draft Transmitter failed, causing Bypass Stack #1 to open.</td><td>09/01/2022</td><td>09/01/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>24 hour notification of malfunction</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT005286</td><td>F002376</td><td>AIM Recycling Phoenix - McDowell Rd</td><td>Minor</td><td>Metal Recycling and Recovery</td><td>CMP022222</td><td>AIM Recycling Phoenix LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Two Reports are included -
     *EPA Method 9 - compliance demonstration - August 9, 2022 - 
          *Notified via CROMMER & Email - August 1, 2022
          *Two MCAQD employees on site for a.m. demonstration
          *No notable issues

      *Semiannual Explosions & Fire Report
            *January 1 2022 to June 30, 2022

Ty - Chris Buboltz - 602-394-7978 - Harrow Environmental</td><td>08/31/2022</td><td>09/13/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The facility has provided documentation showing the observers had EPA Method 9 Certification. The visible emissions observation forms show the emissions readings were taken at the right points of the facility and within the allowable limits.

The facility submitted this report within greater than 60 days. Another inspector had a copy of this report which was submitted to someone with the Maricopa County Air Quality Department but not submitted as a compliance report. They have been reminded the department requires their fire and explosion reports to be submitted within 60 calendar days. This fire and explosion report has times and days explosions and/or fires occurred, explanation of the incidents and suspected causes, and if the cause is unknown, the report indicated that the cause is unknown and corrective action taken. If no corrective action was taken, the report indicated that no corrective action was taken.

*I gave a phone call to the facility and requested some clarification on how the facility sets their automatic control system which regulates the water flow into the shredder depending on what the amperage of the motors are. 

*The facility submitted via email the proportions for water added to the shredder dependant on the type of material being sent through the shredder. It was explained that the water flow reading and the amperage being drawn has a slight lag and the recording equipment is slightly off. No issues observed.</td></tr>
