Sincerely,
Morgan R. Olsen
Executive Vice President, Treasurer and CFO</td><td>08/25/2022</td><td>08/26/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Per Permit Condition 6, the facility is required to submit Semi-Annual Emissions Reports. The report received is for the reporting period from January 1, 2022 - June 30, 2022. The due date for this report shows the facility has not exceeded its twelve month rolling total emissions and therefore demonstrated compliance with their current Maricopa County Air Quality Permit.The Air Quality Permit lists two sets of emissions limits. I gave a phone call to Mr. Ekren and he made clear the values listed in the report are for the facility as a whole which combines emissions from both operating scenarios.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT005258</td><td>F043218</td><td>KB-1 Aggregate Mine Site</td><td>Minor</td><td>Crushing and Screening, Stationary</td><td>CMP003733</td><td>Custom Landscape Materials LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Dust Control Plan</td><td>Rule 316 Dust Control Plan</td><td>08/25/2022</td><td>08/26/2022</td><td>No-Revision Requested</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The Plan cannot be approved at this time for the following reasons:

1.	Section 1b – document must be signed

2.	Section 2n – weed abatement
a.	Must select yes or no
b.	If selecting yes, then control measures must be selected for the relevant sections

3.	Section 2t – asphaltic concrete plants
a.	Must select yes or no
b.	If selecting yes, then entire section must be completed

4.	Section 2v(2) – soil moisture testing methods
a.	Speedy Moisture Meter has been selected
b.	If using the Speedy Moisture Meter, must indicate yes that all requirements have been met
c.	If using Speedy Moisture Meter, must attach required documents

5.	Section 2v(3) – soil moisture testing frequency
a.	Must select yes that all samples will be collected within one hour after startup
b.	Must select yes that samples will be collected within one hour before shutdown
c.	Must select yes that soil moisture samples will be collected at least once in every 8 hour period

6.	Section 2v(4) – soil moisture testing attachments
a.	Must attach process diagram
b.	Diagram must include all required information

7.	Section 2w(1) – reduction in sampling points
a.	Must select yes or no
b.	If selecting yes, must include a written request for approval

8.	Section 2w(2) – alternative minimum moisture content
a.	Must select yes or no
b.	If selecting yes, must include required explanations for approval from MCAQD and EPA

9.	Section 2w(3) – alternative moisture testing equipment or method
a.	Must select yes or no
b.	If selecting yes, must complete entire section

10.	Section 2x – dust suppressants
a.	Liquid Soil Cement has been selected
b.	Must include product specification information for product

11.	Section 2y – map
a.	Dust Control Plan will not be approved unless a map is submitted
b.	Must include property boundaries, nearest public cross roads with street names, identification of staging areas, areas for stockpiles, haul/access roads, storage and parking areas
c.	Identify paved areas and cohesive hard services
d.	Include exit locations
e.	Include north arrow
f.	Include disturbed areas/acreage

This document shall be uploaded as a compliance report into the AQD Online Portal on or before Friday, 02-Sep-2022.  There is no charge for submitting the document.</td></tr>
