One deviation was reported in the compliance report. Specifically, on 10-Jun-22 the AGET 9000 CFM baghouse broke down. Operations continued in the marble grinding booth with emissions venting to the indoor air wall dust collectors. Excess emissions from the operation were captured either through the air wall dust collectors or within the building itself. No excess emissions were released from the building and no visible emissions were observed from the baghouse malfunction. Per the report, the baghouse was repaired and returned to operation on 21-Jun-22. A notice of non-compliance was not issued as the deviation did not result in excess emissions. 

Overall no issues of non-compliance were observed in the compliance report.</td></tr>
