<tr><td>CRPT005119</td><td>F002681</td><td>SFPP-Phoenix Terminal</td><td>Title V</td><td>Petroleum Products Bulk Storage/Handling</td><td>CMP002921</td><td>SFPP LP</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>2022 1H Phoenix Semiannual & GDGACT Report Submittal</td><td>07/22/2022</td><td>08/15/2022</td><td>No-Revision Requested</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Compliance report submitted covering several semiannual compliance reports for the reporting period from 01-Jan-22 to 30-Jun-22. The compliance report was submitted in a timely manner on 22-Jul-22.

After review of the compliance report, I determined that several revisions will needed for the report. The changes reflect the excess emissions report submitted on 03-May-22 regarding the tank landing event in external storage tank P-49, as well as an issue with the permit conditions being used in the semiannual monitoring report.

Specifically, the document contains the following sections:

- A) Semiannual Certification Report – revision requested
- B) Semiannual Monitoring Report – revision requested
- C) Monitoring Summary Report
- D) Semiannual Subpart BBBBBB Compliance Report – revision requested

Sections A and D of the report did not properly reflect the excess emissions event for tank P-49, and therefore the following changes need to be made:

- Section A: the row regarding permit condition 23.c needs to be updated so that column 2 states “intermittent” instead of “continuous” and column 5 states “see note 3” instead of blank.

- Section D: the last row regarding 40 CFR Subpart 63.10(e)(3) needs to be updated to contain the phrase “see notes 2-4” rather than “see note 3” as both notes 2 and 4 relate to excess emissions events (2 being a non-reportable event and 4 being the 03-May-22 excess emissions event).

- Section B, the Semiannual Monitoring Report, will need to be entirely redone, as it appears the permit conditions being used in the report correspond to the previous permit version V95002 even though they are labeled as permit version P0008826. This is leading to none of the permit conditions lining up with the correct descriptions or requirements. The Semiannual Monitoring Report will need to be resubmitted with the permit conditions corresponding correctly. 

Since each of these sections are part of the same rejected document, they will all need to be resubmitted. This will not be cause for a notice of non-compliance, however, and the original submission date of 22-Jul-22 will be honored. Sections A, B and D will need a new signature from Bill Toepfer after the revisions have been made. Please resubmit the document as a new compliance report by 29-Aug-22.

Revised compliance report, CRPT005231, submitted on 16-Aug-22. See CRPT005231 for further details.</td></tr>
