<tr><td>CRPT004394</td><td>F001391</td><td>Allied Tube And Conduit</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Metal Fabrication</td><td>CMP000179</td><td>Allied Tube & Conduit Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Semi Annual VOC Report</td><td>07/15/2022</td><td>07/18/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semi-annual HAP emissions report for the period of 01-Jul-21 to 31-Dec-21. Semi-annual report was submitted per Permit Condition 4 of the air quality permit for the facility.

I reviewed the semi-annual report data and discussed the single HAP emissions, specifically Xylene, with Eric Eastwood, EHS Manager with Allied Tube and Conduit. After further review, it was confirmed that the data was correct and up to date. Per the report, HAP emissions for the period totaled 2.96tons (limit: 9tons). Emissions for single HAPs Xylene, HCl, and Chromic Acid were within single HAP limits (18,276lbs).

Compliance Report determined to be in compliance.


AREA OF CONCERN:

- Permit Condition 4: Emissions report must be submitted with 45 days of period ending.

The semi-annual report was officially received by Maricopa County Air Quality on 15-Jul-22, which would be outside of the 45 day limit outlined in Permit Condition 4. During the compliance report review, I noticed that the cover letter and data were uploaded to IMPACT on 31-Jan-22. Mr. Eastwood stated that the information was uploaded within the 45 day limit, however the final submission was not made in IMPACT due to user error. After discussion with my supervisor, it was determined that a Notice of Non-Compliance would not be issued due to the circumstances. However, please be advised that compliance reports must be properly submitted and received by Maricopa County Air Quality before the reporting date requirements in order to remain in compliance.</td></tr>
