<tr><td>CRPT004906</td><td>F000038</td><td>APS West Phx Power Plant</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP003677</td><td>Arizona Public Service Company</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>72-hour report for the APS West Phoenix Power Plant CC4 excess emission that occurred on 5/19/22.</td><td>05/20/2022</td><td>05/26/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Per section 48.f of the West Phoenix Title V Permit, APS submitted notification to provide Maricopa County Air Quality Department with detailed information regarding the excess emissions event that occurred on May 19, 2022, at I :48pm with the excess emission during the 0000-0059 hour of 5/19/22 from CC4. CC4 exceeded the NOx startup/shutdown permit limit of 87.7 lb/hr with a resultant value of 109.8 lb/hr (22.1lb/hr above the permit limit) as recorded by the facility CEMS/DAHS. 

While conducting a shutdown on the unit during the 0000 hour, the unit was taken to 40 MW to allow the steam turbine to come offline. During this time, the unit inadvertently came out of pre-mix load and entered the lean-lean mode which resulted in high NOx emissions at that load. 

The operator failed to immediately notice this abnormal event and did not take corrective actions in a timely fashion to reduce the NOx and avoid the exceedance. The unit was completely shutdown and no other exceedances occurred.

See inspection Report ID: INSP168539.</td></tr>
