<tr><td>CRPT004893</td><td>F000409</td><td>Coating Technologies</td><td>Minor</td><td>Metal Fabrication</td><td>CMP002753</td><td>Coating Technologies LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>O&M Plan</td><td>Bi-Annual Inspection May, 2020 - April, 2022
Process Control Document PCD-851-003 Rev 1 submitted per request. Section 1.10 Pertains to operation and maintenance of central dust collection system.</td><td>05/17/2022</td><td>05/26/2022</td><td>No</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The Department is in receipt of the Operations & Maintenance Plan submitted for Coating Technologies facility F000409.  Unfortunately, I am unable to approve this document and a new document is required to be submitted.

The document appears to be an SOP for the abrasive blasting operations.  However, an Operations & Maintenance Plan is strictly for the emission control system (the single external dust collector) that the process exhausts to.

The minimum acceptable operating parameters for a dust collection system is daily visible emissions and pressure drop.

Do not submit an O&M Plan for equipment or operations that does not require one.  The O&M Plan must include checklists/logs for operational checks (visible emissions, pressure drop) and preventative maintenance (emptying bins, filter replacement, system integrity checks, calibration of gauge, etc).  Operational checks and preventative maintenance must not only be performed, but recorded.

Tips and guidelines for preparing an O&M Plan may be located here:
https://www.maricopa.gov/1818/Permits-Forms-and-Payments

The Maricopa County Air Quality Department has transitioned to online permitting and payment processes.  MCAQD no longer accepts mailed or emailed applications, registrations, notifications, or payments.  These items must be processed directly through the appropriate MCAQD Online Portal.

Assistance with the AQD Online Portal:
AQDImpact@maricopa.gov
602-506-7833

The Department is pleased to offer a Business Assistance (BA) Program for the regulated community.  The purpose of the BA Program is to provide air quality information and technical assistance to business owners.  They offer permit application assistance, courtesy site visits, rule interpretation and education, and enforcement case review. BA Program may be reached at 602-506-5102 and/or AQbusinessassistance@maricopa.gov. 

The facility is required to upload an approvable O&M Plan on or before Friday, 03-Jun-2022.</td></tr>
