<tr><td>CRPT004844</td><td>F000047</td><td>Southeast Water Reclamation Plant</td><td>Minor</td><td>Wastewater Treatment Plants and Lift Stations</td><td>CMP000816</td><td>City of Mesa</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Dust Control Plan</td><td>The plant has completed a project to cover all exposed dirt at the plant  The letter describes what was added and includes a site map before and after.</td><td>05/02/2022</td><td>05/31/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The Permittee has decided to maintain a Rule 310 DCP instead of continuing with their request to terminate DCP due to improvements. This is because source contact has been informed of the definitions in Rule 310 for Routine and Dust Generating Operations.  The Permittee has submitted a revised Rule 310 DCP delineating areas that has been improved.</td></tr>
