<tr><td>CRPT004843</td><td>F000769</td><td>Pima Utility Company</td><td>Minor</td><td>Wastewater Treatment Plants and Lift Stations</td><td>CMP002532</td><td>Pima Utility Company</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>On March 31 2022 Pima Utility had an Air Quality Inspection. On that day we were given a notice of non compliance for not turning in a property fence line H2S monitor report in a timely manner.  I have attached a report for the H2S monitoring at the fence line on the property closest to the nearest residence and the dates of this test are 4/23/2020 - 4/27/2020.</td><td>05/02/2022</td><td>05/18/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Compliance report submitted on 02-May-22 as part of disposition for inspection report INSP166491. A notice of non-compliance was issued for failure to submit the compliance report in a timely manner. Specifically, permit condition 10.a requires the facility to maintain concentrations of H2S below 0.03 parts ppm, and permit condition 11 specifies the manner in which the concentration must be measured. The results of the test showed that the facility had a maximum H2S content of 17ppb and average of 6ppb (limit: 0.03ppm or 30ppb). The compliance report was reviewed and determined to be in compliance.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT004837</td><td>F001347</td><td>Southwest Regional Landfill</td><td>Title V</td><td>Landfills</td><td>CMP000180</td><td>Allied Waste Industries Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>Semi-Annual Compliance Report covering October 1, 2021 through March 31, 2022.  The report is due April 30, 2022.  The report contains the Semi-Annual Compliance Certification and the Semi-Annual Monitoring Report for the reporting period.</td><td>05/02/2022</td><td>11/27/2023</td><td>No-Revision Requested</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Review of the facility Semiannual Monitoring Report and Compliance Certification for time period October 1, 2021 - March 31, 2022.  Review of the compliance report was pending Maricopa County Air Quality Department’s delegation of authority of the federal plan for existing municipal solid waste landfills.

Environmental Protection agency(EPA) conducted a full compliance evaluation of the facility in April of 2022.  On October 12, 2022, EPA delivered their Findings and Notice of Violation to Southwest Regional Landfill.

On December 1, 2023, I contacted Jennifer Vera, Environmental Manager with Southwest Regional Landfill to request a revision to the Semiannual Monitoring Report and Compliance Certification to reflect the correct compliance status for facility permit conditions based on EPA's issuance of a Notice of Violation. 

Compliance Certification submitted was not consistent with the facility's current(expired) version of their Air Quality Permit.  Please use the current facility permit for the revision submittal of the Compliance Certification and include all applicable record documents for the monitoring report.</td></tr>
