<tr><td>CRPT004813</td><td>F001644</td><td>Northwest Regional Landfill</td><td>Title V</td><td>Landfills</td><td>CMP003877</td><td>Waste Management Arizona Landfills Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Title V Compliance Certification</td><td>April 2022 Semi-Annual NSPS AAAA Rpt</td><td>04/27/2022</td><td>08/15/2023</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semi-annual compliance report submitted for the reporting period from 01-Oct-21 to 31-Mar-22. The report was submitted in a timely manner on 27-Apr-22. The report covers the reporting requirements as part of Permit Condition 21 of the facility’s air quality permit, with notes as follows:


AREA OF CONCERN

Compliance Certification for Permit Condition 20.C: The facility notes that the Q4 quarterly emissions monitoring test was not completed for LFG Engine 2. Per the report, Engine 2 was out of service due to unexpected electrical issues at the time of Q4 monitoring. Per the emissions summary, the engine operated for 0hrs in Dec21. The semi-annual compliance certification section of the report did state "one missed quarterly report, see comment," however after discussion with my supervisor it was determined that a revision would be required to include "intermittent compliance" to keep in standing with EPA requirements.

I discussed the issue with David Bearden, Senior Environmental Protection Manager, over the phone and he confirmed that the maintenance was scheduled for Dec-21 and that the engine had malfunctioned prior to the maintenance inspection. Mr. Bearden confirmed that the engine was offline through the entire month of Dec-21. Mr. Bearden stated that he would submit an updated semi-annual compliance certification report to me to address the syntax issue.


SEMI-ANNUAL MONITORING REPORT

Report was reviewed with no issues observed for Permit Conditions 21.A.i – 21.A.x, and 21.A.xii – 21.A.xv, with notes as follows:

PC21.A.vi Emissions Report per PC18: Emissions report was attached in Appendix E.
- Facility wide 12-month rolling emissions:
-- VOC: 9.19tons(limit: 50tons)
-- CO: 203.14tons (limit: 225tons)
-- NOx: 48.92tons (limit: 85tons)
-- SOx: 6.64tons (limit: 25tons)
-- PM10: 15.39tons (limit: 30tons)
-- PM2.5: 15.39tons (limit: 30tons)
-- Single HAP: HCl – 1.14tons(limit: 9tons)
-- Total HAPs: 1.80tons (20tons)

PC21.A.xi Surface Emissions Monitoring: Quarterly landfill surface emissions monitoring completed by Tetra Tech BAS from 11-Nov-21 to 17-Nov-21 (Q4) and from 17-Mar-22 to 23-Mar-22 (Q1). 
- Q4: There were exceedances noted at the following locations: EW-118, CS-6, LCR-10, EW-30 (16-Nov-21), and LCR-8 (17-Nov-21). The areas were re-monitored on 24-Nov-21, with only LCR-10 exceeding a second time. LCR-10 was monitored again on 03-Dec-21 and determined to be below 500ppm. All exceedance locations were re-monitored on 15-Dec-21 and confirmed to be below 500ppm.
- Q1: No exceedances were noted during this monitoring event.


COMPLIANCE CERTIFICATION

Per the report, the facility was in continuous compliance with all permit conditions other than PC 20.C.</td></tr>
