<tr><td>CRPT004603</td><td>F006421</td><td>Resolute Performance Iron</td><td>Minor</td><td>Metal Fabrication</td><td>CMP021982</td><td>Resolute Performance Iron Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>November 4th 2021 to December 1st 2021</td><td>03/17/2022</td><td>03/28/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Annual Certification of Compliance Report for Resolute Performance Iron for the period between 04-Nov-21 to 31-Dec-21. This compliance report was submitted on 17-Mar-22, after request for revision to the compliance report, CRPT004269, submitted on 06-Jan-22.

I reviewed the documents submitted with the compliance report. 

The original compliance report was submitted on 06-Jan-22, which meets the requirement for Permit Condition 8.c.i.

The Cover Letter attachment meets the requirements for Permit Condition 8.c.ii. 

The Method 22 attachment contained Method 22 tests dating form 04-Nov-22 to 10-Dec-22. The tests were reviewed and found to be compliant, with no visible emissions observed during the tests. This qualifies Resolute Performance Iron to complete Method 22 tests on a monthly basis. Once 3 consecutive compliant monthly Method 22 tests have been completed, the facility may move to completing tests on a quarterly basis. The attachment also meets the requirements for Permit Condition 8.c.iii.  

As the Method 22 tests submitted were compliant, no Method 9 tests were required. Please be advised, if visible emissions are observed during a Method 22 test, Method 9 tests must be conducted by a Method 9 certified individual in accordance with Permit Condition 8.e. Due to these findings, Permit Conditions 8.c.iv, 8.c.v, and 8.c.vi do not apply.

Annual Certification of Compliance Report determined to be in compliance.</td></tr>
