<tr><td>CRPT004358</td><td>F003458</td><td>El Mirage Transmix Facility</td><td>Minor</td><td>Petroleum Products Bulk Storage/Handling</td><td>CMP001426</td><td>Fuel Processing Operators LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Submittal of the facility's semi-annual compliance report for the period pf July 1, 2021 through December 31, 2021.</td><td>01/28/2022</td><td>02/14/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Reviewed Semi-annual Compliance Report covering the period of July 1, 2021 through December 31, 2021.
Tanks 20-23 have not been yet installed.
CEMS Quarterly CGA's conducted and results provided as required.

According to the report:

On October, 16, 2021, the facility manager was made aware that the span gas bottle had a faulty pressure
valve which was later determined to be leaking. The facility replaced the span gas bottle pressure valve on
October 18, 2021, and the CEMS passed the calibration drift (CD) test after the repair was made. After
reviewing the CEMS data, it was determined that the daily CD checks were not valid dating back to October 6,
2021. Out abundance of caution the CEMS data starting on October 6 through October 18, 2021, has been
considered to be out of control. During this period there were no excess emissions.

On December 13, 2021, the facility manager was made aware that the zero gas bottle was empty. The facility
replaced the bottle with the extra bottle that is kept on hand and the CEMS unit passed CD test after the
bottles were switched out. After reviewing the CEMS data it was determined that the daily CD checks were
not valid dating back to December 12, 2021. Out abundance of caution the CEMS data starting on December
12 through December 13, 2021, has been considered to be out of control. During this period there were no
excess emissions.

No compliance issues reported or observed.</td></tr>
