Richard Maestas (Shop Manager)
01/01/2021-12/31/2021</td><td>01/06/2022</td><td>02/18/2022</td><td>No-Revision Requested</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Annual Certification of Compliance Report for Resolute Performance Iron for the period between 01-Jan-21 to 31-Dec-21. This is the first compliance report submitted by the facility after the transfer of the permit from Resolute Performance Contracting LLC to Resolute Performance Iron Inc.

After review of the compliance report, it was determined that Method 9 visible emissions tests were submitted, however the Method 22 visible emissions tests required by PC8(c)(iii) were not uploaded as part of the annual compliance report. I discussed the issue with Anastasia Valdez, Compliance Contact for Resolute Performance Iron, and Ms. Valdez stated that the tests were properly conducted but that they were unsure which tests were required to be submitted through the annual compliance report. I clarified the reporting requirements and stated that an amended compliance report would need to be submitted in order to determine compliance. I sent a request for revisions on 10-Mar-22, with a due date of 17-Mar-22.

I called Ms. Valdez on 17-Mar-22 to remind them of the due date for the compliance report. Ms. Valdez stated that the compliance is ready to upload, but they have been unable to submit it due to issues with the "Certifier" on the SCS portal. Ms. Valdez stated that they are working with the Business Assistance team to get a new Certifier confirmed so that they can submit the new report. I stated that I would provide an extension until 28-Mar-22 due to this and other logistics issues.

