<tr><td>CRPT004243</td><td>F001685</td><td>Southwest Asphalt</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Asphalt Plant, Portable</td><td>CMP001368</td><td>Fisher Sand & Gravel Co</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>O&M Plan</td><td>Attached is an updated O&M clarifying testing for the Blue Smoke, Lime and Drum Dryer Baghouse. Note:  In speaking with the manufacturer, there is no way to be able to test the blue smoke or lime silo baghouses due to how they operate. The only way to measure them is to do a Method 9. If dust was put into the blue smoke baghouse, the powder would stick to the residual oil on the bags and make it immediately inoperable and requiring the change of bags. As for the lime silo…the baghouse on top only receives pressure from the silo when it is being loaded with product due to the fact they use air pressure to fill. The silo receives upward pressure and airborne admix inside the silo during this process and only during this process. The bags catch this product and return it to the silo.</td><td>12/30/2021</td><td>01/04/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Reviewed and approved on 1/4/22.</td></tr>
