<tr><td>CRPT004223</td><td>F001461</td><td>Cave Creek Landfill</td><td>Minor</td><td>Soil Remediation Unit, Portable</td><td>CMP002086</td><td>Maricopa County</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Soil Vapor Extraction Unit Test Report</td><td>Quarter 4 CCL SVE system report. Due 12/24/2021</td><td>12/21/2021</td><td>01/10/2022</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Quarterly soil vapor extraction unit sampling results.

Performance Test conducted 11/17/21 for the fourth quarter of 2021. 

Test conducted by Wood Environment & Infrastructure Solutions, Inc., with additional lab reporting by AirTech Environmental Laboratories. Test was submitted on 12/21/21, within 30 days of test completion.

PERMIT CONDITIONS

1) Allowable Emissions: 
a.) Per report, twelve month rolling emissions totals are as follows:
- VOC: 709.2 lbs; limit: 6,397 lbs 
- HAPs: 5,002 lbs; limit: 6,979 lbs

7) Vapor Sampling Requirements:
a.) The following information was gathered as part of the soil vapor emissions (SVE) control unit test:
- i.) SVE samples were taken from the MW-09 and SVE-04 wells.
- ii.) Influent VOC concentration was determined to be 74.6 mg/m3 (29 ppmv) with effluent VOC concentration estimated to be 3.005 mg/m3 (1.0 ppmv). VOC removal efficiency determined to be 97%. Influent HAP concentration was determined to be 121 mg/m3 (28.5 ppmv) with effluent HAP concentration of 13.6 mg/m3 (12.5 ppmv). HAP removal efficiency determined to be 88.8%.
- iii.) Volumetric flow rate measured to be 925 ft3/min at time of testing.
c.iii.) Process temperature of 110 degrees Fahrenheit at time of testing.</td></tr>
