Rule 316 basic and comprehensive dust control training is now available online. Please see our new training website at https://mcaqd.learningcart.com/. 
 
To successfully register for a dust control certification course on our new training website, customers will be required to create an individual user account linked to their specific email address.  After successfully creating a user account, customers can then select and purchase the certification course that’s applicable to their companies work operations and their own job responsibilities.  
 
Dust control training certification cards may be located in the user account profile in the AQD Online Portal.  These are not mailed or emailed.
 
Assistance with dust control training:
AQTraining@maricopa.gov
602-372-1467
 
Assistance with the AQD Online Portal:
AQDImpact@maricopa.gov
602-506-7833
 
The Department is pleased to offer a Business Assistance (BA) Program for the regulated community.  The purpose of the BA Program is to provide air quality information and technical assistance to business owners.  They offer permit application assistance, courtesy site visits, rule interpretation and education, and enforcement case review. BA Program may be reached at 602-506-5102 and/or AQbusinessassistance@maricopa.gov.</td></tr>
