I verified the following four (4) O&M Plans are attached and the changes corrected deficiencies discovered during INSP162517.

O&M Plan CO-1803-01 was submitted with description "CO-1903-01 O&M Plan Updates" I telephoned Ms. Villegas who acknowledged this was errata.  I observed no issues with the submittal itself.

O&M Plan CO-1804-01 changes included a revised operating parameter for Lean Oil Temperature i.e. from '&lt; 93' to '&lt; 85'.  I telephoned Irma Villegas and Mike Hartzell and Mr. Hartzell stated this was errata i.e. the Lean Oil Temperature should have remained '&lt; 93'.

O&M Plan DC-0103-01 - no issues.

O&M Plan HX-1803-01 - no issues.

I emailed Ms. Villegas explaining the submittal will be rejected and to resubmit the plans (with the correction to CO-1804-01 as discussed) as an all new Compliance Report.

Status: CRPT004028: REJECTED resubmittal necessary.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT004031</td><td>F041847</td><td>MC#2</td><td>Minor</td><td>Crushing and Screening, Portable</td><td>CMP018050</td><td>Superstition Crushing LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Dust Control Plan</td><td>The Maricopa County Air Quality Department is in receipt of the Dust Control Plan submitted by Superstition Crushing for MC#5.  The Plan cannot be approved for the following reasons:

1.	Section 2i – trackout
a.	Facility does not utilize a gravel pad or a wheel wash system
b.	Must check P for primary measure and select pave and rumble grate
c.	Trackout and trackout control device responsibilities fall to all plants at a location and the Dust Control Plan must match the current scenario
2.	Section 2s – crushing and screening
a.	There is no wet plant for Superstition Crushing
b.	Must select “no”

Please revise the above items and upload all attachments as one compliance report in the AQD Online Portal on or before Friday, 19-Nov-2021.

