<tr><td>CRPT003987</td><td>F039408</td><td>Fire Fighting Instruction</td><td>Open Burn</td><td>Not Applicable</td><td>CMP000816</td><td>City of Mesa</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Administrative Change</td><td>Patricia Hawkins with City of Mesa submitted a Presumptive Permission to Burn for a fire training exercise on Wednesday, November 3rd from 1700-2100 hrs.</td><td>11/02/2021</td><td>11/02/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Patricia Hawkins with City of Mesa submitted a Presumptive Permission to Burn for a fire training exercise on Wednesday, November 3rd from 1700-2100 hrs.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT003985</td><td>F001759</td><td>Gila River Power Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Gila River Power Station (GRPS) has an Aboveground Storage Tank (AST) of 250-gallon capacity for gasoline. This gasoline storage tank meets the definition of insignificant activity defined in MCAQD Rule 100, Section 200.61.k. However, GRPS is required under 40 CFR Part 63.11116.b to calculate and document monthly throughput.  During the previous 4 reporting periods GRPS was under the assumption that the gasoline tank was not in service with zero throughput.  GRPS later discovered that the AST was placed back into service in September of 2019.  By the time of the discovery, GRPS had incorrectly reported the status and throughput of the AST in the Semiannual Monitoring and Compliance Certification Report for October 1, 2019 – March 31, 2020.

As per GRPS Title V permit condition 16.c.ii, GRPS has logged the permit deviation into the facility records and is resubmitting the Semiannual Monitoring Report and Compliance Certification for the reporting period stated above.</td><td>11/01/2021</td><td>11/09/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Permit Condition 21. Reporting Requirements, Section: a.vii states that required semiannual monitoring reports and compliance certifications shall contain the summary of the monthly and 12-month rolling total records of gasoline delivered. See Inspection Report -  INSP163890</td></tr>
