No odor complaints received in reporting period.

2,311 total gallons of gasoline received during reporting period. Gasoline throughput limitations of Permit Condition 19.E.I. were not exceeded.

No hydrogen sulfide monitoring test was performed within reporting period. Zero odor complaints were received, so a monitoring test was not triggered as required by Permit Condition 20.C.I.

Emissions report, including calculations and date, included in Appendix B. No Permit Condition 18.A. emission exceedances recorded.

No 40 CFR § 60.756 reportable exceedances noted. Monitoring records provided in Appendix C.

Gas stream diversion is not incorporated into the design of control devices. No gas stream diverted from control devices during reporting period.

Three failures over 1 hour. P.3 of Report P. 25 of Permit. Reportable time limits were not exceeded.

There were zero instances which the collection system was not operational for an excess of five days. Well Monitoring Report included in Appendix C, and closed well tables included in Appendix F.

Monitoring records included in Appendix D show no exceedances of 500 ppm surface methane were recorded during this reporting period. Device calibration records also provided in Appendix D.

Well collection system SR85 LVL 13 Horizontal Collector HC-1-4A-13 installed during reporting period, July 2021. Addition includes three collector pipes, 13A, 13B, 13C. Location included in Appendix E.

Actions taken were consistent with the approved SSM Plan, so no reports were required. 

Report Section 13: Pavement striping performed. An SDS is included in Appendix B, and VOC emissions from paint used included in semiannual emission calculations. Permit Condition 21.E. satisfied.

No issues noted.

Review of the facility compliance report was pending Maricopa County Air Quality Department’s delegation of authority of the federal plan for existing municipal solid waste landfills.</td></tr>
