<tr><td>CRPT003921</td><td>F000015</td><td>Salt River Project - Kyrene Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>72-Hour Excess Emissions Report - Unit K7 excess emissions of the NOx lb/hr startup limit in the 1000 hour on October 16.</td><td>10/20/2021</td><td>10/22/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This report was generated as a result of a self-reported violation of SRP Kyrene Generating Station permit condition 18.a.ii. Table 3 of permit condition 18.a.ii states that the hourly emission limit for combined cycle system K-7 during periods of startup, shutdown and tuning and testing shall not exceed 162.0 lb/hr. The report provided to MCAQD reports an emission of 188.2 lb/hr for the 10:00 hour of October 16, 2021 during unit K-7 startup. This constitutes a violation of permit condition 18.a.ii. 

This report was provided to MCAQD in a timely manner pursuant to permit condition 16 of the active air quality permit.</td></tr>
