<tr><td>CRPT003864</td><td>F000220</td><td>Rogers Corporation - Roosevelt Ave Facility</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Semiconductors and Electronics</td><td>CMP002773</td><td>Rogers Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Quarterly Subpart VVV report for the period from July 1, 2021 to September 30, 2021.</td><td>10/07/2021</td><td>10/22/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This quarterly Subpart VVV Report was submitted to MCAQD in a timely manner. This report documents that there were no reportable instances that occurred a the facility during the reporting period of July 1 - September 30 2021.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT003838</td><td>F001684</td><td>Fisher Sand & Gravel</td><td>Minor</td><td>Asphalt Plant, Portable</td><td>CMP001368</td><td>Fisher Sand & Gravel Co</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Test Report</td><td>Baghouse black light test corrected per MCAQD review and placed under the proper permit.</td><td>10/07/2021</td><td>10/13/2021</td><td>No</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semi-annual black light testing conducted on 23-Jul-2021.

The drum dryer is exhausted to an Almix Model 80 KRA baghouse with 80,000 cfm.

Run 1 was performed at 12:30am using 2 lbs of fluorescent powder. The result was 7 bags replaced.
Run 2 was performed at 2:30 am also using 2 lbs of fluorescent powder.

Per section 19 of the associated permit conditions:
As an alternative to the annual performance test the permittee shall perform a black light test on the drum dryer baghouse every 5 to 7 months.  The baghouse black light test shall be performed according to the procedure provided by the baghouse manufacturer, and such procedure shall be incorporated in the Operations & Maintenance Plan.

Per the submitted report and the approved O&M Plan, the surface area of the cloth is 16,243 square feet.  The amount of fluorescent powder utilized should be 1 pound per 1,000 square feet of cloth.  Based on the dimension of the bags and the quantity of bags, 16 pounds of powder should be used.  However, only 2 pounds of fluorescent powder was used.

The Maricopa County Air Quality Department will be declining to issue a notice of non-compliance at this time for failing to use the appropriate amount of powder during black light testing.

However, performing the black light test again using the correct amount of fluorescent powder will be required on or before Wednesday, 10-Nov-2021.

Additionally, the Department will be requiring the facility to submit a new and complete Operations & Maintenance Plan to incorporate the procedure for performing the alternative compliance determination.  The revised Operations & Maintenance Plan will also be due on or before Wednesday, 10-Nov-2021.  All hot mix asphalt plants that operate in Maricopa County and conduct black light testing will be required to complete this action item if the test procedure is not already a part of their Operations & Maintenance Plan on file.

The Department is pleased to offer a Business Assistance (BA) Program for the regulated community.  The purpose of the BA Program is to provide air quality information and technical assistance to business owners.  They offer permit application assistance, courtesy site visits, rule interpretation and education, and enforcement case review. BA Program may be reached at 602-506-5102 and/or AQbusinessassistance@maricopa.gov.</td></tr>
