<tr><td>CRPT003858</td><td>F001522</td><td>Mesquite Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP002166</td><td>Mesquite Power LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Requested Source Records</td><td>With this submittal, Salt River Project (SRP) is providing the information requested during the inspection conducted by the Maricopa County Air Quality Department (MCAQD) at the Mesquite Generating Station (MQGS) on September 21, 2021. 

Attachment 1. (18.1)	12 Month Rolling Total Emissions
This attachment contains records for 12-month rolling total emissions for CO, PM10, SO2 and VOC from each block (Block #1 and #2 individually) and 365 day rolling total emissions for NOx from each block for the specified dates.  The 12-month rolling total PM emissions from the cooling towers for the specified dates are also included with this attachment.

Attachment 2. (Table 18.2)	Hourly Emissions
Hourly emissions for Units 1, 2, 5 and 6 for the specified inspection period are included in this attachment.  These records demonstrate compliance with Table 18.2 for normal operations and Table 18.5 for periods of startup, shutdown, tuning and testing.

Attachment 3 (18.3)	 3-hour Rolling Average Emissions
Reports for Units 1, 2, 5, and 6 are attached demonstrating three-hour rolling averages for NOx and CO during normal operations for the dates specified.

Attachment 4. (Table 18.5)	Hourly Emissions
Hourly emissions for Units 1, 2, 5 and 6 during periods of startup, shutdown, tuning and testing for the specified inspection period are included in attachment 2.  

No instances of tuning and testing occurred during the specified dates.

Attachment 5 (18.6)	Cooling Tower Emissions
Hourly PM10 emissions from the cooling towers for the dates specified are included in this attachment.  

Attachment 6 (19.b.ii.2), 7 (19.b.ii.3), 8 (20.a.i.4), and 9 (20.a.ii.5)  Normal and Extended Startup Duration
Records for the 10 longest normal startups and all extended startups for the specified inspection period are included in this attachment.  There were no normal startups that exceeded 5 hours and no extended startups that exceeded 8 hours.

Attachment 10 (19.b.ii.6), 12 (19.b.ii.8), and 14 (19.a.i.7) Tuning and Testing Records  
There was one instance of Tuning and Testing during the inspection period.  On May 12, 2021, Unit 6 Stack was placed in Tuning/Testing mode.  Emissions remained within the limitations for normal operation mode (Table 18.2) as well as the Startup/Shutdown/Tuning/Testing limits (Table 18.5).  A daily compliance report for May 12, 2021 for Unit 6 is included in this attachment.

Attachment 11 (19.b.ii.7) Multiple Gas Turbines in Startup/Shutdown and Tuning/Testing
During the inspection period, no combustion turbines were operating in startup while an additional combustion turbine was undergoing tuning or testing.

Attachment 13 (20.a.i.6) Steam Turbine Reheat Bowl Temperature
Records for the steam turbine reheat bowl temperature prior to each unit startup for the dates specified are included in this attachment.

Attachment 16 (20.a.i.9) Natural Gas Combustion
Records of the hourly natural gas combustion for each Combined Cycle System for the dates specified are included in this attachment.

Attachment 17 (20.a.i.10) Gross Electrical Energy Output
Records of the hourly gross electrical energy output for each combustion turbine and steam turbine for the dates specified are included in this attachment.

Attachment 15, 18, 19, 20 (20.a.i.8, 20.a.ii.8, 20.a.ii.9, 20.a.ii.10) Malfunction(s) of CEMS, CC Systems or Air Pollution Control Devices
