<tr><td>CRPT003796</td><td>F000320</td><td>AGC Multi Material America.</td><td>Minor</td><td>Semiconductors and Electronics</td><td>CMP002290</td><td>AGC Multi Material America Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>F-55 Carbon Adsorption System - Quarterly Test Report: 2021 Quarter 3 July 1 - September 30 2021</td><td>09/17/2021</td><td>10/21/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>SVE unit sampling results. 
I used the Permit Conditions with an expiration date of 8/31/2021 to review the compliance report. The renewal Permit Conditions have not been issued yet in Impact.
 
Permit Condition 10. Vapor Sampling Requirements for F-55 Series Carbon Vapor Absorber: a. The Permittee shall test the F-55 Series Carbon Vapor Absorber to demonstrate compliance with these Permit Conditions: i. The Permittee shall take representative grab samples of the gases entering and exiting the carbon
adsorption system upon startup and then once every two weeks for the first six weeks, then monthly for the following six months, then quarterly thereafter.

The time frame submitted for this report was July 2021 - September 2021.

The sampling and submittal date was 9/17/2021.

F-55 CARBON ADSORPTION SYSTEM:

Sampling was performed with photoionization detector (PID) by AGC.

Permit Condition 10. a. iv. The PID shall be calibrated using isobutylene but any absolute ppmv measurement shall be correlated and expressed as hexane.

The report states the absolute ppmv measurements shall be correlated and expressed as hexane. Hexane Correction Factor (CF) = 4.3. PID Calibration Correction Factor (CF) = 1.04. 

Permit Condition 10. c. Test Report Submittal: The Permittee shall complete and submit a separate test report for each test to the Control Officer within 30 days after the completion of testing. The report shall include, at a minimum for each grab sample:
i. Date of sampling, type of air pollution control in use, and the name of the company performing the laboratory analyses;
ii. Actual volumetric flow rate of the gases exiting the carbon adsorption system; and
iii. Process temperature of the carbon adsorption system (°F).
iv. The concentration of VOC at the inlet and outlet of the carbon adsorption system (ppmv);
v. The emission rate of VOC exiting the carbon adsorption system (lb/hr);
vi. The VOC removal efficiency for the carbon adsorption system.

Permit Condition 5.b.iv. 3) The carbon adsorption system shall achieve at least a 95% VOC removal efficiency demonstrated in by the method in Condition 10.a.

Results submitted:
Flow Rate (CFM): 36.6
Process Temp. (°F): 86
Inlet VOC (ppmv): 783.5
Outlet VOC (ppmv): 25
Emission Rate (lb/ hr): 0.012
Removal Efficiency (%) (1- VOC out/ VOC in) *100 = 96.8%</td></tr>
