<tr><td>CRPT003718</td><td>F000763</td><td>Arizona State University Tempe Campus</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Institutions - Public/Government</td><td>CMP000336</td><td>Arizona State University</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>August 25, 2021

Hanna Valenzuela
Compliance and Enforcement Division Manager
Maricopa County Air Quality Department 
3800 N. Central Ave., Suite 1400
Phoenix, AZ 85004

RE:	Semiannual Emission Report, Air Permit No. 960886, Facility ID No.000763
	Reporting Period – January 1, 2021, through June 30, 2021

Arizona State University (ASU) is submitting the attached semiannual nitrogen oxide (NOx) and carbon monoxide (CO) emission report for the Tempe Campus.  As required by Permit Condition 6, the report contains monthly and 12-month rolling total emission rates for the Tempe Campus during the period from January 1, 2021, through June 30, 2021.

We discovered an error in our calculation for the Combined Heat and Power Expansion Turbine emissions during the CO and NOx emissions report review.  Additionally, we have updated the approved emissions factors for the Combined Heat and Power Expansion Turbine with the approved emissions factors from the July 9, 2019 performance test. Therefore, ASU is providing corrected emissions data for your review beginning with January 2020.  Emissions are compliant with the ASU Tempe Campus permit limits.

Thank you for your consideration.  If you have any questions, please call me at 480-965-1893.

Sincerely,
 Suzanne Kennedy
Associate Director, Safety in the Built Environment</td><td>08/26/2021</td><td>09/01/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This report was submitted to MCAQD in a timely manner. The report indicates that the maximum twelve month rolling throughput for CO and NOx was 30740 lbs in and 55,443 in April of 2020, respectively. These values are within the compliance limits provided in the air quality permit.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT003716</td><td>F003666</td><td>NXP Semiconductors</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Semiconductors and Electronics</td><td>CMP004395</td><td>NXP USA Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Submital of Emission Inventory to Compliance</td><td>08/25/2021</td><td>08/26/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>On 26-Aug-2021; I reviewed the source emissions report required by PC 12.a. and verified the reported emissions met the limits in PC 1. as follows:
I compared the totals provided to the Allowable Emissions in PC 1 as follows:
POLLUTANT         PC1 LIMIT (tons/yr)     2019-12-mo EMISSIONS (tons/yr) (rounded)
CO                             30                                               11
NOx                           24                                               18
SOx                             1.25                                            0.18
PM10                         14.8                                              4.6
PM2.5                        14.8                                              0.9
VOC                           49                                               17
Total HAPS                18                                                 3
Single HAP                  7.5                                              1.8 (Hydrogen Fluoride)

All emissions within the PC 1 allowable emission limits.

I telephoned and informed facility's Compliance Contact, Peggy Felice of the following area of concern:

AREA OF CONCERN [Rule 220 §503; PC 12.a.]: which, in summary requires this particular emissions
         report to be submitted by the same due date each year as the annual emissions inventory report.
          • The 2020 annual emissions inventory report due date was 30-Apr-2021.
          • This report's submittal was more than 3 months late.

End report.</td></tr>
