Good morning Mr. Deering,

I am in receipt of the Rule 316 Dust Control Plan submitted for Core Ready Mix located at 8050 S Jackrabbit Trail.  Unfortunately I am unable to approve this Plan for the following reasons:

1.	Section 1b – no signature
2.	Sections 2a, 2b – must select primary and contingency control measures
3.	Section 2h(1) – must select contingency control measure
4.	Section 2h(2) – must select primary and contingency control measures
5.	Section 2h(3) – must select contingency control measure

Please complete a new Rule 316 Dust Control Plan and upload into the AQD Online Portal on or before Friday, 03-Sep-2021.

https://www.maricopa.gov/DocumentCenter/View/24934/Rule-316-Dust-Control-Plan-PDF

The Department is pleased to offer a Business Assistance (BA) Program for the regulated community.  The purpose of the BA Program is to provide air quality information and technical assistance to business owners.  They offer permit application assistance, courtesy site visits, rule interpretation and education, and enforcement case review. BA Program may be reached at 602-506-5102 and/or AQbusinessassistance@maricopa.gov.   

Thank you,</td></tr>
