<tr><td>CRPT003665</td><td>F002813</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP000654</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>72 Hour notice of Environmental Malfunction that occured on 8/15/2021 at 17:17.  Power was suspended by power company for 9 minutes.  After power was restored, equipment was started as quickly as possible to minimize emissions.</td><td>08/16/2021</td><td>08/20/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Emissions occurred at the #1 and #2 bypass stacks.

The event occurred on 15-Aig-2021 from 1717 to 1817 hours.

Malfunction due to power outage from unknown reasons. Loss of power caused all flames to go out and the bypass stacks to open. It was later determined that the power outage was caused from the power company suspending power due to repairs in the area. 

The feed was stopped when plant power was lost. The equipment was quickly restarted to allow the bypass stacks to be closed.

Per the source, the malfunction did not cause emissions to exceed limits.</td></tr>
