Test Date: 7/1/2021
Failed Run 2 leak check, additional test run completed for Cyclone 1a.  Impinger exit temperature TC stopped working during testing.
Cyclonic flow check not completed for Cyclone 3a.  This stack previously tested as Cyclone 2 in 2013 and passed cyclonic check.</td><td>08/10/2021</td><td>12/20/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>N/A</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT003648</td><td>F002813</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP000654</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Attached is the 72 hour letter for the malfunction that occured at 00:38 on 8/08/2021.  Process conditions caused natural gas pressure to rise above safety limit switch and gas was shut off.  Once flame was lost, bypass stacks opened.  Maintenance was called in to investigate issue.  Feed was stopped via interlock.</td><td>08/09/2021</td><td>08/12/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Equipment involved: #1 kiln to #1 bypass and #2 kiln to #2 bypass

Occurrence: 08-Aug-2021 from 0038 to 0238 hours

Cause: The product being ran on #1 kiln caused blockage in the feed system. While blockages were being cleared, temps were fluctuating throughout the system. The temperature in the thermal oxidizer was rising. To compensate, the gas valve closed leading to an excess of gas pressure. The high pressure switch caused the gas safety valves to shut and the flame in the thermal oxidizer was lost. This in turn caused both bypass stacks to open.

Corrective action: Gas pressure regulator was adjusted to allow some variation in pressure before the high pressure switch was tripped. Going forth, the the poor product will be blended to avoid blockages.

Emissions due to malfunction event:
SO2 - 0
NOX - 0.03 lbs
CO - 8.03 lbs
VOC - 0.01 lbs
PM - 3.00 lbs
HCl - 0.04 lbs

Source is to include emissions from malfunction events in rolling emissions report.</td></tr>
