Permit Condition 10. a. The Permittee shall submit a bi-annual emission report to the department. The report shall include the following information:
i.  Hours of operation of each engine.
ii. The maximum output kW load placed on the generators during each run.
iii. For each run: The total time the engine is operated and the amount of time at which the engine exhaust is less than 572 ºF.
iv. The emission factors and 12-month rolling total emissions of NOx and CO.

Permit Condition 10. a. i. The hours of operation for each engine were submitted in Tables 5.a - 5.r.
Tables 5a. and 5b. were partially cut off in the bi-annual report.

Permit Condition 10.a. ii. The maximum output kW load placed on the generators during each run was recorded in Tables 5.a - 5.r.

Permit Condition 10.a. iii. For each run: The total time the engines were operated and the amount of time when the engines exhaust was less than 572 ºF were included in Tables 5.a - 5.r.

Permit Condition 10.a. iv. The reported NOx emissions for group 1, 2, 3 and 4 fire pumps were reported at 0.03 tons. The reported NOx emissions for engines 5, 6 and 7 were reported at 2.15 tons. These are less than the allowable emissions in Permit Condition 1.a. 
The reported CO emissions for group 1, 2, 3 and 4 fire pumps were reported at 0.01 tons. The reported CO emissions for engines 5, 6 and 7 were reported at 0.48 tons. 
I also reviewed the last bi-annual report for the NOx emissions numbers.
The emission factors were included in the bi-annual report.

This report was submitted within 30 days of the end of the reporting period.</td></tr>
