<tr><td>CRPT003569</td><td>F002470</td><td>New Wincup Holdings</td><td>Title V</td><td>Plastics, Polymers, Fiberglass, Foam</td><td>CMP002307</td><td>New Wincup Holdings Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>O&M Plan</td><td>O&M Plan</td><td>07/23/2021</td><td>11/01/2022</td><td>No</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This July 23, 2021 version [CRPT003569] of the O&M Plan followed my June 8, 2021 rejection of previous plan [CRPT000429] dated January 10, 2020.

Acronyms in this report:
DAQ (Data Acquisition System)
PRS (Pentane Recovery System)

This review was deferred because of the disposition of the facility's current control system was undecided.

This particular version is being rejected for the following deficiencies:

[1] This version includes a daily monitoring ([PC 21.c.ix] requires monthly at a minimum) for ensuring compliance with [PC 20.a.ii.]. However, the daily work sheets limit the monitoring to the boilers, not the required evaluation of the entire PRS. The subject O&M Plan omits the main trunk of the PRS from the O&M Plan which according to PC 21.c.ix.(1) requires a monthly inspection. The subject O&M Plan submittal omits a monthly inspection but retains the inspections of the PRS limited to each particular boiler component in the Daily, Monthly, and Semi-Annual PM Logs. The inspection which is required by PC 21.c.ix.(1) is applicable to the whole PRS, from the boilers to all the common ductwork upstream.

[2] During previous 2021 inspection I observed boiler firebox temperatures commonly recorded in the DAQ reports at 2,498°F and never above this temperature.  Previous on-site inspection observations observed temperatures which exceeded this 2,498°F. I have also observed records of 2,498°F in the DAQ reports while a respective boiler is logged as off in correlating daily records.
It is likely a malfunctioning thermocouple contributes to this and warrants inspection and testing of the thermocouple to ensure it is working. i.e. In summary: your facility's thermocouple does not record temperatures which exceed 2,498°F; and the thermocouples report 2,498°F both when temperature exceeds 2,498°F and sometimes when the boiler is off. The subject O&M Plan omits thermocouple inspection and testing. The subject O&M Plan omits verification the thermocouple is functioning properly-- the failure of which may go undiscovered indefinitely with potential result in PRS damper remaining open when boiler is below minimum temperature or turned off.

[3] Facility has recently replaced the damper control system. Ensure the new O&M Plan is congruent with the needs of the new system.
------------------------------------

Following updates requested:
(1) Update O&M Plan with required monitoring record ensuring the entire PRS is monitored at least monthly according to PC 21.c.ix.(1).
(2) Update upper temperature of boilers to less than 2,498°F; or equip thermocouple device which records temperatures which exceed 2,498°F. In the former; a temperature of exactly 2,498°F should trigger a maintenance action.
(3) Update requested: Expected permit modification warrants a new O&M Plan.

Submit the new O&M Plan as a compliance report in the department's online user portal A due date for the new O&M Plan is December 30, 2022.</td></tr>
