Permit Condition 5.b. requires the cutting cycle duration for each silicon block as well as the monthly and 12-month rolling total of silicon blocks cut during the preceding 12 calendar months, this information was not provided in the report.
August 26, 2021:
Email sent to Brian Beetso, the EHS Specialist for SUMCO Southwest Corporation, to request information regarding the cutting cycle duration for each block cut.
August 27, 2021:
Mr. Beetso resubmitted the HAPS report, however the information regarding duration for each block was not clear.
I called Mr. Beetso regarding the information provided in the resubmitted report and he said he would get more information and send me an email with an explanation.
August 16, 2021:
I did not receive clarification regarding the information provided in the report.
I sent Mr. Beetso an email and asked him to provide the information by the end of the day on August 17, 2021.
August 17, 2021:
Mr. Beetso provided an a detailed explanation to show the cutting time of 10 hours per block was not exceeded
(Please see attached email)
Mr. Beetso will provide this information in the HAPS reports going forward.</td></tr>
