<tr><td>CRPT003319</td><td>F038518</td><td>A.B.C. Sand & Rock Co..</td><td>Minor</td><td>Crushing and Screening, Stationary</td><td>CMP015311</td><td>A B C Sand & Rock Company Incorporated</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Test Report</td><td>The Department is in receipt of the visible emission test submitted by A.B.C. Sand & Rock Co located at 5401 N 119th Ave for Maricopa County Air Quality facility F038518.  The submitted test has been rejected for the following reasons:

1.	Method 9 requires a test duration of 30 minutes (five 6 minute averages)
a.	Only a single 6 minute run was conducted for each of the required locations – crusher, screen, material transfer points
b.	Per Method 9: When determining compliance with the fugitive emissions standards the duration of the Method 9 observations shall be 30 minutes (five 6 minute averages). Compliance with the applicable fugitive dust emission limits shall be based on the average of the five 6 minute averages.
c.	Refer to section 6 of your permit conditions.
d.	This will require a re-test within two weeks and a 7 day advance notification shall be submitted
e.	Each 30 minute period requires a separate observation form

2.	Observation forms not completed
a.	Must select method used
b.	Must complete angle, distance, etc sections instead of “N/A”
c.	Must complete source layout sketch
d.	Must include copy of observer’s Method 9 certification with report

Additional information regarding EPA Method 9 may be located here:
https://www.epa.gov/emc/method-9-visual-opacity 

