<tr><td>CRPT003238</td><td>F002140</td><td>Arizona State University Polytechnic Campus</td><td>Minor</td><td>Institutions - Public/Government</td><td>CMP000270</td><td>Arizona Board Of Regents</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>7-Day Notice</td><td>Dear Mr. Martin:
This letter is to request a change to the permitted equipment list included in the Polytechnic Campus Air Quality Permit. The requested change is for a boiler replacement project at the Polytechnic Campus Academic Center building. One AJAX WG-525 natural gas boiler, rated at 0.525 MMBtu/hr, will be removed and replaced with a gas boiler. The new gas boiler is a Lochinvar FTXL model FTX500 rated at 0.5 MMBtu/hr. The AJAX boiler is identified in the Maricopa County Air Impact system as BOL014, PRC014.

Additionally, a piece of de minimis fuel-burning equipment will be replaced with another piece of de minimis equipment. An AO Smith water heater, rated at 75,100 BTU/hr, will be replaced with a Navien NPE-240A tankless water heater, rated at 199,000 BTU/hr.

Potential emissions from regulated pieces of equipment for the campus will be reduced, as demonstrated in Attachment 1. There is no request to change current emission limits or permit conditions. Attachment 2 includes manufacturer data for the new equipment.

Thank you, in advance, for your consideration. If you have any questions or need any additional information, please contact me at 480-965-1893 or 602-460-8173.

Sincerely,
Suzanne M. Kennedy
Associate Director
Safety in the Built Environment</td><td>05/17/2021</td><td>06/02/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Equipment description for BOL014 updated in IMPACT.</td></tr>
