[pc 21.B.I.] Visible Emission Observations: COMPLIANT - except for the following area of concern:
                   AREA OF CONCERN [pc 21.b.I.(6)]; which, in summary omits the company/agency providing
                                                                                  the (Method 9) certification to the certified individual.

[pc 21.B.II.] Odor Complaint Log - COMPLIANT

[pc 21.B.III.] Gasoline Monthly Throughput Limits: Required certification present. - COMPLIANT

[pc 21.B.IV.] Statement included per pc 21.B.IV.(7). - COMPLIANT

[pc 21.B.V.] The required emissions report demonstrates compliance with pc 18.A.  However, the Department
                     would be grateful for a more "on the nose" demonstration in subsequent Semiannual Monitoring
                     Reports which do not require the reader to mine for the target values and perform the calculations
                     themselves.
                       SR85 Landfill Flare Emissions: - COMPLIANT
                       VOC: 5+39+53 (97 lbs) 
                       NOx:  479+2463+869 (3811 lbs) 
                       HCl:   11+68+20 (99 lbs)
I emailed Mr. Sawyer requesting a written explanation to supplement this particular report explaining the disparity of LandGEM data values for Accepted Waste between current semiannual report and past two semiannual reports.

[pc 21.B.VI.] No exceedances to report. - COMPLIANT - AREA OF CONCERN follows:

AREA OF CONCERN [40 CFR 60.753(c)]; which, in summary, states; Operate each wellhead in the collection
                                                                       system with a landfill gas temperature less than 55°C. et al.
• The Appendix C; 10-Mar-2021 Gas Well Monitoring Report shows Well ID Number HC-136AE Gas
   Temperature was measured at 130.8°F which is 54.9°C.
• There is no distinction between 54.9°C and 55°C when reduced to the significant figures specified in the
   standard. I recommend corrective actions prescribed by §60.755 be employed when the Gas Temperature
   reaches 55°C.

[pc 21.B.VII.] Facility reports no bypass lines are incorporated into the design of the Flare Gas Handling Skid.
                       I infer this to mean no bypass per either 40 CFR §60.756(c) or 40 CFR §757(f)(2) is possible.
                       - COMPLIANT


[pc 21.B.VIII.] Shut down log delineating 12 shutdowns during reporting period. Shutdown event with longest
                        duration was on 25-Nov-2020 for duration of 56 hours and 49 minutes.- COMPLIANT

[pc 21.B.IX.] Facility reports no instances when the collection system was not in operation for more than 5 days. - COMPLIANT

[pc 21.B.X.] Facility reports no Surface Monitoring exceedances or deviations during the reporting period. 
