<tr><td>CRPT003161</td><td>F001759</td><td>Gila River Power Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Please note, this report re-submission is to add an additional permit deviation that occurred on April 1 as well as revise all of the permit conditions in the compliance statement to align with the current permit.

This letter and report are submitted to fulfil the requirements for the Gila Bend Operations Company (GBOC) Semi-Annual Compliance Certification and Reporting as required in Permit Condition 21.a. 

Please note the following Reporting requirements specified by Condition 21.a:

•	See Attached Statement for Condition 21.A.1- a summary of the compliance status for each permit condition;
•	There were three deviations from permit conditions: 1) for Unit 1B on December 25, 2021 (noted on conditions 10 and 18.a in the compliance statement),  2) Unit 4B on March 1, 2021 (noted on conditions 10 and 18.a in the compliance statement), and 3) Unit 1A on April 1, 2021 (noted in condition 19.e.i.15)
•	Summary of the hours of operation for each turbine and duct burner is attached. (required by Condition 21.a.iii);
•	The facility has not discharged any air contaminant, other than uncombined water vapor in excess of 40% opacity for a period aggregating more than three minutes in any 60-minute period per SIP Rule 30.  Visible Emissions (VE) determined per US EPA Method 9.  A sampling of the records maintained on site is included. (required by Condition 21.a.iv);
•	The facility received no odor complaints during the reporting period. (required by Condition 21.a.v);
•	Diesel fuel sulfur content cannot be more than 15ppm from the refinery as of 2014. Fuel suppliers no longer certify ULSD because there is only ULSD available (required by Condition 21.a.vi);
•	There were no gasoline deliveries to the site during the reporting period. (required by Condition 21.a.vii);
•	The facility does not have a submerged gasoline storage tank.  Therefore, records for Permit 		condition 21.a.viii as required cannot be submitted. (required by Condition 21.a.i);
•	Conditions 21.a.ix-x state “any applicable reporting requirements for support operations” and “any other records or reports required by any permit condition” could require every piece of data maintained at the facility. Several statements and records are provided below plus several hundred electronic records were provided to the site inspector following the annual onsite permit inspection. Any other supporting records are available on request;
•	Under 21.c a separate “duct burner report” will be submitted;
•	Per Permit Condition 24, no surface coating operations other than architectural coatings occur at 	the facility;
•	Per Permit Condition 25, abrasive blasting activities for the facility comply with County Rule 335.  	 
•	Per Permit Condition 26, architectural coatings for the facility comply with County Rule 335
•	Per Permit Condition 27, no activities subject to County Rule 330 occur at the facility; 
•	Per Permit Condition 28, no cold degreasing or other operations subject to County Rule 331 occur at the facility other than wipe cleaning;
•	Per Permit Condition 29, wipe cleaning activities at the facility comply with County Rule 331.

If you have any questions regarding this information, please Roy Campbell at (602)236-7607 or email roy.campbell@srpnet.com.</td><td>04/29/2021</td><td>05/18/2021</td><td>No-Revision Requested</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Report submitted is missing information.
I sent an email to Roy Campbell to request an amended report to include the missing information.
The amended report CRPT003143 was submitted on May 21, 2021.</td></tr>
