<tr><td>CRPT003086</td><td>F002234</td><td>Paloma Ready Mix & Materials</td><td>Minor</td><td>Nonmetallic Mineral Processing</td><td>CMP002419</td><td>Paloma Ready Mix & Materials LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Dust Control Plan</td><td>The Dust Control Plan for Paloma Ready Mix & Materials LLC located at 21209 W Beloat Rd cannot be approved for the following reasons:

1.	Section 1a
a.	Reference F002234 instead of the legacy permit number 080022, this is no longer the permit number for the facility
b.	Add submittal date
c.	Note that the first two pages of the Dust Control Plan are very difficult to read

2.	Section 2u
a.	Must check primary control measure – Install a pressure control system designed to shut off the silo filling process/leading operations
b.	If dry material storage silo was installed after November 7, 2018, please note this on line below

3.	Section 2v(2)
a.	Must fill out entire section
b.	Section is blank

4.	Section 2v(3)
a.	Must select yes – Soil moisture samples will be collected within one hour after startup
b.	Must select yes – Soil moisture samples will be collected at least one in every 8 hour period

5.	Section 2v(4)
a.	Must include soil moisture testing attachments
b.	Identify all screen outlets of material containing &lt;0.25”
c.	Identify all crusher outlets of material containing &lt;0.25”
d.	Identify all stacker points of material containing &lt;0.25”
e.	Identify all sample points for soil moisture tests
f.	Identify the applicable minimum soil moisture content for each sample point
g.	Provide an explanation or justification for each sampling point that a sample cannot be taken from

6.	Section 2w(3)
a.	The alternative soil moisture testing method is not approvable
b.	There is no analysis of the correlation between ASTM results and alternative method
c.	There is no QA/QC 
d.	Rule 316 does not allow for exemptions to soil moisture testing due to saturated material
e.	Moisture testing shall be conducted in accordance with the requirements of ASTM C566-97 (2004) “Standard Test Method for Total Evaporable Moisture Content of Aggregate by Drying” with the exception that smaller sample portions may be used

Please make the above corrections and submit a complete Dust Control Plan on or before Monday, 26-Apr-2021.</td><td>04/16/2021</td><td>04/19/2021</td><td>No-Revision Requested</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Dust Control Plan received on 16-Apr-2021
*NOT APPROVED*</td></tr>
