<tr><td>CRPT003036</td><td>F002813</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP000654</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Permit expires on 31-Oct-2021. A Non-Title V permit renewal application shall be submitted 6 to 18 months prior to the expiration date.

Annual administrative fees received on 15-Sep-2020.

Routine inspection conducted on 12-Apr-2019.

Malfunction notification and report received by Maricopa County Air Quality Department within acceptable time frame.

Stack/emission point: The emissions occurred at the #1 and #2 bypass stacks.

Date and duration: The event occurred on 26-Mar-2021, beginning at 2052 hours and ending on or before 2252 hours.

Equipment involved: The emissions emanated from #1 kiln to #1 bypass and from #2 kiln to #2 bypass.

Nature and cause of malfunction: The malfunction occurred when a fuse blew in a control panel. The fuse, which allows the thermal oxizider emergency damper position signal to go to the PLC, malfunctioned. This caused the PLC to not know the position and, in turn, shut off all burners as a safety interlock.

Corrective action taken: The technician identified the issue and the fuse was replaced. During diagnosis, no electrical shorts were found and all systems have been operational with no issues since the event.

Emissions: Per the source the malfunction did not cause the facility to exceed permit limits (calculations provided based on 2016 stack testing). Note that future malfunction reports will be required to utilize calculations based on 2021 stack testing.

The calculations assume the duration of the malfunction is from when the stack cap opens to when it is closed and the pollution control system is fully operational or resident time in the reactivation kiln is approximately two hours, thus emissions associated with a malfunction will be limited to a max duration of two hours, whichever is less.

The source is to include malfunction emissions in the rolling total emissions report.

Emissions due to the malfunction event:
NOX – 0.03 lbs 
CO –  8.03 lbs
VOC – 0.01 lbs
PM – 3.00 lbs
HCl – 0.04 lbs</td><td>03/29/2021</td><td>04/07/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Malfunction event occurred on 26-Mar-2021
Malfunction notification received on 27-Mar-2021
Malfunction report received on 29-Mar-2021</td></tr>
