<tr><td>CRPT002871</td><td>F001759</td><td>Gila River Power Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Notification</td><td>72-Hour Excess Emissions Report for March 1, 2021 NOX ppm corrected exceedance on Unit 4B.</td><td>03/08/2021</td><td>03/10/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>I spoke to Roy Campbell on March 10, 2021.
Mr. Campbell informed me the exceedance occurred due to a calibration started at 1900 hours causing the NOx injection rate to lock.
At 2000 hours the control room personnel attempted to lower the NOx injection rate but were unable to do so because it was locked. Consequently, this caused the NOx level to rise to 2.8 ppm and therefore this hour combined with the next two hours had an average of 2.6ppm for the 3 hour average.
Mr. Campbell informed me this event occurred on March 1, 2021, however; the control room personnel did not notify Mr. Campbell of the event.
Mr. Campbell discovered this event on March 5, 2021 and notified me the same day.

Refer to INSP156143 for violation report.</td></tr>
