<tr><td>CRPT002821</td><td>F002813</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP000654</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Permit expires on 31-Oct-2021. A Non-Title V permit renewal application shall be submitted 6 to 18 months prior to the expiration date.

Annual administrative fees received on 15-Sep-2020.

Routine inspection conducted on 12-Apr-2019.

Malfunction notification and report received by Maricopa County Air Quality Department within acceptable time frame.

Stack/emission point: Emissions occurred at #2 bypass stacks.

Date and duration: The event occurred on 23-Feb-2021 beginning at 1706 hours and ending on or before 1759 hours.

Equipment involved: Emissions emanated from #2 kiln to #2 bypass.

Nature and cause of malfunction: The thermal oxidizer temperature fell below the permit required level of 1400 degrees F and the bypass stack opened as a safety interlock. 

Corrective action taken: The draft transmitter for the thermal oxidizer was identified as not functioning properly, providing a false draft reading. This caused the draft to rise to a higher than optimal level. The positive draft reduced heat being pulled into the thermal oxidizer and allowed the temperature to drop. The draft transmitter is scheduled for replacement. 

Emissions: Per the source the malfunction did not cause the facility to exceed permit limits (calculations provided based on 2016 stack testing).
The calculations assume the duration of the malfunction is from when the stack cap opens to when it is closed and the pollution control system is fully operational or resident time in the reactivation kiln is approximately two hours, thus emissions associated with a malfunction will be limited to a max duration of two hours, whichever is less.

The source is to include malfunction emissions in the rolling total emissions report.

Emissions due to the malfunction event:
NOX – 0.01 pounds
CO – 1.77 pounds
VOC – 0 pounds
PM – 0.66 pounds
HCl – 0.01 pounds

The Department has declined to issue any notices of non-compliance at this time.

Plant manager contact information added to online database. 
Kent Campbell
480-527-4863 (cell)
Kent.Campbell@kuraray.com

Items used to determine compliance:
Malfunction notification
Malfunction report
Permit conditions
Performance testing results</td><td>02/25/2021</td><td>03/05/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Equipment malfunction report received from source via email</td></tr>
