<tr><td>CRPT002714</td><td>F002813</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP000654</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Semi-annual report outlining Corrective Action Plan (CAP) submitted via email on 10-Feb-2021.

The Gila Bend plant submitted four notices to the Department during the reporting period of 01-Jun-2020 through 31-Dec-2020.

09-Aug-2020
HMI server power loss
The GFCI trip allowed loss of communication to the PLC/HMI. The plant interlocks then shut down all burner systems in the plant and opened the bypass stack. 
As a corrective action, the plant has replaced the plug for the server, which will eliminate false circuit trips to the server rack.

10-Sep-2020
Thermal oxidizer flame went out
The thermal oxidizer flame went out after the air dryer valve would not open, which blocked air flow to the plant. This caused the safety interlock to shut off gas to the burners and opened the bypass stacks.
As a corrective action, the plant will include new critical parts that will increase the reliability of this equipment. New parts include regeneration valves, blowoff valves, actuators, all solenoids, and desiccant will all be replaced in the spring of 2021.

29-Sep-2020
Thermal oxidizer flame went out
The thermal oxidizer flame went out after the air dryer valve would not open, which blocked air flow to the plant. This caused the safety interlock to shut off gas to the burners and opened the bypass stacks.
As a corrective action, the plant will include new critical parts that will increase the reliability of this equipment. New parts include regeneration valves, blowoff valves, actuators, all solenoids, and desiccant will all be replaced in the spring of 2021.

26-Oct-2020
Thermal oxidizer flame went out
The instrument air pressure/low pressure switch malfunctioned, which reduced air flow to the plant. This caused the safety interlock to shut off gas to the burners and opened the bypass stacks.
As a corrective action, the plant replaced the pressure switch with a new switch.

All basic and comprehensive dust control training is now available online. Please see our new training website at https://mcaqd.learningcart.com/. 

To successfully register for a dust control certification course on our new training website, customers will be required to create an individual user account linked to their specific email address.  After successfully creating a user account, customers can then select and purchase the certification course that’s applicable to their companies work operations and their own job responsibilities.  

The Department is pleased to offer a Business Assistance (BA) Program for the regulated community.  The purpose of the BA Program is to provide air quality information and technical assistance to business owners.  They offer permit application assistance, courtesy site visits, rule interpretation and education, and enforcement case review. BA Program may be reached at 602-506-5102 and/or AQbusinessassistance@maricopa.gov. 

