<tr><td>CRPT002614</td><td>F002628</td><td>Maax Spas Industries Corp</td><td>Title V</td><td>Plastics, Polymers, Fiberglass, Foam</td><td>CMP002064</td><td>Maax Spas Industries Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Semiannual Monitoring and Semiannual Compliance Certification Report
Reporting Period 01-July-2020  to 31-December-2020</td><td>01/29/2021</td><td>04/28/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>NOTE: Submitted reports reviewed for formal compliance with reporting requirements. Material compliance will be determined in annual compliance inspection.

On 08-Apr-2021; I reviewed the submitted periodic reports i.e. Annual Permit Compliance Cert and Semiannual Compliance Reports and discovered they need correction to the following deficiencies:

ANNUAL PERMIT COMPLIANCE CERTIFICATION REPORT for period 01-Jan-2020 to 31-Dec-2020:
   • I verified the Compliance Certification delineated all required elements of pc 4.a. but was generated
      the following area of concern:

          AREA OF CONCERN [Rule 210 §305.1.d.; pc 4.a.]: which, in summary; requires submittal  
                                                  of certification of compliance annually by 31-January for most recent ANNUAL
                                                  period ending 31-December.
                    • This particular submittal is limited to SEMIANNUAL period 01-Jul-2020 through 31-Dec-2020.
                    • 03-Aug-2020 permit renewal P0006958 revised the compliance certification reporting
                       period from SEMIANNUAL to ANNUAL.
                    • No resubmittal of the [pc 4.a.] report is requested at this time. Commence submittal of the [pc 4.a.]
                       report annually, henceforth.

   • The submittal OMITTED some of the required [pc 4.b.] Semiannual Monitoring Report and all of the required
      [pc 4.c.] Semiannual MACT WWWW Compliance Certification. 

   • I emailed Mr. Picazo informing him of the omissions and requested submittal of the [pc 4.b.] and [pc 4.c.] 
      reports by 26-Apr-2021.

   • On 26-Apr-2021; Mr. Picazo emailed me the revised [pc 4.b.] and the [pc. 4.c.] reports.

   • On 28-Apr-2021; I reviewed all the resubmittals for completeness. Summary of resubmittal follows:

SEMIANNUAL MONITORING REPORT
   • I verified the report included all required elements of pc 4.b. 

SEMIANNUAL MACT WWWW COMPLIANCE CERTIFICATION REPORT
   • I verified the report included all required elements of pc 4.c. 

No [pc 4.] violations noted.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT002613</td><td>F001209</td><td>SR 85 Landfill</td><td>Title V</td><td>Landfills</td><td>CMP000821</td><td>City of Phoenix</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>2020 Annual Soil Stabilization Report</td><td>01/29/2021</td><td>02/01/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The subject report is not an actual periodic report, albeit the facility includes it in their OSOP (Opacity Stabilization Observation Plan); but rather a necessary dust control record as required by Rule 310 §502.1 e.

The reported states the test conducted on 18-Dec-2020 discovered a particular unpaved roadway in Area 5 [a north-south roadway along the eastern perimeter of cell 1] exceeded the silt loading threshold of 0.33 oz/sf and failed silt content limit 6% as referenced in Rule 310 §304.2a. However, §304.2b. provides an alternative to meeting the stability standard of §304.2a. as long as the source limits vehicle trips on the unpaved roadway to no more than 20; limits speed to 15 mph or less; and puts this in their DCP (Dust Control Plan).

I reviewed the facility's DCP (dated 28Dec2020); and the subject control measures are delineated in Category A.2. of the DCP summarized as follows:
-----------
Primary:        Apply water
Primary:        Apply asphalt millings on perimeter roads without pavement, limit speed and traffic.
Contingency: Apply and maintain gravel, recycled asphalt, or other suitable material.
Contingency: Apply and maintain dust suppressants other than water.
Contingency: Limit vehicle trips to no more than 20 per road and limit speed to no more than 15 mph
                      [list maximum vehicle trips; how speed will be restricted; and list of areas this will apply to]
                      Note: "1-3 trips per day on perimeter roads for monitoring the landfill gas collection system"
-----------
The DCP category A.2. complies with §304.2b. and includes the required elements of §402.3c(4).  This precludes any violation as prescribed by §501.2b. 

The report states the control measure §305.7e. was being used; which is a contingency control measure which is required to be employed in the event the primary control measure is ineffective; in which case the record keeping requirement of 502.1f. was met.

The Monthly Opacity Report for December 2020 reported no opacity exceedances on the unpaved roads.

On 02-Feb-2021; I emailed source query whether the Area 5 perimeter unpaved roadway had asphalt millings applied.

On 04-Feb-2021; Jonathan Bunch responded with before and after photos demonstrating the millings were omitted when the test was conducted but recently applied.

On 05-Feb-2021; I emailed Mr. Bunch recommending the facility ensures the primary control measure in their DCP be maintained henceforth.

No violation noted.</td></tr>
