<tr><td>CRPT002392</td><td>F000015</td><td>Salt River Project - Kyrene Generating Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>72-hour Excess Emissions Report for Kyrene Generating Station Unit K7.</td><td>01/07/2021</td><td>01/14/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>This report was generated as a result of a self-reported violation of SRP Kyrene Generating Station permit condition 18.a.ii. Table 3 of permit condition 18.a.ii states that the hourly emission limit for combined cycle system K-7 during periods of startup, shutdown and tuning and testing shall not exceed 162.0 lb/hr. The report provided to MCAQD reports an emission on 167.1 lb for the 18:00 hour of October 28, 2020 during unit startup. This constitutes a violation of permit condition 18.a.ii. 

In addition, permit condition 16.f.i.1) states that MCAQD must be notified via telephone or facsimile within 24 hours of the time frame when the Permittee first learned of the occurrence of excess emissions. I received a voicemail from Lori Trout on Thursday 01/07/21 at 08:49 AM informing me that the excess emissions were discovered on Monday 01/04/21 and that due to a internal mix up the excess emissions report was not sent in at the appropriate time. As documented on the 72-Hour Excess Emission Report provided by the source, it was sent to MCAQD on 01/07/21 which constitutes a violation of permit condition 16.f.i.1.</td></tr>
