<tr><td>CRPT002284</td><td>F001461</td><td>Cave Creek Landfill</td><td>Minor</td><td>Soil Remediation Unit, Portable</td><td>CMP002086</td><td>Maricopa County</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Soil Vapor Extraction Unit Test Report</td><td>Soil Vapor Extraction Performance Test conducted on August 19, 2020.</td><td>12/11/2020</td><td>01/05/2021</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Review of the SVE-Carbon Adsorption System Vapor Sampling Test Report for the performance test conducted on August 19, 2020.
According the results of the performance test, the system is operating within the required limits.

Permit Condition 7.f. and Rule 270 Section 401 require the test results to be submitted to the department within thirty days of the completion of testing.
The test results for the August 19, 2020 testing were received on December 11, 2020.
I called Brian Kehoe, the Maricopa County Division Manager -Waste Resources and Recycling and asked him about the late report.
Mr. Kehoe explained the testing company, usually submits these reports to the department. Mr. Kehoe said he would have Doug Fisher of Wood, the testing company call me.
Mr. Fisher called and explained there had been a change in personnel that resulted in the performance test report submittal to Mr. Kehoe.

I informed Mr. Kehoe I would issue a notice of non-compliance.
I explained the violation process to Mr. Kehoe and informed him the Enforcement Division would issue an Opportunity to Correct or a Notice of Violation.</td></tr>
