<tr><td>CRPT002231</td><td>F003666</td><td>NXP Semiconductors</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Semiconductors and Electronics</td><td>CMP004395</td><td>NXP USA Inc</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>7-Day Notice</td><td>Per the source:

We are sending you notification per Rule 220 Section 404.3 a. NXP will be replacing existing scrubber (Harington SC204) with substantially similar unit (Viron model # VHS-96108-FRP-50.0-60-S-3-H-460-3-60), which has the same capacity (50K CFM) and is guaranteed by the manufacturer to have the same or better abatement efficiency. No change in emissions is expected to result from this change.

Installation of the replacement scrubber SC204 is planned to begin in December 2020 with start-up expected in early 2021.  Upon completion of the installation this abatement device will function as the previous SC204 did.  It will be part of a scrubber system together with the permitted scrubbers SC205 and SC207 abating the east half of North/South Fab. Within this system, one of the units will serve as a stand by unit to back up the other two. The units will be rotated on periodic basis; thus each may be abating the process exhaust some part of the year and may serve as a stand by for the rest.

We will be renewing our air permit in 2021 and scrubber testing will be required by early 2022. We would like to request that performance testing for this replacement SC 204 be performed during the planned testing in 2022 and thus be completed together with the other scrubbers that are due for performance test.</td><td>11/20/2020</td><td>11/30/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>E-mail Notice of Control Device Replacement (scrubber)</td></tr>
