<tr><td>CRPT002102</td><td>F002813</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP000654</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Permit expires on 31-Oct-2021. A Non-Title V permit renewal application shall be submitted 6 to 18 months prior to the expiration date. Reminder email sent on 30-Oct-2020.

Annual administrative fees received on 15-Sep-2020.

Routine inspection conducted on 12-Apr-2019.

Malfunction notification and report received by Maricopa County Air Quality Department within acceptable time frame.

Stack/emission point: Emissions occurred at the bypass stacks.
Date and duration: The event occurred on 26-Oct-2020, beginning at 0616 hours and ending on or before 0816 hours.
Equipment involved:  Emissions emanated from #1 kiln to #1 bypass.
Nature and cause of malfunction: The thermal oxidizer burner flamed out, causing the bypass stack to open due to safety interlock.
Corrective action taken: The feed was stopped by interlock. The instrument air low pressure switch was determined to have failed. The maintenance team adjusted switch to prevent further issues. Replacement part is on order.
Emissions: Per the source the malfunction did not cause the facility to exceed permit limits (calculations provided based on 2016 stack testing).

The calculations assume the duration of the malfunction is from when the stack cap opens to when it is closed and the pollution control system is fully operational or resident time in the reactivation kiln is approximately two hours, thus emissions associated with a malfunction will be limited to a max duration of two hours, whichever is less.

The source is to include malfunction emissions in the rolling total emissions report.

Emissions due to the malfunction event:
NOX – 0.02 lbs
CO – 4.02 lbs
VOC – 0 lbs
PM – 1.50 lbs
HCl – 0.02 lbs</td><td>10/30/2020</td><td>11/02/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Malfunction report due to equipment failure</td></tr>
