Pursuant to Permit Condition 21C. C.2 and CFR 60.49a(b) the reports from the CEMS are attached.
Pursuant to Permit Condition 21.C.4 and 40 CFR 60.49a(f), for any periods for which nitrogen oxides
emissions data were not available, no changes were made in operation of the emission control system
during the period of data availability, based on a comparison of operations of the control system before
and following the period of data unavailability.
Pursuant to Permit Condition 21.C.5 and 40 CFR 60.49a (g), we hereby certify the following:
- The required continuous emission monitoring system calibration, span, and drift checks and other
period audits have been performed.
The data to show compliance were obtained in accordance with approved methods and
procedures and is representative of plant performance.
The minimum data requirements have been met.
Compliance with the standards has been achieved during the reporting period, as noted in the
reports.

Pursuant to 21.C.6, 21.E, and 40 CFR 60.7(c) and (d) the summary Excess emissions and CEMS downtime reports are attached.</td><td>10/26/2020</td><td>11/10/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>I have reviewed the Semi-Annual Duct Burner/ Part 60 Excess Emissions and Monitor Downtime Report for the reporting period of April 1, 2020 to September 30, 2020.</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRPT002000</td><td>F001759</td><td>Gila River Power Station</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP015964</td><td>Salt River Project</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Due October 31, 2020
From April 1, 2020 through September 20, 2020

This letter and report are submitted to fulfil the requirements for the Gila Bend Operations Company (GBOC) Semi-Annual Compliance Certification and Reporting as required in Permit Condition 21.A.  
Please note the following Reporting requirements specified by Condition 21.A: 
• See Attached Statement for Condition 21.A.1- a summary of the compliance status for each permit condition; • There was a Deviation from permit conditions 10 and 18.A as noted on the compliance statement for Unit 4A on September 4, 2020 which was corrected immediately upon discovery (required by Condition 21.A.2); Note:  MCAQD issued an NOV ENF015945 for a failed performance test that occurred in March 2020, which was in the previous semi-annual reporting period.    • Summary of the hours of operation for each turbine and duct burner is attached. (required by Condition 21.A.3); • The facility has not discharged any air contaminant, other than uncombined water vapor in excess of 40% opacity for a period aggregating more than three minutes in any 60-minute period per SIP Rule 30.  Visible Emissions (VE) determined per US EPA Method 9.  A sampling of the records maintained on site is included. (required by Condition 21.A.4); • The facility received no odor complaints during the reporting period. (required by Condition 21.A.5); • Diesel fuel sulfur content cannot be more than 15ppm from the refinery as of 2014. Fuel suppliers no longer certify ULSD because there is only ULSD available (required by Condition 21.A.6); • There were no gasoline delivered to the site during the reporting period. (required by Condition 21.A.7);
The facility does not have a submerged gasoline storage tank. Therefore, records for Permit
condition 21.A.8 as required cannot be submitted. (required by Condition 21.A.1);
Conditions 21. A.9 and 10 require records for the Mechanical spray evaporators which have not
been placed in service to date.
Conditions 21. A.11 and 12 state "any applicable reporting requirements for support operations"
and "any other records or reports required by any permit condition" could require every piece
of data maintained at the facility. Several statements and records are provided below plus
several hundred electronic records were provided to the site inspector following the annual
onsite permit inspection. Any other supporting records are available on request;
Under 21.C a separate "duct burner report" will be submitted;
Per Permit Condition 24, no surface coating operations other than architectural coatings occur at
the facility;
Per Permit Condition 25, abrasive blasting activities for the facility comply with County Rule 335.
Per Permit Condition 26, architectural coatings for the facility comply with County Rule 335
Per Permit Condition 27, no activities subject to County Rule 330 occur at the facility;
Per Permit Condition 28, no cold degreasing or other operations subject to County Rule 331 occur
at the facility other than wipe cleaning;
Per Permit Condition 29, wipe cleaning activities at the facility comply with County Rule 331.</td><td>10/26/2020</td><td>11/09/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>I have reviewed the Compliance Certification Report for the reporting period of April 1, 2020 through September 30, 20202.</td></tr>
