<tr><td>CRPT001971</td><td>F000220</td><td>Rogers Corporation - Roosevelt Ave Facility</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Semiconductors and Electronics</td><td>CMP002773</td><td>Rogers Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>6-month Xylenes Report for the reporting period April 1, 2020 thru September 30, 2020 per permit condition 3.  Due October 30, 2020.</td><td>10/15/2020</td><td>11/02/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The Semi-annual Highest Single HAP (Xylenes) Emissions Report was dated October 15, 2020 and was submitted in accordance with Permit Condition (PC) 3 for F000220, for the period April 1, 2020 through September 30, 2020. Since the Emission Factor Development Protocol required in Permit Condition 1 and associated waste xylenes testing are still in-process, this report does not deduct any of the xylenes sent off-site as liquid waste. Because of this, the emissions of xylenes reported are higher than the actual emissions.

I reviewed the semi-annual report and no compliance issues were noted.

PC 3.a Xylenes Emissions: The Permittee shall submit a twelve month rolling total xylene emission report every six months from the date of permit issuance.
PC 3. b. The xylenes emission report shall contain a complete listing of all xylene-containing materials used during the previous 12-month rolling period and the xylene content for each materials. Xylene usage shall be summed (in pounds) for all materials used within the previous 12-month rolling period.
3. c. The xylenes emission report shall contain a complete record of all xylene-containing waste materials produced during the previous 12-month rolling period and the xylene content, and all supporting mass balance calculations. The total xylene waste stream shall be summed (in pounds) for all waste produced within the previous 12-month rolling period.
3. d. The xylenes emission report shall be submitted within 30 days after each 6-month period. The reporting period shall be from April – September and October – March.

I sent a static copy of the Inspection Report to Curtis Kempton.</td></tr>
