<tr><td>CRPT001935</td><td>F002813</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP000654</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Permit expires on 31-Oct-2021. A Non-Title V permit renewal application shall be submitted 6 to 18 months prior to the expiration date.

Annual administrative fees received on 07-Oct-2020.

Routine inspection conducted on 12-Apr-2019.

Malfunction notification and report received by Maricopa County Air Quality Department within acceptable time frame.

Stack/emission point: The emissions occurred at the #1 and #2 bypass stacks

Date and duration:  Event occurred on 29-Sep-2020 beginning at 2005 hours and ending on or before 2205 hours

Equipment involved:  Emissions emanated from #1 kiln to #1 bypass and from #2 kiln to #2 bypass

Nature and cause of malfunction:  The air dryer became blocked and stopped air flow from the plant. This reduced the air pressure in the plant, causing the plant burners to shut down due to a safety interlock. The issue was unknown at the time of the malfunction. 

Corrective action taken:  The feed was stopped by interlock. The operator on duty bypassed the air dryer at the direction of the maintenance technician. The air compressor vendor arrived on site on 01-Oct-2020 confirmed that the valves on the air dryer were not functioning. The valves would not open and thus blocked the flow. The control units for the valves along with other air dryer parts are now scheduled to be replaced in order to reduce the chance of future issues. 

Emissions: Per the source the malfunction did not cause the facility to exceed permit limits (calculations provided based on 2016 stack testing).

The calculations assume the duration of the malfunction is from when the stack cap opens to when it is closed and the pollution control system is fully operational or resident time in the reactivation kiln is approximately two hours, thus emissions associated with a malfunction will be limited to a max duration of two hours, whichever is less.

The source is to include malfunction emissions in the rolling total emissions report.

Emissions due to the malfunction event:
NOX – 0.03 lbs
CO – 8.03 lbs
VOC – 0.01 lbs
PM – 3.00 lbs
HCl –0.04 lbs

The Department has declined to issue any notices of non-compliance at this time.

Items used to determine compliance:
Malfunction notification and report submitted by source</td><td>10/02/2020</td><td>10/07/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Malfunction report received on 02-Oct-2020</td></tr>
