<tr><td>CRPT001773</td><td>F002376</td><td>AIM Recycling Phoenix - McDowell Rd</td><td>Minor</td><td>Metal Recycling and Recovery</td><td>CMP022222</td><td>AIM Recycling Phoenix LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Periodic Semiannual Reporting for the second half of 2019.</td><td>08/11/2020</td><td>09/11/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>During the periodic report review performed in Aug-2020 it was noted that the periodic report from the previous 6 months could not be located in the database (OnBase or IMPACT).  It was fully believed to have been submitted.  The Holder was asked to resubmit the documents for proper filing.  Documents were received on 11-Aug-2020
The report was compared to the requirements of Permit Conditions 4 and 6 as listed below:

4a.  Permittee is required to perform a compliance demonstration twice a year, between 5 and 7 months from the last demonstration.   The last compliance demonstration was performed  on 25-Jun-19.
       The Permittee as required obtained opacity readings of the emissions from the shredder and cyclone while processing material through the shredder, magnetic drum separator and Z-box for more than 1 hour during daylight hours. 
       Opacity readings on the shredder and cyclone emissions were conducted in accordance with EPA Reference Method 9 as modified by EPA Reference Method 203B by two individuals certified in EPA Reference Method 9 evaluation. The compliance demonstration was conducted under representative operating conditions.
     Testing commenced at 0756 on 17-Dec-19.  Sunrise was 0726.
     The flow rate of the water injection system was calibrated.
4b.  A Department Representative did not attend.  A Test Notification could not be located.
     Submitted report demonstrates compliance with Permit Condition 4.
6b. Permittee is required to submit a semiannual report to the Department within 60 days of the end of each 6-month period stating at a minimum every occurrence of an explosion or fire at the shredder or anywhere on the property including the date and time, cause, and corrective action taken.
     This report was submitted as required and demonstrated compliance with Permit Condition 6b.	  

Items used to determine compliance:
Records reviewed electronically</td></tr>
