<tr><td>CRPT001632</td><td>F002813</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP000654</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Semi-annual report for Gila Bend plant submitted via email. Reporting period is 01-Jan-2020 through 30-Jun-2020 and includes 5 malfunction reports.

12-Feb-2020
Vibration sensor due to human error
Induced draft fan vibration sensor was being inspected due to an error in its reading. During the inspection the reading of the sensor was too high and triggered a high vibration shut down on the fan. The plant interlocks then shut down all burner systems in the plant and opened the bypass stack. As a corrective action, the plant provided training to reduce the likelihood of mistakes. In addition the plant is planning to create a list of equipment requiring work authorization when there is interlock potential to shut down the system while operating.

18-Mar-2020
Power outage due to thunderstorm
A thunderstorm caused an area power outage. To be proactive in reducing emissions during storm related power outage, operators will observe radar when storms are expected and shut feed off ahead of a storm to avoid or limit emissions.

20-Mar-2020
Uninterrupted power supply (UPS) failure
A UPS for the HMI computers in the control room failed causing all of the equipment plugged into it to lose power. This resulted in shutdown of the entire process, including feed to the system.

20-Mar-2020
GFCI tripped
The GFCI tripped due to overload of the circuit causing a shutdown. This resulted in shutdown of the entire process, including the feed to the system. An overload was also expected to be the root cause of the UPS failure earlier on the same day. Temporary power was run until a replacement power source was added during the shutdown. Additional improvements continue to be investigated. 

07-May-2020
High pressure on kiln
There was a high pressure in the kiln that resulted in a bypass. It is believed that a bad processor and potential burner issue was the cause. The corrective action was to replace the PLC processor and tune the burner.

Permit expires on 31-Oct-2021. A Non-Title V permit renewal application shall be submitted 6 to 18 months prior to the expiration date.

Annual administrative fees received on 25-Sep-2019.

Routine inspection conducted on 12-Apr-2019.

Items used to determine compliance:
Semi-annual report submitted by source</td><td>08/18/2020</td><td>08/19/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semi-annual report</td></tr>
