<tr><td>CRPT001592</td><td>F002813</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP000654</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Permit expires on 31-Oct-2021. A Non-Title V permit renewal application shall be submitted 6 to 18 months prior to the expiration date.

Annual administrative fees received on 25-Sep-2019.

Routine inspection conducted on 12-Apr-2019.

Malfunction notification and report received by Maricopa County Air Quality Department within acceptable time frame.

Stack/emission point: Emissions occurred at the #1 bypass stack

Date and duration: Event occurred on 09-Aug-2020 beginning at 2122 hours and ending on or before 2228 hours

Equipment involved: #1 kiln to #1 bypass

Nature and cause of malfunction: Main HMI server rack GFCI tripped which resulted in a power situation to the rack. The rack had recently been upgraded with a new UPS and power strip. Feed was stopped by interlock.

Corrective action taken: Remote power was brought to the rack so it could be restarted. An electrician is scheduled to examine this circuit to aid with proper replacement choice. 

Emissions: Per the source the malfunction did not cause the facility to exceed permit limits (calculations provided based on 2016 stack testing).

The calculations assume the duration of the malfunction is from when the stack cap opens to when it is closed and the pollution control system is fully operational or resident time in the reactivation kiln is approximately two hours, thus emissions associated with a malfunction will be limited to a max duration of two hours, whichever is less.
The source is to include malfunction emissions in the rolling total emissions report.

Emissions due to the malfunction event:
NOX – 0.01 lbs
CO – 2.28 lbs
VOC – 0 lbs
PM – 0.85 lbs
HCl – 0.01 lbs</td><td>08/11/2020</td><td>08/12/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Malfunction report due to equipment failure</td></tr>
