<tr><td>CRPT001473</td><td>F003458</td><td>El Mirage Transmix Facility</td><td>Minor</td><td>Petroleum Products Bulk Storage/Handling</td><td>CMP001426</td><td>Fuel Processing Operators LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Semi-Annual Compliance Report For reporting period January 1, 2020 to June 30, 2020.</td><td>07/24/2020</td><td>07/31/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The Semi Annual Compliance Report for the El Mirage Transfix Facility is dated July 20, 2020 and it was for the Reporting Period January 1, 2020 - June 30, 2020.
The Semi Annual Compliance Report was submitted before the due date of July 31, 2020.
The Semi Annual Compliance Report references the Permit Conditions (140045) with a revision date of 11/28/2018 and expiration date 5/31/2020.
The current Permit Conditions (P0006789 & P0007018, F003458) have a revision date of 4/24/2020 and an expiration date of 5/31/2025.
Both Permit Conditions were used to determine compliance.

The following information is based on the information submitted in the Semi Annual Compliance Report:
Permit Condition (PC) 17.a. Tank 19 Transmix IFR meets the requirements for Permit Condition 6 (b)(ii)(1)(b)(iii) with a mechanical shoe primary seal and shoemounted secondary seal.
PC 17.a. Tank 20 has not been installed yet.
PC 17.b. Tank 17 Toluene/Xylene Horizontal Fixed meets the requirements for Permit Condition 6 (c) (i) & (ii) and is connected to Vapor Recovery Unit (VRU). 
PC 17.b. Tank 18 Butane/Toluene/Xylene Horizontal Fixed meets the requirements for Permit Condition 6 (d) and is connected to Vapor Recovery Unit (VRU).
PC 6. Tank 4 Ethanol IFR meets the requirements of Permit Condition 6 (b)(ii)(1)(b)(iii) with a mechanical shoe primary seal and rimmounted secondary seal.
PC 6. Tank 13 Transmix IFR meets the requirements of Permit Condition 6 (b)(ii)(1)(b)(iii) with a mechanical shoe primary seal and shoemounted secondary seal.
PC 6. Tank 14 Transmix Gasoline Product IFR meets the requirements of Permit Condition 6 (b)(ii)(1)(b)(iii) with a mechanical shoe primary seal.
PC 6. Tank 15 Transmix IFR meets the requirements of Permit Condition 6 (b)(ii)(1)(b)(iii) with a mechanical shoe primary seal and shoemounted secondary seal.
PC 6. Tank 16 Transmix Gasoline Product IFR meets the requirements of Permit Condition 6 (b)(ii)(1)(b)(iii) with a mechanical shoe primary seal.

PC 17.d.i. Loading Racks: No loading of gasoline cargo tanks occurred without prior record of vapor tightness documentation specified in the compliance period.

PC 17.d.ii. Equipment Leak Inspections: There were no equipment leaks that were not repaired or where an attempt was made within 5 days or for which repair was not completed within 15 days after detection in the compliance period.

PC 17. e. Excess Emissions: There were no excess emission events in the reporting period.

PC 17.d. iii: The CEMS Quarterly CGA reports dated 3/4/2020 and 5/19/2020 for each requirement under Permit Condition 17.d.iii. 
The CGA audit value on 3/4/2020 for the audit point 1 low level was 0.550 and the audit point 2 mid level was 1.010, the CEMS response was 0.557 for the audit point 1 low level and 1.020 for the audit point 2 mid level.
The CGA audit value on 5/19/2020 for the audit point 1 low level was 0.550 and the audit point 2 mid level was 1.010, the CEMS response was 0.56 for the audit point 1 low level and 1.02 for the audit point 2 mid level.

PC 34.a. Tank 23 has not been installed (Naphtha IFR) but when it is it will contain a mechanical shoe primary seal and shoemounted secondary seal.</td></tr>
