Submitted to MCAQD on 17-Jun-2020</td><td>06/17/2020</td><td>09/15/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>020051 VMC Burner Optimization Report for period 25-Sep-2019 to 29-Jun-2020 [Due every 200,000 tons]
• Optimization conducted 29-Jan-2020
• Submitted: 01-Jul-2020 (also 04-Mar-2020)

[See INSP067820]; On 04-Mar-2020; Scott Johnson submitted 29Jan2020 BCO Report with statement 180,000 tons since the 9/25/2019 test.  

• My 09-Mar-2020 email response to Mr. Johnson instructed Mr. Johnson to submit the subject BCO through normal submittal channels, not as record submittal during the site's annual inspection as illustrated by the following excerpt from INSP067820:
Excerpt begin]
Burner optimization report
On 04-Mar-2020; I reviewed requested records and emailed Mr. Chronowski a followup request for the following:
• PC 21.a. Burner Combustion Optimization because apparent 281K tons of HMA produced since most recently submitted Burner Combustion Optimization conducted 26-Jul-2019.
• PC 21.c.i. Semiannual/100,000 ton (whichever is first) monitoring of NOx, O2 and CO at the outlet of the drum dryer.
Scott Johnson, the facility's Compliance Manager emailed me the requested records demonstrating compliance as follows:
• PC 20.c.i. NOx, CO, and O2 concentrations measured on 02-Oct-2019 and 02-Dec-2019.
• PC 20.d. Burner Combustion Optimization conducted 29-Jan-2020. Submittal date not passed. Mr. Johnson responded to the record request with a similar report for the West 43rd Ave Plant.  I emailed Mr. Johnson I would be grateful for submittal of the reports through normal submittal channels to preclude losing them in inspection support documents.
[Excerpt end]

Per 15-Sep-2020 email from Brian Chronowski; • PC 20.c.i. Flame analysis conducted on 02-Oct-2019 and 02-Dec-2019 were conducted associated with the following HMA tonnages:
• 02-Oct-2019:  HMA production between 25-Sep-2019 and 02-Oct-2019 = 7,040 tons
• 02-Dec-2019: HMA production between 02-Oct-2019 and 02-Dec-2019 = 116,936 tons
Mr. Chronowski explained a math error likely contributed to the source conducting the 02-Dec-2019 past the 100,000 ton trigger; and only noticed the error when reviewing my request for the tonnage now.  Action was immediately taken tho ensure data review and recording is conducted by two persons.

020051 VMC Burner Optimization Report for period 27-Jul-2019 to 23-Sep-2019 [Due every 200,000 tons]
• Optimization conducted 23-25 Sep-2019
• Submitted: 01-Jul-2020

Per 14Sep2020 email from Brian Chronowski; HMA Production between 27-Jul-2019 and 25-Sep-2019 is 95,217 tons.
Flame Analyzer conducted on 27Jul2019 and 25Sep2019 [Due every 100,000 tons]

Late submittal: Due 24-Nov-2019; Submitted 01-Jul-2020. Per conference call with Scott Johnson and Brian Chronowski; the period this occurred has been a tumultuous time in the order of personnel changes; as the entire compliance team has turned over.  Mr. Johnson says this an effort will be made to ensure this does not recur.  Per source logs, Sydney Stauffer logged submittal of this report on 24-Nov-2019. Unable to locate in Department files.

On 15-Sep-2020; I telephoned Mr. Chronowski and informed him of the following Area of Concern:

AREA OF CONCERN [Rule 220 §302.2; p.c. 21.c.i.]: Permittee shall monitor and record concentrations of NOx, O2, and CO semiannually or 100,000 tons of HMA produced, whichever comes first.
• 116,936 tons HMA produced during period 02-Oct-2019 through 02-Dec-2019 
• Monitoring the NOx, O2, and CO required every 100,000 tons HMA

I informed Mr. Chronowski a violation may be issued for recurrence.

No violation issued.</td></tr>
