<tr><td>CRPT001255</td><td>F002813</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP000654</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Permit expires on 31-Oct-2021. A Non-Title V permit renewal application shall be submitted 6 to 18 months prior to the expiration date.

Annual administrative fees received on 25-Sep-2019.

Routine inspection conducted on 12-Apr-2019.

Malfunction notification and report received by Maricopa County Air Quality Department within acceptable time frame.

Stack/emission point: #2 bypass stack
Date and duration: Event occurred on 17-Jun-2020 beginning at 0728 and ending on or before 0928
Equipment involved: Emissions emanated from #2 kiln to #2 bypass
Nature and cause of malfunction: Brief power outage lasting approximately one minute resulted in a loss of power to all equipment which then opened the bypass stack after the burners shut off. The loss of all power to the plant shut off the feed to the kilns.
Corrective action taken: The power loss resulted in minor equipment damage to the thermal oxidizer which had to be investigated. Troubleshooting was performed and the issue was fixed by the maintenance department. After identification and correction the equipment was restarted.

Emissions: Per the source the malfunction did not cause the facility to exceed permit limits (calculations provided based on 2016 stack testing).

The calculations assume the duration of the malfunction is from when the stack cap opens to when it is closed and the pollution control system is fully operational or resident time in the reactivation kiln is approximately two hours, thus emissions associated with a malfunction will be limited to a max duration of two hours, whichever is less.

The source is to include malfunction emissions in the rolling total emissions report.

Emissions due to the malfunction event:
NOX – 0.02 lbs
CO – 4.02 lbs
VOC – 0 lbs
PM – 1.50 lbs
HCl – 0.02 lbs

Facility contacts updated in database.</td><td>06/22/2020</td><td>06/24/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Malfunction report due to power outage</td></tr>
