<tr><td>CRPT001169</td><td>F003826</td><td>Booster Pump Station 36-5</td><td>Below Threshold</td><td>Generator, Stationary (ATO)</td><td>CMP003722</td><td>City of Scottsdale</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Permit Close Request</td><td>Hi Susan, 
Thank you for submitting your request for permit cancellation. We’ve received and processed your request, and have determined that you do not currently require an Air Quality permit. The facility class has been changed to below threshold for facilities, F000241, F000246, F000247, F000248, F000249, F000250, F000252, F000257, F000259, F000260 and F003826. 

Please be aware that although a permit is not required at this time, you must comply with Rule 324: Stationary Reciprocating Internal Combustion Engines (RICE). You must maintain records per Section 500 – Monitoring and Records, to demonstrate that you have not exceeded 500 hours of operation, and 100 hours of maintenance and engine readiness testing per 12-month rolling period. Any additional engines or emission units added will need to be reevaluated for possible permitting. In addition, all internal combustion engines must comply with federal rules and New Source Performance Standards (NSPS) IIII, JJJJ, and MACT ZZZZ. For more information on EPA standards, visit the EPA webpage. 

Please refer to our Stationary Emergency Generators General Permit Help Sheet for assistance with maintaining compliance with Rule 324. For any additional questions, please contact the Air Quality department at 602-506-6702.</td><td>05/26/2020</td><td>05/26/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr>
