<tr><td>CRPT001116</td><td>F002813</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP000654</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Permit expires on 31-Oct-2021. A Non-Title V permit renewal application shall be submitted 6 to 18 months prior to the expiration date.

Annual administrative fees received on 25-Sep-2019.

Routine inspection conducted on 12-Apr-2019.

Malfunction notification and report received by Maricopa County Air Quality Department within acceptable time frame.

Stack/emission point: #2 bypass stack
Date and duration: 07-May-2020, beginning at 1246 hours and ending on or before 0115 hours
Equipment involved: Emissions emanated from #2 kiln to #2 bypass
Nature and cause of malfunction: The kiln experienced higher than normal temperatures due to a product change that was occurring. It was later determined that the kiln had discharge plugging issues which would have led to the abnormal temperature issues. During the product change while the kiln was at a higher temperature the burner went to low fire and unexpectedly flamed out. During the relighting process the burner purged and a high pressure condition in the kiln was observed. The bypass stack opened due to the high pressure condition.
Corrective action taken: The kiln burner was restarted after the occurrence and the bypass stack closed. The kiln door was opened on 08-May-2020 and slag material was determined to be causing a plug. This material was removed by staff. Feed was off due to interlocks.

Emissions: Per the source the malfunction did not cause the facility to exceed permit limits (calculations provided based on 2016 stack testing).

The calculations assume the duration of the malfunction is from when the stack cap opens to when it is closed and the pollution control system is fully operational or resident time in the reactivation kiln is approximately two hours, thus emissions associated with a malfunction will be limited to a max duration of two hours, whichever is less.

The source is to include malfunction emissions in the rolling total emissions report.

Emissions due to the malfunction event:
NOX – 0 lbs
CO – 0.97 lbs
VOC – 0 lbs
PM – 0.36 lbs
HCl – 0 lbs

The Department has declined to issue any violations.

Items used to determine compliance:
Notification and report submitted by source

The Department is pleased to offer a Business Assistance (BA) Program for the regulated community.  The purpose of the BA Program is to provide air quality information and technical assistance to business owners.  They offer permit application assistance, courtesy site visits, rule interpretation and education, and enforcement case review. BA Program may be reached at 602-506-5102 and/or AQbusinessassistance@maricopa.gov.</td><td>05/11/2020</td><td>05/13/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Malfunction report due to high pressure on 07-May-2020.</td></tr>
