<tr><td>CRPT000784</td><td>F003399</td><td>Hydro Extrusion USA</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Metal Production - Foundry, Forge, etc</td><td>CMP001686</td><td>Hydro Extrusion USA LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>The report was received and date stamped by the Department on 02-Mar-20.  The envelope was not retained.  It is therefore assumed that the report was actually submitted within the 60 day requirement.  The report was submitted to fulfill the requirements of Permit Conditions 12.a. and b. and 40CFR63.10(e)(3)(v).

Twelve excursions from the normal operations were described and the Corrective Action Reports (CARs) were included.  There were three instances of discrepancy between the summary report and the individual CARs.  Neither the Permit nor the approved O&M Plan on file with the Department require that the CAR be written contemporaneously with the event nor that the original CAR be submitted to the Department for review.  Since the provided individual CARs were prepared on the same day the logical conclusion drawn was that transcription errors were made during the copying of the information.  None of the discrepancies would change the outcome that no excess emissions occurred during the review period.  Therefore, the report was accepted as submitted.

The conditions of Permit Condition 12 and of 40CFR63.10 were satisfied as required.</td><td>03/02/2020</td><td>03/13/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Semiannual report of excess emissions/summary report was received for review.  Half year covered was July 1, 2019 to Dec 31, 2019.</td></tr>
