<tr><td>CRPT000512</td><td>F001186</td><td>91st Ave Wastewater Treatment Plant</td><td>Synthetic Minor</td><td>Wastewater Treatment Plants and Lift Stations</td><td>CMP000821</td><td>City of Phoenix</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Semannual Report for period covering July - December 31st 2019.</td><td>01/29/2020</td><td>02/03/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Synthetic Minor AIRS Emissions Reporting: 

Permit Condition 3 

The Permittee shall submit a SOX emission report to the Department (Attention: Compliance Division Manager) every six months.  The reports shall cover the periods from January 1st through June 30th and July 1st through December 31st and be submitted no later than 45 days after the end of each reporting period.  The SOX emission report shall include: 

a.	Monthly and 12-month rolling total emissions of SOX during the preceding 12 months, calculated in accordance with Permit Condition 2;
b.	Results of the digester gas sulfur tests for each city business day;
c.	Daily, monthly and 12 month rolling total volume of digester gas (MMscf) burned at the facility in each boiler and flare. 
d.	Verification, in accordance with Permit Condition 17.a.iii, that no diesel fuel exceeding 15 ppm sulfur content is burned in stationary equipment at the facility. 
e.	Monthly and 12 month rolling total number of times sodium bisulfite is loaded into the tank for each calendar month during the preceding 12 months.
[SIP Rule 220 §§302.7, 302.8, 302.23(a)(2), 304.1][SIP Rule 100 §502]

All required information included in semi-annual report. 

Summary of emissions: 
Largest rolling total of SOx in July total at 169,305 lbs (limit 182,000 lbs)
6 sodium bisulfite deliveries since January 2019. 
Highest 12 month rolling total for sites digester gas in July 2019 at 838.83 MM cu Ft (1400 MM cu Ft limit)

No compliance issues observed.</td></tr>
