<tr><td>CRPT000467</td><td>F001504</td><td>New Harquahala Generating</td><td>Title V</td><td>Power Plant</td><td>CMP002301</td><td>New Harquahala Generating Co LLC</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>Semi Annual Compliance Certification for reporting period April 1 2019 through September 30 2019 was received on October 15 2019. The semi annual report was due by October 31 2019. During this period the Combined Cycle Units did not operate.</td><td>10/15/2019</td><td>01/24/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The report was reviewed and determined to be in compliance. However, there are some areas where statements could have been better stated. PC 18a has "Confirmed via records that CTG 1,2,3 were operated in compliance with the allowable emission limits during this reporting period" A better statement would be the "CTG 1,2,3 did not operate during this period". However, they were still in compliance with emission limits since they did not run. 
PC 21e ( ix) States " If no complaints were received during the reporting period, a statement to that effect may be substituted for the copy of the odor log". As observed during  on site inspection the log showed no complaints. This permit condition did not have a statement of no complaints. However the permit condition 20e(ii) did contain this statement. 
PC 19 says "Confirmed air pollution control equipment was operated at all times in a manner consistent with good air pollution control ..." More accurate statement would be " the control equipment did not run as the Combined Cycle units did not operate".</td></tr>
