<tr><td>CRPT000278</td><td>F002813</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Minor</td><td>Chemical Manufacture, Processing, etc</td><td>CMP000654</td><td>Calgon Carbon Corporation</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Self-Report</td><td>Permit expires on 31-Oct-2021. A Non-Title V permit renewal application shall be submitted 6 to 18 months prior to the expiration date.

Annual administrative fees received on 25-Sep-2019.

Routine inspection conducted on 12-Apr-2019.

Malfunction notification and report received by Maricopa County Air Quality Department within acceptable time frame.

Stack/emission point: #1 bypass stack
Date and duration: Event occurred on 20-Nov-2019, beginning at 1738 and ending on or before 1938
Equipment involved: Emissions emanated from #1 kiln to #1 bypass
Nature and cause of malfunction: Power outage due to weather event that lasted for several hours.
Corrective action taken: All burners were off as well as the feed due to the power outage. Plant was brought back online according to standard procedure.

Emissions: Per the source the malfunction did not cause the facility to exceed permit limits (calculations provided based on 2016 stack testing).
The calculations assume the duration of the malfunction is from when the stack cap opens to when it is closed and the pollution control system is fully operational or resident time in the reactivation kiln is approximately two hours, thus emissions associated with a malfunction will be limited to a max duration of two hours, whichever is less.

The source is to include malfunction emissions in the rolling total emissions report.

Emissions due to the malfunction event:
NOX – 0.02 pounds
CO – 4.02 pounds
VOC – NA
PM – 1.5 pounds
HCl – 0.02 pounds

Facility:
Calgon Carbon Corporation
520 S Butterfield Tr, Gila Bend AZ, 85337

Contact:
Jeremy Dolan, Plant Manager
jdolan@calgoncarbon.com
928.683.6060

Inspector:
Laurie Cline, Senior Inspector
3800 N Central Ave #1400, Phoenix AZ, 85012
Laurie.cline@maricopa.gov
602.319.6003

Items used to determine compliance:
Communication, notification, report from source

The Department is pleased to offer a Business Assistance (BA) Program for the regulated community.  The purpose of the BA Program is to provide air quality information and technical assistance to business owners.  They offer permit application assistance, courtesy site visits, rule interpretation and education, and enforcement case review. BA Program may be reached at 602-506-5102 and/or AQbusinessassistance@maricopa.gov.</td><td>11/21/2019</td><td>11/22/2019</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Malfunction report</td></tr>
