<tr><td>CRPT001306</td><td>F000217</td><td>World Resources Company</td><td>Minor</td><td>Metal Recycling and Recovery</td><td>CMP003626</td><td>World Resources Company</td><td>Compliance Report</td><td>Periodic Reporting</td><td>The annual report for the Summary of Ambient Air Sampling at the property line, the Annual Average Total Percentage of metal HAPs, and the Annual Average Percentage of chromium and nickel percentage of HAPs.  This was submitted to fulfill the requirements of permit condition 12.  The period of review was listed as the calendar year 2019 and the date of receipt of the report was 6-Jun-20 via certified mail.

Per Permit Condition 9b. the Holder shall conduct air sampling at one of 4 property line air monitors during normal production operations.  This is to be conducted by the closest downwind unit from the activity at a minimum of twice per month.  The metals tested shall be at a minimum silver, cadmium, chromium, nickel, and lead.  
The submitted documents demonstrated compliance with this requirement and also with Permit Condition 12.a.

Per Permit Condition 12.b, c. the Holder us to submit a report listing the average total percent of metal HAPs in the waste and the annual average total percent of chromium and nickel HAPs.  
The submitted document demonstrated compliance with both of these requirements.

The report was due for submission on or before 1-Jul-20.  The report was received within the required timeframe.</td><td>06/10/2020</td><td>06/10/2020</td><td>Yes</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>The annual report for the Summary of Ambient Air Sampling at the property line, the Annual Average Total Percentage of metal HAPs, and the Annual Average Percentage of chromium and nickel percentage of HAPs.
Per Permit Condition 9 the metals that need to be tested for are lead, chromium, cadmium, nickel and silver.  The documents submitted indicate compliance with this condition.
Per Permit Condition 12a, the annual summary report listing the previous 12 months of sampling data must be submitted by 1-July of the following year.  This report was received at the Department on 10-Jun, which is within the required time frame.
Permit Condition 12.b. requires the annual average total percentage of metal in the waste processed be reported.  The document submitted confirmed compliance with this requirement.
Permit condition 12.c.</td></tr>
